":2,"1780":3,"1781":3,"1782":3,"1783":2,"1784":2,"1785":3,"1786":4,"1787":3,"1788":3,"1789":2,"1790":3,"1791":3,"1792":3,"1793":3,"1794":4,"1795":4,"1796":4,"1797":3,"1798":3,"1799":3,"1800":3,"1801":3,"1802":3,"1803":3,"1804":3}}},"docs":{"docs":{"1":{"id":"/docs/changelog","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"page","content":"Changelog","breadcrumbs":["Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog"},"2":{"id":"/docs/changelog-0","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"What's new in Visuno — components, docs, and tooling, newest first."},"3":{"id":"/docs/changelog-1","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"Unreleased"},"4":{"id":"/docs/changelog-2","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-07","content":"2026-11-07"},"5":{"id":"/docs/changelog-3","page_id":"/docs/changelog","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-06","content":"2026-11-06"},"6":{"id":"/docs/changelog-4","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog","content":"Notable changes to the Visuno component library and these docs, newest first.\nComponent source lives in the components repository."},"7":{"id":"/docs/changelog-5","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Angular demos** — restored the React demos’ interactive state updates, streamed stories, retries, approvals, replay controls, and reduced-motion behavior. Added missing controlled inputs and copy/disabled button support in the Angular library."},"8":{"id":"/docs/changelog-6","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Angular** — component selectors now use PascalCase that mirrors the React component names (`<vo-status-pill>` → `<StatusPill>`, `<vo-icon>` → `<Icon>`, `<vo-agent-tree>` → `<AgentTree>`, …). The three selectors that shadowed native HTML elements are prefixed to stay unambiguous: `<VoButton>`, `<VoButtonCopy>`, `<VoProgress>`. The `voGridItem` / `vo-field-zone` directives become `gridItem` / `fieldZone`. The shared `--vo-*` design tokens and `vo-*` CSS classes are unchanged. **Breaking:** update Angular templates to the new tag names."},"9":{"id":"/docs/changelog-7","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Docs** — a global site footer now appears on every page (MIT licence, Star on GitHub, a link to the machine-readable **llms.txt**, Imprint, and \"Powered by SDK Industries\"), plus a floating **back-to-top** button that fades in once you scroll."},"10":{"id":"/docs/changelog-8","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Angular Stat cards** — adapt columns and spacing to the component width so cards fit narrow panels as well as mobile screens."},"11":{"id":"/docs/changelog-9","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Angular Code viewer** — removed oversized gaps between code lines while preserving code indentation and blank lines."},"12":{"id":"/docs/changelog-10","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Angular test bench** — added the missing Number field, OTP field, Search input, and Slider examples with interactive states."},"13":{"id":"/docs/changelog-11","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Docs** — new getting-started guides: **Installation** (per-framework setup), **Theming** (the two switches and the `--vo-*` token system, with per-framework code tabs), **Accessibility** (semantics, keyboard, focus, reduced motion), and **Using with AI** (point a coding assistant at the `llms.txt` docs). Grouped under a collapsible **Docs** section in the sidebar, and every nav entry now carries a Visuno icon."},"14":{"id":"/docs/changelog-12","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Angular** — use the same shared web styles as React for consistent typography, controls, icons, and Soft/Blueprint themes."},"15":{"id":"/docs/changelog-13","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Slider** — new shared component in all four frameworks: a track with a\nsingle value or a range, optional discrete steps and named stops, and an\nagent-recommended value marked on the track. Keyboard and drag, tokens only."},"16":{"id":"/docs/changelog-14","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Search input** — new shared component in all four frameworks: a search\nfield with scoped filters, recent queries and an inline agent answer."},"17":{"id":"/docs/changelog-15","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Number field** — new shared component in all four frameworks: type a number\nor step it with minus and plus, with units, limits, and a note when a value is\nclamped to fit."},"18":{"id":"/docs/changelog-16","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**OTP field** — new shared component in all four frameworks: a one-time code,\none box per digit, that auto-advances, navigates by keyboard and fills from a\npaste."},"19":{"id":"/docs/changelog-17","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Docs preview** — live example stages now always use the docs page's own theme\n(light or dark), never the browser's colour-scheme preference. The per-preview\nLight/Dark toggle has been removed; the component tokens follow the site theme."},"20":{"id":"/docs/changelog-18","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Icon** — new shared component in all four frameworks: one line icon from a shared\nMIT set of ~5,200, or your own SVG. Colour follows `currentColor` so icons theme for\nfree; sizes run `xs`–`xl` on a 24×24 grid. Any name resolves on the web; Angular and\nFlutter draw names outside the compiled core set, and custom glyphs, from a `path`.\nThe whole set now uses canonical, descriptive names (`chevron-right`, `circle-check`,\n`terminal-2`…) across every framework."},"21":{"id":"/docs/changelog-19","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Packages** — the library now publishes as installable packages: `@visuno/react` and\n`@visuno/angular` on npm, and `visuno` on pub.dev for Flutter. Each is released from its\nframework directory in the components repo."},"22":{"id":"/docs/changelog-20","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Vanilla JS dropped** — Visuno is now **three frameworks**: React, Angular and Flutter.\nThe Vanilla JS tabs have been removed from every component page, and the docs, FAQ and\nroadmap updated to match. React is now the reference implementation."},"23":{"id":"/docs/changelog-21","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Landing page** — the home page now showcases the **whole library** live: every\nshipped component appears as a running preview card, grouped by category, with the\ncomponent count derived from the list. New marketing hero leading with the Visuno\nname, a secondary \"Star on GitHub\" action, and feature pills."},"24":{"id":"/docs/changelog-22","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Frameworks slider** — the frameworks strip is now an auto-scrolling black & white\nlogo slider covering React, Angular, Flutter and the React\nmeta-frameworks it works with (Next.js, Remix, Gatsby, Astro)."},"25":{"id":"/docs/changelog-23","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Modal** — new shared component in all three frameworks: a centred dialog over a\ndimmed backdrop, closed by the backdrop, a button or Escape, with focus and page\nscroll kept in check. It carries the active style and theme to its portal, so it\nmatches the surrounding components (rounded in Soft, correct light/dark)."},"26":{"id":"/docs/changelog-24","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Run summary** — the \"Run details\" and \"Open changes\" buttons now work: Run\ndetails opens a Modal with the run's stats, Open changes opens a full diff view."},"27":{"id":"/docs/changelog-25","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Thinking states** — four new indicators: Pulse, Wave, Bounce and Spiral."},"28":{"id":"/docs/changelog-26","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Run cost** — the spend bar now glides with the number instead of stalling."},"29":{"id":"/docs/changelog-27","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Toast** — a dismissed toast can be shown again straight after."},"30":{"id":"/docs/changelog-28","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Imprint page** added with the legal information of SDK Industries, linked from\nthe docs navigation and the homepage footer."},"31":{"id":"/docs/changelog-29","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#unreleased","content":"**Stat cards** homepage preview reworked into a responsive single-column layout."},"32":{"id":"/docs/changelog-30","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-07","content":"**16 Conversation components** documented: live answer, thread panel, composer,\nmodel picker, voice capture, voice orb, tool call, artifact card, image generation,\nrich text editor, prompt starters, prompt library, attachment tray, response versions,\nanswer action bar, and feedback sheet."},"33":{"id":"/docs/changelog-31","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-06","content":"**7 Agent status components** documented, including status pill, thinking, reasoning\ntrail, agent phases, step loader, action log, and context meter."},"34":{"id":"/docs/changelog-32","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-06","content":"Docs landing page **redesigned** — a quieter hero with live, self-animating component\npreviews and the full library advertised as preview cards."},"35":{"id":"/docs/changelog-33","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-06","content":"Component documentation updated and **sections reorganised** for clarity (Agent status,\nConversation, Charts and tables, Dates, Forms and inputs)."},"36":{"id":"/docs/changelog-34","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-06","content":"Light wordmark asset added so the logo reads correctly in dark mode."},"37":{"id":"/docs/changelog-35","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-06","content":"**GitHub Pages** deployment enabled, with the private components repository read through\na GitHub App token in CI."},"38":{"id":"/docs/changelog-36","page_id":"/docs/changelog","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/changelog#2026-11-06","content":"Initial commit — docs site scaffolded on Next.js and Fumadocs."},"39":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","type":"page","content":"Account table","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/account-table"},"40":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-0","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table","content":"Customer accounts with health, plan and an agent note per row."},"41":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-1","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/account-table#usage","content":"Usage"},"42":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-2","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"Properties"},"43":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-3","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/account-table#theming","content":"Theming"},"44":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-4","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table","content":"Customer accounts you can search and filter by plan. Each row shows the logo, plan tag, seats, a\nhealth bar and the MRR; click a row and it opens to the note the agent left — with an optional\naction button (like **Draft email**) that spins until its promise settles, then shows its done\nlabel. The rows stagger in again whenever the search or the filter changes."},"45":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-5","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                    | Description                                                                                                  |\n| ---------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `accounts` | `AccountTableAccount[]` | The account rows. Each has `name`, `color`, `plan`, `seats`, `health` (0–100), `mrr` and an optional `note`. |","table":"table-0"},"46":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-6","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name    | Type       | Description                                                                           |\n| ------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `plans` | `string[]` | The plan filters after All. Defaults to the plans in `accounts`, in first-seen order. |","table":"table-0"},"47":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-7","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                   | Description                                                                  |\n| ----------- | ---------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `planTones` | `Record<string, Tone>` | The tag colour per plan. Defaults to Enterprise purple, Pro blue, Team teal. |","table":"table-0"},"48":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-8","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type     | Description                              |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `plan` / `defaultPlan` | `string` | The active plan filter, or `''` for All. |","table":"table-0"},"49":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-9","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                          |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onPlanChange` | `(plan) => void` | Called when a filter chip is picked. |","table":"table-0"},"50":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-10","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type     | Description                             |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `query` / `defaultQuery` | `string` | The search text. Matches account names. |","table":"table-0"},"51":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-11","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                        |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onQueryChange` | `(query) => void` | Called as the search text changes. |","table":"table-0"},"52":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-12","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type             | Description                               |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `string \\| null` | The account whose row is open, or `null`. |","table":"table-0"},"53":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-13","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                        |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(name) => void` | Called when a row opens or closes. |","table":"table-0"},"54":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-14","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                             | Description                                                                                              |\n| -------- | -------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `action` | `{ label; doneLabel?; onClick }` | A button in the open row's note. Return a promise and it spins until it settles, then shows `doneLabel`. |","table":"table-0"},"55":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-15","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | The search field's placeholder. Defaults to `Search accounts`. |","table":"table-0"},"56":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-16","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `emptyLabel` | `string` | Shown when nothing matches the search and filter. |","table":"table-0"},"57":{"id":"/docs/components/account-table-17","page_id":"/docs/components/account-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/account-table#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The plan\ntags run a little brighter than the shared tones — each plan takes its own saturated tint (blue,\npurple, teal and so on), and the health bar fills green from 80, amber from 60 and red below, all\nfrom the theme tokens. In Soft the panel, chips and tags are rounder."},"58":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","type":"page","content":"Action log","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/action-log"},"59":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-0","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log","content":"Every tool call the agent makes, as a list that grows while it works, where each row opens to show its output."},"60":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-1","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/action-log#usage","content":"Usage"},"61":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-2","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/action-log#properties","content":"Properties"},"62":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-3","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/action-log#theming","content":"Theming"},"63":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-4","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log","content":"An action log is a streaming list of what the agent does: each read, search, edit or command\nlands as a row, running with a spinner, then done with a check and the time it took. A row with\noutput opens to show it, like a diff or test run. The header shows a spinner while the run is live\nand a green dot once it finishes."},"64":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-5","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log#properties","content":"| Name      | Type       | Description                                                                                                                                                      |\n| --------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `actions` | `Action[]` | The tool calls, newest at the end. Each has an `icon`, a `title`, an optional `detail`, a `state` of running or done, an optional `time`, and optional `output`. |","table":"table-0"},"65":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-6","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                    |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The header text. Defaults to \"Agent activity\". |","table":"table-0"},"66":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-7","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                           |\n| --------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `running` | `boolean` | Shows a spinner in the header while true, and a green dot once false. |","table":"table-0"},"67":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-8","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                         |\n| -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The words beside the header mark. Defaults to \"Running step N\", then \"N steps, Xs\". |","table":"table-0"},"68":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-9","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set false to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"69":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-10","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type       | Description                       |\n| ------------------------ | ---------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `onToggle` / `toggleRow` | `callback` | Fires when a row opens or closes. |","table":"table-0"},"70":{"id":"/docs/components/action-log-11","page_id":"/docs/components/action-log","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/action-log#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the rows and the output panes are squared off with hairline edges; in Soft they are\nrounded chips with soft fills. Added and removed lines in a row's output take the add and remove\ncolors from the tokens."},"71":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","type":"page","content":"Activity heatmap","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap"},"72":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-0","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","content":"When the agent and the team were busy, by day and hour."},"73":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-1","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#usage","content":"Usage"},"74":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-2","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"Properties"},"75":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-3","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#theming","content":"Theming"},"76":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-4","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","content":"An activity heatmap shows when something is busy, as a 7×24 grid of cells — one a day down, one\nan hour across — each tinted from the accent by its value. Pass one or more `series`; each is 168\nvalues from 0 to 1 (Monday 12am first), with a `max` and `unit` for the tips and an optional\n`note`. With two or more series a switch appears, and picking one sweeps it in as a wave from the\ntop left. In a narrow card the grid shows half the day at a time in bigger cells and scrolls\nsideways, starting at the latest hours."},"77":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-5","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                      | Description                                                      |\n| -------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `series` | `ActivityHeatmapSeries[]` | One or more series; the switch shows when there are two or more. |","table":"table-0"},"78":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-6","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                         |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` | `string` | The series on show, by key. Leave it out to let the switch pick it. |","table":"table-0"},"79":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-7","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultValue` | `string` | The series shown first when uncontrolled. Defaults to the first series. |","table":"table-0"},"80":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-8","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name            | Type            | Description                            |\n| --------------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(key) => void` | Called when the switch picks a series. |","table":"table-0"},"81":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-9","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                          |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `title` | `string` | Header text. Defaults to `Activity`. |","table":"table-0"},"82":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-10","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                                                   |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `period` | `string` | The line under the title before the cells fill in, and when a series has no note. Defaults to `Last 4 weeks`. |","table":"table-0"},"83":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-11","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                              |\n| -------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `series[].key` | `string` | Identifies the series, used by `value` / `defaultValue`. |","table":"table-0"},"84":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-12","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                     |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `series[].label` | `string` | The switch label, like `Agent`. |","table":"table-0"},"85":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-13","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name              | Type       | Description                                             |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `series[].values` | `number[]` | 168 values from 0 to 1, one an hour, Monday 12am first. |","table":"table-0"},"86":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-14","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                       |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `series[].max` | `number` | What a full cell counts, for the tips, like `40`. |","table":"table-0"},"87":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-15","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `series[].unit` | `string` | What it counts, for the tips, like `runs`. |","table":"table-0"},"88":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-16","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                       |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `series[].note` | `string` | The line under the title while this series shows. |","table":"table-0"},"89":{"id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap-17","page_id":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/activity-heatmap#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface, and each cell is a mix of the accent into the chip by its value — so the whole\ngrid shifts with the theme's accent and the empty cells read against the surface. In Soft the card\nand cells are a touch rounder."},"90":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","type":"page","content":"Agent inbox","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox"},"91":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-0","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","content":"Every run that needs you, is running or is done, in one list."},"92":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-1","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#usage","content":"Usage"},"93":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-2","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"Properties"},"94":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-3","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#theming","content":"Theming"},"95":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-4","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","content":"The agent inbox puts every run in one list, grouped by what it needs: **Needs you**, **Running** and\n**Done**. A running run shows a live clock; one that waits for you offers **Approve**, and one that\nfailed turns red and offers **Retry**. When a run changes group it glides to its new place, an empty\ngroup goes away, and the line beside the title says what is left."},"96":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-5","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name   | Type         | Description                           |\n| ------ | ------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `runs` | `InboxRun[]` | Every run to show, each in its group. |","table":"table-0"},"97":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-6","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name        | Type           | Description                                                |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onApprove` | `(id) => void` | Adds Approve to the runs that need you and haven't failed. |","table":"table-0"},"98":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-7","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name      | Type           | Description                         |\n| --------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `onRetry` | `(id) => void` | Adds Retry to the runs that failed. |","table":"table-0"},"99":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-8","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                              |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The inbox's name. Defaults to `\"Inbox\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"100":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-9","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                                                   |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line beside the title. Defaults to `\"2 need you\"`, then `\"2 running\"`, then `\"All clear · 4 done today\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"101":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-10","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                            |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `run.id` | `string` | Keeps a run's row when it moves group. |","table":"table-0"},"102":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-11","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                           |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run.title` | `string` | What the run is for, like \"Publish the pricing page\". |","table":"table-0"},"103":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-12","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run.agent` | `string` | Which agent runs it. Its first letter marks the row. |","table":"table-0"},"104":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-13","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run.color` | `string` | The mark's fill, like `var(--vo-av-l)`. Defaults to the accent. |","table":"table-0"},"105":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-14","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                       | Description                              |\n| ----------- | -------------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `run.group` | `needs \\| running \\| done` | Which part of the inbox the run sits in. |","table":"table-0"},"106":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-15","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                                          |\n| ------------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run.detail` | `string` | The line under the title: why it needs you, or what it is doing now. |","table":"table-0"},"107":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-16","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name         | Type      | Description                                            |\n| ------------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `run.failed` | `boolean` | Turns the row red and offers Retry instead of Approve. |","table":"table-0"},"108":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-17","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                           |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run.why` | `string` | More on the failure, in a tooltip on its detail line. |","table":"table-0"},"109":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-18","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `run.seconds` | `number` | How long a running run has gone. Its clock counts on from here. |","table":"table-0"},"110":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-19","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `run.ended` | `string` | When a finished run ended, like \"12m ago\". |","table":"table-0"},"111":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox-20","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-inbox","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-inbox#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface with the card shadow; a failed run tints with the bad tokens, the running clock and\nthe Approve pill use the accent, and the avatar marks take the shared `--vo-av-*` colours with their\nown ink. In Soft the panel and its rows are rounder."},"112":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","type":"page","content":"Agent lanes","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes"},"113":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-0","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","content":"Several agents working in parallel, each with its own lane and hand-offs."},"114":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-1","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#usage","content":"Usage"},"115":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-2","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"Properties"},"116":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-3","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#theming","content":"Theming"},"117":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-4","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","content":"Agent lanes show several agents working side by side, each in its own lane and hue — its badge, its\nstep track, its `Working` tag and its stretch of the relay line that joins the badges. A working lane\nbreathes, shimmers and fills its next step; a `handoff` opens a line between two lanes and runs a\nlight down the relay line from the sender's badge to the taker's, and the stretch it crossed stays\nlit. Each `lane` takes a `name`, an `icon`, a `tone`, a `status`, the `activity` it is on, how many\n`steps` the track is cut into and how many are `done`, and an optional `log` the row opens to."},"118":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-5","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name    | Type          | Description                               |\n| ------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `lanes` | `AgentLane[]` | The agents, each in its own lane and hue. |","table":"table-0"},"119":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-6","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Header text. Defaults to \"N agents working\", \"All agents paused\" or \"All N agents finished\". |","table":"table-0"},"120":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-7","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                        |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds to show as `m:ss`. Leave it out to let the header count while agents work. |","table":"table-0"},"121":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-8","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name     | Type      | Description                                                                          |\n| -------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `paused` | `boolean` | Whether every agent is paused. Working lanes then show `Paused` and the clock stops. |","table":"table-0"},"122":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-9","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                                                   |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onPausedChange` | `(paused) => void` | Adds the Pause all / Resume button, until every lane is done. |","table":"table-0"},"123":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-10","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name      | Type           | Description                                                                                |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `handoff` | `AgentHandoff` | The hand-off to show. Clear it and its line slides away; the stretch it crossed stays lit. |","table":"table-0"},"124":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-11","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name       | Type       | Description                                                                  |\n| ---------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `expanded` | `string[]` | Keys of the lanes that are open. Leave it out to let each row toggle itself. |","table":"table-0"},"125":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-12","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"126":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-13","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                          |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `lane.name` | `string` | The agent's name, like \"Researcher\". |","table":"table-0"},"127":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-14","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name        | Type       | Description                     |\n| ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `lane.icon` | `IconName` | The glyph on the agent's badge. |","table":"table-0"},"128":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-15","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                                                                 | Description                         |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `lane.tone` | `blue \\| purple \\| green \\| orange \\| red \\| yellow \\| pink \\| teal` | The lane's hue. Defaults to `blue`. |","table":"table-0"},"129":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-16","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name          | Type                                             | Description                                                                      |\n| ------------- | ------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lane.status` | `queued \\| waiting \\| working \\| paused \\| done` | `working` breathes and fills its next step; `done` fills the badge with its hue. |","table":"table-0"},"130":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-17","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                                                  |\n| --------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lane.activity` | `string` | What the agent is on, or what it waits for. Crossfades on change and shimmers while working. |","table":"table-0"},"131":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-18","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                            |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `lane.steps` | `number` | How many steps the track is cut into. Defaults to `3`. |","table":"table-0"},"132":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-19","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                            |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `lane.done` | `number` | How many steps are finished. The next one fills while the agent works. |","table":"table-0"},"133":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-20","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                                          |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `lane.progress` | `number` | How far through the step in hand, 0 to 1. Leave it out and that step fills part way. |","table":"table-0"},"134":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-21","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                | Description                                                              |\n| ---------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `lane.log` | `{ text; time? }[]` | What the agent did, shown when the lane is opened. New entries slide in. |","table":"table-0"},"135":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-22","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                 | Description                                            |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `handoff` | `{ from; to; what }` | One agent passing work to another down the relay line. |","table":"table-0"},"136":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes-23","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-lanes","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-lanes#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each lane's\nhue comes from the theme's agent palette tokens (`--vo-pb`, `--vo-pl`, `--vo-pm` …) with a livelier\n\"mark\" variant for its track, line and finished badge, so the lanes stay 3:1 against the surface; in\ndark mode the agent colours are light already and are used as they are. In the Soft style the lanes\nare rounder and the tracks are hatched rather than washed."},"137":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","type":"page","content":"Agent phases","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-phases"},"138":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-0","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases","content":"One line for which phase an agent is in, from thinking to done, that stops to ask, says when it is slow, and folds to how long it took."},"139":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-1","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#usage","content":"Usage"},"140":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-2","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"Properties"},"141":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-3","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#theming","content":"Theming"},"142":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-4","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases","content":"Agent phases show which phase the agent is in, in one line: its glyph, its name shimmering while the\nphase lasts, and the seconds so far, with a track of six short segments under it that fills phase by\nphase. When the agent needs you, is slow or fails, a line under the track says so with what to do;\nonce it is done the line reads how long it took and opens to the phases it ran through."},"143":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-5","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                                             | Description                  |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `phase` | `thinking \\| searching \\| reading \\| waiting \\| writing \\| done` | Which phase the agent is in. |","table":"table-0"},"144":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-6","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                     |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | What the line says. Defaults to the phase's name; once done, \"Thought for 12s\". |","table":"table-0"},"145":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-7","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                       |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds so far. Counts by itself while left out, and stops while waiting for you. |","table":"table-0"},"146":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-8","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                                                   |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `error` | `object` | A step that failed: the line turns red and says so, with Retry. Has `text`, optional `detail`, and `onRetry`. |","table":"table-0"},"147":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-9","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `slow` | `object` | Shown while the phase takes long, with Stop. Has `text` and an optional `onStop`. |","table":"table-0"},"148":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-10","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                                                                               |\n| ----- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ask` | `object` | What the agent waits for in the waiting phase. Has `text`, optional `approveLabel`, `onApprove` and optional `onDecline`. |","table":"table-0"},"149":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-11","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name   | Type                    | Description                                                     |\n| ------ | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `took` | `Record<phase, number>` | Seconds each phase took, for the list a finished line opens to. |","table":"table-0"},"150":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-12","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                                                      |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether the finished line is open. Leave `open` out to let the header toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"151":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-phases-13","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-phases","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-phases#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The glyph\nand the current segment take the phase's colour — the accent while it works, amber while it waits,\nred on an error and green when done. In Blueprint the segments are squared off and the shimmer rests\non a solid colour."},"152":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","type":"page","content":"Agent run timeline","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline"},"153":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-0","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","content":"Every model and tool step of a run on one time axis — a Gantt chart with a playhead, the time each step takes, and the cost as it adds up."},"154":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-1","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#usage","content":"Usage"},"155":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-2","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"Properties"},"156":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-3","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#theming","content":"Theming"},"157":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-4","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","content":"An agent run timeline draws one run as a Gantt chart. Every step is a bar on a shared time axis:\nthe model thinking or writing (purple), a tool like a file read or a test run (teal), or an app the\nagent works in, such as Figma or GitHub (orange), each with its own mark. A playhead marks now while\nthe run streams and the lanes it has passed take a faint wash; the step at work breathes a ring round\nits icon and its bar carries a bright leading edge. A failed step hatches red and tags its label, and\na retry hangs a dashed line off the end of the step it retries. The key under the title counts how\nlong each kind has run, and the footer adds up the total time, cost, steps and retries. Once the run\nis done the playhead stops at the finish and turns green."},"158":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-5","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The run's name, shown over the status line. |","table":"table-0"},"159":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-6","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                                          |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `TimelineStep[]` | The steps of the run, each a bar on the shared axis. |","table":"table-0"},"160":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-7","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                                                   |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `time` | `number` | Seconds into the run. Bars grow up to it and the playhead sits on it. Leave it out once the run has finished. |","table":"table-0"},"161":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-8","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                                   |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `span` | `number` | Seconds the axis covers. Defaults to the end of the last step, rounded up to a multiple of 4. |","table":"table-0"},"162":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-9","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name    | Type       | Description                                                       |\n| ------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ticks` | `number[]` | Labels on the axis, in seconds. Defaults to quarters of the span. |","table":"table-0"},"163":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-10","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                            |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to the steps running now, then \"Finished in 11.7s\". |","table":"table-0"},"164":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-11","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                                                                                                                         |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stats` | `TimelineStat[]` | The figures in the footer once the run is done. Defaults to the total time, cost, steps and retries, which count up while it plays. |","table":"table-0"},"165":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-12","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                      | Description                                                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `kindLabels` | `{ model?; tool?; app? }` | The names of the kinds in the key. Defaults to Model, Tools and Apps. |","table":"table-0"},"166":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-13","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set false to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"167":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-14","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#properties","content":"A `TimelineStep` has a `label`, an optional `icon` or `brand` (an app's own mark, like `figma`,\n`github` or `slack`), a `kind` (`model`, `tool` or `app`, which picks its colour), a `start` and\n`duration` in seconds, an optional `color`, `cost`, and — for a step that failed — `failed`, a `tag`\nand a `note`, and `retry` to hang a dashed line off the step it retries. A `TimelineStat` has a\n`value`, a `label` and an optional `icon`."},"168":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline-15","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-run-timeline#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each kind\nkeeps its colour from the chart palette — purple for the model, teal for tools, orange for apps — and\nthe playhead runs in the accent, turning green at the finish. In Blueprint the bars square off and a\nrunning bar switches from a sweeping sheen to a marching stripe; a failed bar is red and hatched in\nevery theme."},"169":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","type":"page","content":"Agent tree","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-tree"},"170":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-0","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree","content":"An orchestrator and its sub-agents, with cost rolled up per branch."},"171":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-1","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#usage","content":"Usage"},"172":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-2","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"Properties"},"173":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-3","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#theming","content":"Theming"},"174":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-4","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree","content":"An agent tree shows an orchestrator and its sub-agents as a tree. Each row has its `name`, its\n`task`, a status glyph and a `cost`; a branch's cost is its own plus everything under it, and the\nheader rolls up the whole run. A chevron folds a branch, and the arrow keys move through it as in\nany tree view. A failed step can carry a `fix` — a button under its task that offers the way out."},"175":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-5","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                                    |\n| ------ | ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `root` | `AgentNode` | The orchestrator, with its agents and their steps as children. |","table":"table-0"},"176":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-6","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The run's goal, like \"Redesign the pricing page\". |","table":"table-0"},"177":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-7","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                  |\n| -------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to \"Running\", \"N steps failed\" or \"Done\". |","table":"table-0"},"178":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-8","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds to show as `m:ss`. Leave it out to count up until the root is done. |","table":"table-0"},"179":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-9","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name      | Type              | Description                                                                         |\n| --------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `summary` | `string \\| false` | Shown under the tree once the root is done. `false` hides it; default rolls one up. |","table":"table-0"},"180":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-10","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name        | Type       | Description                              |\n| ----------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `collapsed` | `string[]` | Ids of the folded branches (controlled). |","table":"table-0"},"181":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-11","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name               | Type       | Description                                 |\n| ------------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultCollapsed` | `string[]` | Ids folded to begin with when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"182":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-12","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name                | Type            | Description                                                      |\n| ------------------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCollapsedChange` | `(ids) => void` | Emitted when a branch folds or unfolds, with the ids now folded. |","table":"table-0"},"183":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-13","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                  | Description                                                 |\n| ------------ | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `formatCost` | `(dollars) => string` | Writes a cost. Defaults to dollars and cents, like `$0.12`. |","table":"table-0"},"184":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-14","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `AgentNode.id` | `string` | Identifies the node; used as the fold key. |","table":"table-0"},"185":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-15","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                            |\n| ---------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `AgentNode.name` | `string` | Like \"Design agent\", or a step's name. |","table":"table-0"},"186":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-16","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                                    |\n| ---------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `AgentNode.task` | `string` | Its task, or what it is doing now. Crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"187":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-17","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name               | Type                                  | Description                          |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `AgentNode.status` | `queued \\| running \\| done \\| failed` | Picks the status glyph and row tint. |","table":"table-0"},"188":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-18","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                                                    |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `AgentNode.cost` | `number` | What this node spent on its own. A branch shows this plus everything under it. |","table":"table-0"},"189":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-19","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name            | Type                 | Description                                                        |\n| --------------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `AgentNode.fix` | `{ label; onClick }` | On a failed step, a button under its task that offers the way out. |","table":"table-0"},"190":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-20","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#properties","content":"| Name                 | Type          | Description                          |\n| -------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `AgentNode.children` | `AgentNode[]` | The agents or steps under this node. |","table":"table-0"},"191":{"id":"/docs/components/agent-tree-21","page_id":"/docs/components/agent-tree","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/agent-tree#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The tree\nsits on a surface; the running glyph spins in the accent colour, a done branch turns green and a\nfailed step tints its row with the bad-tone background, so it reads in either theme. In Soft the\ncard, rows and the fix button are rounder."},"192":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","type":"page","content":"Answer action bar","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar"},"193":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","content":"Copy, regenerate, rate and listen to an answer from one row under it."},"194":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#usage","content":"Usage"},"195":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"Properties"},"196":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#theming","content":"Theming"},"197":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","content":"Every action on an answer in one raised rail under it: **copy** it, **regenerate** it — which\nkeeps each version and pages between them — give it a **thumbs** up or down (a down asks what was\noff, and the reason can write a new version that answers it), and **read it aloud**, which widens\nthe button into a progress bar and a clock and lights each word as it is read. Pass `versions`\noldest first; each version carries its own `meta`, its own `rating`, and an optional `changed`\nphrase that is highlighted as what moved from the version before."},"198":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `question` | `string` | The person's message the answer replies to, shown as a bubble above it. |","table":"table-0"},"199":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-6","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name       | Type              | Description                                       |\n| ---------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `versions` | `AnswerVersion[]` | Every version of the answer so far, oldest first. |","table":"table-0"},"200":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-7","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name                         | Type     | Description                                                                        |\n| ---------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `version` / `defaultVersion` | `number` | Which version is showing. Leave `version` out to let the arrows page through them. |","table":"table-0"},"201":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-8","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name              | Type              | Description                            |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onVersionChange` | `(index) => void` | Called when the version shown changes. |","table":"table-0"},"202":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-9","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                                         |\n| ----------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `streaming` | `boolean` | The newest version is still being written: paging and reading wait. |","table":"table-0"},"203":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-10","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name           | Type         | Description                                                              |\n| -------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onRegenerate` | `() => void` | Called by the regenerate button. Add a version and show it to answer it. |","table":"table-0"},"204":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-11","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name     | Type             | Description                                    |\n| -------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCopy` | `(text) => void` | Called with the plain text after it is copied. |","table":"table-0"},"205":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-12","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                      | Description                                                  |\n| -------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onRate` | `(index, rating) => void` | Called when a thumb is pressed or pressed again to clear it. |","table":"table-0"},"206":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-13","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name      | Type       | Description                                                                                            |\n| --------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `reasons` | `string[]` | The reasons a thumbs down offers. Defaults to Wrong numbers, Too long, Not our tone, Missed the brief. |","table":"table-0"},"207":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-14","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                      | Description                                        |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onReason` | `(index, reason) => void` | Called with the reason picked after a thumbs down. |","table":"table-0"},"208":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-15","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                              |\n| -------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The quiet line under the bar, like \"Writing a new version\". It shimmers while streaming. |","table":"table-0"},"209":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-16","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name         | Type         | Description                                                 |\n| ------------ | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `statusTone` | `warn \\| ok` | `warn` turns the status amber; `ok` gives it a green check. |","table":"table-0"},"210":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-17","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name                         | Type                        | Description                                                               |\n| ---------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `reading` / `defaultReading` | `idle \\| playing \\| paused` | Read aloud: `playing` lights each word in turn, `paused` keeps the place. |","table":"table-0"},"211":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-18","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name              | Type              | Description                                             |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onReadingChange` | `(state) => void` | Called when read-aloud starts, pauses, resumes or ends. |","table":"table-0"},"212":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-19","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                                              |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `secondsPerWord` | `number` | How long the built-in reading clock gives each word. Defaults to `0.28`. |","table":"table-0"},"213":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-20","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"214":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-21","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#properties","content":"| Name            | Type                                 | Description                                                                                                |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `AnswerVersion` | `{ text; changed?; meta?; rating? }` | One version: its `text`, the `changed` phrase that is highlighted, its quiet `meta`, and its own `rating`. |","table":"table-0"},"215":{"id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar-22","page_id":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/answer-action-bar#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The rail\nis a surface pill with the shared shadow; the thumbs tint with the ok and bad tokens when pressed,\nthe read-aloud button and the lit word pick up the accent tint, and the changed phrase is marked\nwith the ok highlight — all from the theme tokens, so the bar reads against a light or a dark\nthread."},"216":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","type":"page","content":"Artifact card","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/artifact-card"},"217":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-0","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card","content":"A file the agent made, with its versions, Open, Copy and Download."},"218":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-1","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#usage","content":"Usage"},"219":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-2","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"Properties"},"220":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-3","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#theming","content":"Theming"},"221":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-4","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card","content":"A file the agent made, shown four ways with the same behaviour: a `compact` row, a `preview` card\nwith its first page, an `inline` chip inside a message, or a `stack` of its versions. Each plays a\nwriting state while `state` is `writing` — the meta line shows `status` and the actions hold back —\nthen settles when it turns `ready`. From there you can open the file in a reader, switch between its\n`versions`, Copy its content and Download it."},"222":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-5","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                                    | Description                                         |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `variant` | `compact \\| preview \\| inline \\| stack` | How the card shows the file. Defaults to `compact`. |","table":"table-0"},"223":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-6","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                | Description                 |\n| ---------- | ------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `versions` | `ArtifactVersion[]` | The versions, oldest first. |","table":"table-0"},"224":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-7","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                  |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `version` | `number` | Index of the version shown. Leave it out to let the versions menu change it. |","table":"table-0"},"225":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-8","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultVersion` | `number` | The version shown at first. Defaults to the latest. |","table":"table-0"},"226":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-9","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name              | Type                | Description                            |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onVersionChange` | `(version) => void` | Called when the shown version changes. |","table":"table-0"},"227":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-10","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name    | Type               | Description                                                                    |\n| ------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `state` | `writing \\| ready` | `writing` holds the actions back and shows `status`; `ready` settles the card. |","table":"table-0"},"228":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-11","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                             |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line shown while writing, like \"Reading the page…\". |","table":"table-0"},"229":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-12","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `progress` | `number` | How far the writing has got, from 0 to 1. The compact card draws it along its bottom edge. |","table":"table-0"},"230":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-13","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `kind` | `string` | The kind of file on the meta line, like \"Report\" or \"Table\". |","table":"table-0"},"231":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-14","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description      |\n| ------ | ---------- | ---------------- |\n| `icon` | `IconName` | The file's icon. |","table":"table-0"},"232":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-15","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                                    |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `fileName` | `string` | The name Download saves under, before \"-v3.md\". Defaults to the slugged title. |","table":"table-0"},"233":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-16","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                                               |\n| ----- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ext` | `string` | The extension Download saves with. `csv` also shows the content as a table in the reader. |","table":"table-0"},"234":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-17","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                | Description                                                                               |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpen` | `(version) => void` | Called when the file is opened. With a handler, Open does not show the card's own reader. |","table":"table-0"},"235":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-18","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `openLabel` | `string` | The Open button's tip, like \"Open beside the chat\". Its label stays \"Open\". |","table":"table-0"},"236":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-19","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                | Description                                                       |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCopy` | `(version) => void` | Called after Copy has put the version's content on the clipboard. |","table":"table-0"},"237":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-20","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                | Description                                                      |\n| ------------ | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDownload` | `(version) => void` | Called after Download has saved the version's content as a file. |","table":"table-0"},"238":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-21","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name                    | Type     | Description                      |\n| ----------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `ArtifactVersion.title` | `string` | The file's name in this version. |","table":"table-0"},"239":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-22","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type     | Description                                            |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ArtifactVersion.meta` | `string` | When this version was made, like \"edited 2 hours ago\". |","table":"table-0"},"240":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-23","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type     | Description                                                    |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ArtifactVersion.note` | `string` | What changed in this version. Shown in the menu and the stack. |","table":"table-0"},"241":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-24","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type     | Description                                                |\n| ------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ArtifactVersion.content` | `string` | The file itself, as Markdown (or CSV when `ext` is `csv`). |","table":"table-0"},"242":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-25","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type     | Description                                                                         |\n| ------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ArtifactVersion.summary` | `string` | The text on the preview's first page. Defaults to the first paragraph of `content`. |","table":"table-0"},"243":{"id":"/docs/components/artifact-card-26","page_id":"/docs/components/artifact-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/artifact-card#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the shared shadow, the icon tile and version marks take the accent, and the\nreader opens over the card's nearest positioned ancestor — the stage here, your chat column in an\napp. In Soft the card and its buttons are rounder; the stack also casts a soft shadow on the desk\nthat fades as the sheets are laid out."},"244":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","type":"page","content":"Attachment tray","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray"},"245":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-0","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","content":"Drop files for the agent and watch each one upload."},"246":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-1","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#usage","content":"Usage"},"247":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-2","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"Properties"},"248":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-3","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#theming","content":"Theming"},"249":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-4","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","content":"A drop zone, then the files as plain rows. Each file wears its type's hue — its badge, its\nprogress ring and the wash that fills its row from the left as it uploads. Once a file is up the\nagent reads it: the line shimmers, then says what it found, like `12 pages`. Pass `files` with each\none's `progress`, `reading` and `detail`; `onFiles` hands back what the person dropped or picked."},"250":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-5","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name    | Type           | Description                                               |\n| ------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `files` | `Attachment[]` | The files in the tray, each uploading then read in place. |","table":"table-0"},"251":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-6","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                      | Description                                                          |\n| --------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onFiles` | `(files: File[]) => void` | Files the person dropped on the tray or picked with the file dialog. |","table":"table-0"},"252":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-7","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name       | Type           | Description                                                               |\n| ---------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRemove` | `(id) => void` | Adds a remove button to each file. Called once the file has animated out. |","table":"table-0"},"253":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-8","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                                             |\n| ------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `ReactNode` | The drop zone's heading. Defaults to \"Drop files here\". |","table":"table-0"},"254":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-9","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                 | Description                                                  |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `action` | `{ label; onClick }` | A link after \"or\" in the drop zone, like \"add sample files\". |","table":"table-0"},"255":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-10","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                    |\n| -------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `accept` | `string` | Passed to the file input, like `image/*,.pdf`. |","table":"table-0"},"256":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-11","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| --------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `summary` | `string` | The line under the list. Defaults to how many files the agent can read. |","table":"table-0"},"257":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-12","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name       | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ---------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dragging` | `boolean` | Shows the drop zone as if a file were being dragged over it, for a scripted demo. |","table":"table-0"},"258":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-13","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                              |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `file.progress` | `number` | 0 to 100. The ring closes and the row fills with the file type's colour. |","table":"table-0"},"259":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-14","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name           | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| -------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `file.reading` | `boolean` | While the agent reads the file: a spinner, and \"Reading\" shimmering after the size. |","table":"table-0"},"260":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-15","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `file.detail` | `string` | What the agent found once it has read the file, like \"12 pages\". |","table":"table-0"},"261":{"id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray-16","page_id":"/docs/components/attachment-tray","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/attachment-tray#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each file\ntakes its hue from its type — PDF, image, CSV and the rest — drawn from the palette tokens, so the\nbadge, the ring and the row wash stay in step across the themes; in Soft the drop zone and badges are\nrounder. The dashed drop-zone edge, the uploading rings and the reading shimmer all respect\n`prefers-reduced-motion`."},"262":{"id":"/docs/components/badge","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","type":"page","content":"Badge","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/badge"},"263":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-0","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge","content":"A small label for a plan, environment, or status, with an optional dot or icon and an optional remove button."},"264":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-1","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/badge#usage","content":"Usage"},"265":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-2","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/badge#properties","content":"Properties"},"266":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-3","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/badge#theming","content":"Theming"},"267":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-4","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge","content":"A badge is a compact label. Its `tone` picks the color (neutral, the accent tint, the three\nstates, or one of eight tag colors). Two sizes, an optional dot or icon before the label, and an\noptional remove button after it."},"268":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-5","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge#properties","content":"| Name   | Type                                                                                                                      | Description                                        |\n| ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tone` | `neutral \\| accent \\| success \\| warning \\| danger \\| blue \\| violet \\| green \\| orange \\| red \\| yellow \\| pink \\| teal` | Color as text on its own tint. Neutral by default. |","table":"table-0"},"269":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-6","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                                    |\n| ------ | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `size` | `sm \\| md` | `sm` is 20px tall, `md` is 24px (the default). |","table":"table-0"},"270":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-7","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge#properties","content":"| Name  | Type      | Description                                  |\n| ----- | --------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `dot` | `boolean` | A dot in the badge's color before the label. |","table":"table-0"},"271":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-8","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description               |\n| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `IconName` | An icon before the label. |","table":"table-0"},"272":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-9","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge#properties","content":"| Name                  | Type       | Description                            |\n| --------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onRemove` / `remove` | `callback` | Shows a remove button after the label. |","table":"table-0"},"273":{"id":"/docs/components/badge-10","page_id":"/docs/components/badge","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/badge#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the badge is squared off and set in small caps with a hairline in its own color; in Soft\nit is a pill."},"274":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","type":"page","content":"Bar chart","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/bar-chart"},"275":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart","content":"Weekly agent runs, split by outcome, with a range switch."},"276":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#usage","content":"Usage"},"277":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"Properties"},"278":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#theming","content":"Theming"},"279":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart","content":"A bar chart plots a value per bar, with a readout on hover that breaks each one down by `series` and\na switch between `ranges`. The bars grow in one after another a moment after the chart appears, then\nredraw left to right on every switch while the total rolls to its new figure. Off by default each\nbar is one block in the accent; set `stacked` to split every bar into its parts in the chart palette,\nwith a legend."},"280":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                      |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `label` | `string` | The name over the big number, like \"Agent runs\". |","table":"table-0"},"281":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type               | Description                                                                                                                                                            |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `series` | `BarChartSeries[]` | What each part of a bar means, in order. The readout breaks each bar down by these. Each has a `label`, an optional `tipLabel` and, when stacked, an optional `color`. |","table":"table-0"},"282":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                                                                                                               |\n| --------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stacked` | `boolean` | Draws each bar as a stack of its parts in the palette's colours, with a legend. Off by default: one bar in the accent, with the breakdown in the readout. |","table":"table-0"},"283":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type              | Description                                                                                                                              |\n| -------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ranges` | `BarChartRange[]` | One set of bars per range. Each has a `key`, a `label` and `bars: { label, values }[]`. With more than one, a switch picks between them. |","table":"table-0"},"284":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `range` | `string` | Key of the range shown. Leave it out to let the switch change it. |","table":"table-0"},"285":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                           |\n| -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultRange` | `string` | The range shown first when uncontrolled. Defaults to the first range. |","table":"table-0"},"286":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name            | Type                    | Description                                      |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onRangeChange` | `(key: string) => void` | Called with the new key when the switch changes. |","table":"table-0"},"287":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                      |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `unit` | `string` | What the values count, like \"runs\" in \"66 runs\". |","table":"table-0"},"288":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                    | Description                                             |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `(n: number) => string` | Writes a value. Defaults to whole numbers like `1,240`. |","table":"table-0"},"289":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#properties","content":"Each `BarChartBar` carries `values: number[]` — one per series, stacked from the bottom — so the\nseries order sets the order of the parts, the legend and the breakdown in the readout."},"290":{"id":"/docs/components/bar-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/bar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/bar-chart#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The bars\nuse the chart palette (`--vo-c1..c6`: the accent, then violet, orange, green…) unless a series sets\nits own `color`; the readout tooltip sits on the ink tone and the big number and labels read from the\nforeground and muted tokens. In Soft the bars and tooltip are rounder."},"291":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","type":"page","content":"Browser session","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/browser-session"},"292":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-0","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session","content":"The agent browsing the web for you step by step, in a small browser frame with the steps it takes, and Pause and Take over."},"293":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-1","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/browser-session#usage","content":"Usage"},"294":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-2","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"Properties"},"295":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-3","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/browser-session#theming","content":"Theming"},"296":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-4","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session","content":"A browser session shows the agent browsing the web for you: a small browser frame with the page it\nis on, the steps it takes under it, and Pause and Take over. When a step waits for you — a cookie\nbanner in the way, say — it shows why and a button to let the agent go on. Take over hands the page\nto you: its frame turns the accent colour, its controls become usable, and the button reads Hand\nback."},"297":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-5","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                              |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | What the agent is browsing for, like \"Pricing research\". |","table":"table-0"},"298":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-6","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ----- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `url` | `string` | The address bar: the page's address, or the search being typed. |","table":"table-0"},"299":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-7","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name     | Type      | Description                                                       |\n| -------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `search` | `boolean` | Marks `url` as a search, with a magnifier instead of the padlock. |","table":"table-0"},"300":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-8","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name    | Type            | Description                                                                                                                     |\n| ------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `BrowserStep[]` | The steps the agent takes. Each has a `label`, a `state` of `queued`, `running`, `waiting` or `done`, and an optional `detail`. |","table":"table-0"},"301":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-9","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                                 |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cursor` | `object` | The agent's own pointer, in pixels from the page's top left. Hidden while you have control. |","table":"table-0"},"302":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-10","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                                            |\n| ----- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ask` | `object` | While a step waits: the button that lets the agent go on. Has a `label` and `onAllow`. |","table":"table-0"},"303":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-11","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type      | Description                                                                        |\n| -------------------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `paused` / `defaultPaused` | `boolean` | Pause holds the agent where it is. Leave `paused` out to let the button toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"304":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-12","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name                             | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| -------------------------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `inControl` / `defaultInControl` | `boolean` | Take over hands the page to you. Leave `inControl` out to let the button toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"305":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-13","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                  |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds to show as m:ss. Leave it out to let the clock count while browsing. |","table":"table-0"},"306":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-14","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                          |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to a status word, then the clock. |","table":"table-0"},"307":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-15","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                    |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `summary` | `string` | Shown under the steps once every step is done. |","table":"table-0"},"308":{"id":"/docs/components/browser-session-16","page_id":"/docs/components/browser-session","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/browser-session#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The page\nis drawn small, with real words where they matter and grey lines for the rest; a price the agent has\ntaken is marked in the accent fill. While you have control the frame turns the accent colour. In\nBlueprint the frame and chips are squared off."},"309":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","type":"page","content":"Buttons","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/buttons"},"310":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-0","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons","content":"A pill button in the library's variants and sizes, with built-in busy, done and pressed states."},"311":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-1","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/buttons#usage","content":"Usage"},"312":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-2","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"Properties"},"313":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-3","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/buttons#theming","content":"Theming"},"314":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-4","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons","content":"A button is a pill in one of the variants — `primary` for the main action, `soft` and `line` for the\nrest, `ghost` for the quietest — in three sizes. Return a promise from `onClick` and the button runs\nitself: it shows the busy face until the promise settles, then the done face. `ButtonCopy` copies\ntext and flashes a check."},"315":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-5","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                                                | Description                                                             |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `variant` | `primary \\| accent \\| soft \\| line \\| ghost \\| ink` | The style. Left out, a plain pill. `ink` is the old name for `primary`. |","table":"table-0"},"316":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-6","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name   | Type             | Description                           |\n| ------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `size` | `sm \\| md \\| lg` | The three sizes; `md` is the default. |","table":"table-0"},"317":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-7","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description               |\n| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `IconName` | An icon before the label. |","table":"table-0"},"318":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-8","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                              | Description                                                    |\n| --------- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onClick` | `(e) => void \\| Promise<unknown>` | Return a promise and the button runs busy then done by itself. |","table":"table-0"},"319":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-9","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name            | Type      | Description                                                           |\n| --------------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `busy` / `done` | `boolean` | Drive the busy or done face yourself. Clicks are ignored while shown. |","table":"table-0"},"320":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-10","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type        | Description                            |\n| ------------------------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `busyLabel` / `doneLabel` | `ReactNode` | The labels on the busy and done faces. |","table":"table-0"},"321":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-11","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name        | Type            | Description                                             |\n| ----------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `busyGlyph` | `spin \\| think` | The busy glyph: a spinner, or the agent's turning dots. |","table":"table-0"},"322":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-12","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                |\n| --------- | --------- | -------------------------- |\n| `success` | `boolean` | The done face turns green. |","table":"table-0"},"323":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-13","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                        |\n| --------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pressed` | `boolean` | For a toggle: whether it is on, as `aria-pressed`. |","table":"table-0"},"324":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-14","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `tip` / `kbd` | `string` | A tooltip, with an optional shortcut after it. |","table":"table-0"},"325":{"id":"/docs/components/buttons-15","page_id":"/docs/components/buttons","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/buttons#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nvariants read against the theme's accent and surface tokens; in Soft the pills are rounder and\nsofter, and the busy and done faces blur across in either theme."},"326":{"id":"/docs/components/card","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"page","content":"Card","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card"},"327":{"id":"/docs/components/card-0","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"A surface you drop other components onto, with an optional header, body and footer, and an interactive mode that turns the whole card into a hit target."},"328":{"id":"/docs/components/card-1","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#usage","content":"Usage"},"329":{"id":"/docs/components/card-2","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"Properties"},"330":{"id":"/docs/components/card-3","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#theming","content":"Theming"},"331":{"id":"/docs/components/card-4","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"A card is a surface you build other components onto. It has an optional header (a `title`, a\n`subtitle` and an end `action` slot), a body of whatever you put inside, and an optional `footer`\nof actions. `pad` sets the inset; set `interactive` (or pass `onClick`) and the whole card becomes a\nhit target that lifts on hover, takes focus, and fires on Enter or Space."},"332":{"id":"/docs/components/card-5","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                  |\n| ------- | ----------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `title` | `ReactNode` | A title shown in the header. |","table":"table-0"},"333":{"id":"/docs/components/card-6","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name       | Type        | Description                 |\n| ---------- | ----------- | --------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `ReactNode` | A subtitle under the title. |","table":"table-0"},"334":{"id":"/docs/components/card-7","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name     | Type        | Description                                                        |\n| -------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `action` | `ReactNode` | An end slot in the header, aligned right (a badge, a menu button). |","table":"table-0"},"335":{"id":"/docs/components/card-8","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name     | Type        | Description                         |\n| -------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `footer` | `ReactNode` | A footer of actions below the body. |","table":"table-0"},"336":{"id":"/docs/components/card-9","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name          | Type                      | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `footerAlign` | `start \\| end \\| between` | How the footer's actions align. `end` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"337":{"id":"/docs/components/card-10","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name  | Type               | Description                                         |\n| ----- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pad` | `none \\| sm \\| md` | Inset for header, body and footer. `md` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"338":{"id":"/docs/components/card-11","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name          | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `interactive` | `boolean` | Makes the whole card a hit target that lifts, takes focus and fires on Enter/Space. |","table":"table-0"},"339":{"id":"/docs/components/card-12","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"| Name                            | Type       | Description                                                                    |\n| ------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onClick` / `clicked` / `onTap` | `callback` | Fired when an interactive card is activated. Setting it implies `interactive`. |","table":"table-0"},"340":{"id":"/docs/components/card-13","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#properties","content":"In Angular the header end slot and the footer are projected with the `card-action` and `card-footer`\nattributes; in Flutter `action` is a widget and `footer` a list of widgets."},"341":{"id":"/docs/components/card-14","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In Soft\nthe card has rounded corners and floats on a soft shadow; in Blueprint it is squared off with a\nhairline instead of the float. An interactive card lifts on hover and keeps a visible focus ring;\nwith reduced motion it still restyles but does not travel."},"342":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","type":"page","content":"Change review","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/change-review"},"343":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-0","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review","content":"A diff to review hunk by hunk — keep or undo each change, or ask the agent about a line."},"344":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-1","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/change-review#usage","content":"Usage"},"345":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-2","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"Properties"},"346":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-3","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"`ChangedFile` / `Hunk` / `DiffLine`"},"347":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-4","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/change-review#theming","content":"Theming"},"348":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-5","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review","content":"Change review walks a set of changed `files` as a diff. Pick a file in the list, then **keep** or\n**undo** each hunk on its own — Keep turns to a green done chip, an undone hunk's Undo sits on the\nsurface, and pressing either again takes the choice back. **Keep all** settles the current file and\nsteps to the next; **Undo all** settles it in place. Hover a line to reveal its comment button and\nask the agent about that change. The file list rolls each file up to kept, undone or part-decided."},"349":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-6","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type            | Description                                                                 |\n| ------- | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `files` | `ChangedFile[]` | The files to review. Each has a `name`, an optional `path` and its `hunks`. |","table":"table-0"},"350":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-7","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `file` | `number` | The file shown on the right, by index (controlled). |","table":"table-0"},"351":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-8","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                              |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultFile` | `number` | The file shown first when uncontrolled. Defaults to `0`. |","table":"table-0"},"352":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-9","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name           | Type              | Description                         |\n| -------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `onFileChange` | `(index) => void` | Called when the shown file changes. |","table":"table-0"},"353":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-10","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                                 | Description                               |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `decisions` | `Record<string, 'kept' \\| 'undone'>` | Kept or undone, by hunk key (controlled). |","table":"table-0"},"354":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-11","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name               | Type                                 | Description                           |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultDecisions` | `Record<string, 'kept' \\| 'undone'>` | Starting decisions when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"355":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-12","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name                | Type                  | Description                              |\n| ------------------- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `onDecisionsChange` | `(decisions) => void` | Called when any hunk's decision changes. |","table":"table-0"},"356":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-13","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                | Description                                                                                         |\n| ----------- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onComment` | `(comment) => void` | Called when the person asks the agent about a line. Without a question it sends \"Why this change?\". |","table":"table-0"},"357":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-14","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Header over the file list. Defaults to `\"N files changed\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"358":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-15","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `file.name` | `string` | Like `\"PricingCard.tsx\"`. Its extension becomes the type label. |","table":"table-1"},"359":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-16","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `file.path` | `string` | Shown above the diff. Defaults to the name. |","table":"table-1"},"360":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-17","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                           |\n| ------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hunk.title` | `string` | What the change does, like `\"Use the shared button\"`. |","table":"table-1"},"361":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-18","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                              |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `hunk.key` | `string` | Identifies the hunk in `decisions`. Defaults to `\"<file name>#<index>\"`. |","table":"table-1"},"362":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-19","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"| Name        | Type                | Description                                                            |\n| ----------- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `line.kind` | `add \\| del \\| ctx` | `add` and `del` lines are coloured; `ctx` lines are unchanged context. |","table":"table-1"},"363":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-20","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                          |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `line.line` | `number` | The line number shown in the gutter. |","table":"table-1"},"364":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-21","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#changedfile--hunk--diffline","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description      |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------- |\n| `line.text` | `string` | The line's text. |","table":"table-1"},"365":{"id":"/docs/components/change-review-22","page_id":"/docs/components/change-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/change-review#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Added and\nremoved lines take the ok and bad tints; a hunk's Keep reads as the accent on a tint of itself, and\nturns to the green done chip once kept — all from the theme tokens. The comment box uses the field\ntokens, becoming a squircle in Blueprint where the browser supports it."},"366":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","type":"page","content":"Citation hover card","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card"},"367":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-0","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","content":"Hover a citation to see the exact passage it came from."},"368":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-1","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#usage","content":"Usage"},"369":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-2","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"Properties"},"370":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-3","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#theming","content":"Theming"},"371":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-4","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","content":"An answer with numbered citations. Hovering, focusing or tapping one shows its source in a small card\nunderneath — the coloured mark and site, the title, the passage the answer relies on (with the part\nthat matters highlighted) and a link. The card rises in place; moving to another citation replays the\nentrance. It takes the answer `text` (where `[n]` cites source n and a blank line starts a new\nparagraph) and the list of `sources`."},"372":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-5","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                            |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `text` | `string` | The answer. `[n]` cites source n; a blank line starts a new paragraph. |","table":"table-0"},"373":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-6","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                        | Description                                                      |\n| --------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sources` | `CitationHoverCardSource[]` | The sources behind the citations (source n is `sources[n − 1]`). |","table":"table-0"},"374":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-7","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `openLabel` | `string` | The link in the card's corner. Defaults to `Open source`. |","table":"table-0"},"375":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-8","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                                        |\n| ------ | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `open` | `number \\| null` | Opens a source's card from outside (`0` is the first), or closes it with `null`. Hover, focus and taps still work. |","table":"table-0"},"376":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-9","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                      | Description                                                            |\n| -------------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenSource` | `(source, index) => void` | Called when the card's link is clicked, with the source and its index. |","table":"table-0"},"377":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-10","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                      | Description                                                             |\n| -------------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(index \\| null) => void` | Called when a card opens or closes, with the source's index, or `null`. |","table":"table-0"},"378":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-11","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.mark` | `string` | One or two letters on the source's coloured mark, like `B`. |","table":"table-0"},"379":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-12","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                          |\n| -------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.color` | `string` | The mark's colour, like `#4a5a8a` or `var(--vo-pm)`. |","table":"table-0"},"380":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-13","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.site` | `string` | Where it comes from, like `baymard.com` or `Drive`. |","table":"table-0"},"381":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-14","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description         |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------- |\n| `source.title` | `string` | The source's title. |","table":"table-0"},"382":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-15","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name           | Type        | Description                                                               |\n| -------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.quote` | `ReactNode` | The passage the answer relies on. Wrap the part that matters in `<mark>`. |","table":"table-0"},"383":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-16","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                           |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.meta` | `string` | The quiet line in the corner, like `Read 4 days ago`. |","table":"table-0"},"384":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-17","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                              |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `source.href` | `string` | Opens in a new tab from the card's link. |","table":"table-0"},"385":{"id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card-18","page_id":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/citation-hover-card#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card sits\non a surface with the pop shadow; the citation chips use the hover and accent tokens, the quote's accent\nrule uses `--vo-accent-mark` and its highlight uses the selection tint, so it all reads against the\nstage. In Soft the chips and card are rounder."},"386":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","type":"page","content":"Code viewer","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-viewer"},"387":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-0","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer","content":"Code the agent wrote, with line notes you can ask about."},"388":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-1","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#usage","content":"Usage"},"389":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-2","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"Properties"},"390":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-3","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#theming","content":"Theming"},"391":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-4","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer","content":"The code the agent wrote, across one or more files. The lines it changed are marked — their\nnumber turns green and the line gets a wash — and the `+N changed` count in the header follows the\nopen file. Click a line and the agent explains it: a note folds open under the line, reads for a\nmoment, then crossfades to what it says. The copy button copies the open file's text."},"392":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-5","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name    | Type         | Description                                                 |\n| ------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `files` | `CodeFile[]` | The files the agent changed. Each has a `name` and `lines`. |","table":"table-0"},"393":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-6","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `file` | `string` | The open file, by name. Leave it out to let the tabs switch it. |","table":"table-0"},"394":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-7","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                           |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultFile` | `string` | The file open at first when `file` is not controlled. |","table":"table-0"},"395":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-8","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                                          |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onFileChange` | `(name) => void` | Called with the name of the file the tabs switch to. |","table":"table-0"},"396":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-9","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                   |\n| ------ | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `line` | `number \\| null` | The line whose note is open (0 is the first), or `null`. Leave it out to let a click open it. |","table":"table-0"},"397":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-10","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name          | Type             | Description                                           |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultLine` | `number \\| null` | The line open at first when `line` is not controlled. |","table":"table-0"},"398":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-11","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                                                       |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onLineChange` | `(line) => void` | Called with the line whose note opened, or `null` when it closed. |","table":"table-0"},"399":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-12","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                          |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `delay` | `number` | How long a note says \"Reading the line\" before it answers, in ms. Defaults to `600`. |","table":"table-0"},"400":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-13","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `unchangedNote` | `string` | The note for a line the agent didn't change and has nothing to say about. |","table":"table-0"},"401":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-14","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name     | Type             | Description                                    |\n| -------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCopy` | `(text) => void` | Called with the file's text when it is copied. |","table":"table-0"},"402":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-15","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name            | Type                    | Description                                                        |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `CodeLine.code` | `string \\| CodePiece[]` | The line as plain text, or as `[token, text]` pieces to highlight. |","table":"table-0"},"403":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-16","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name               | Type      | Description                                                                   |\n| ------------------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CodeLine.changed` | `boolean` | The agent changed this line: its number turns green and the line gets a wash. |","table":"table-0"},"404":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-17","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                           |\n| --------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `CodeLine.note` | `string` | What the agent says about the line when you click it. |","table":"table-0"},"405":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-18","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#properties","content":"The highlight tokens are `k` keyword, `s` string, `f` function, `cm` comment, `tg` tag and `at`\nattribute."},"406":{"id":"/docs/components/code-viewer-19","page_id":"/docs/components/code-viewer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/code-viewer#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface; the changed-line wash comes from the `ok` token, the open line and its note from\nthe selection tint, and the syntax colours from the shared highlight tokens, so the code reads the\nsame against either theme."},"407":{"id":"/docs/components/composer","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","type":"page","content":"Composer","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/composer"},"408":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-0","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer","content":"Message input with attachments, what to work on, a mode and dictation."},"409":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-1","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/composer#usage","content":"Usage"},"410":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-2","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"Properties"},"411":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-3","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/composer#theming","content":"Theming"},"412":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-4","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer","content":"The composer is the box you write to the agent in — not a plain field but a small component on a\nsurface. Text grows as you type; attachments load as chips above it and hold Send until they are\nready (a failed one shows in red with a Try again button). Two menus set what the agent works on\n(`contexts`) and what it may do (`modes`), a microphone swaps the toolbar for a dictation bar, and\nSend fires `onSubmit` and clears the box. `value`, `attachments`, `context` and `mode` are\ncontrollable — leave the matching input out to let the composer keep that piece itself."},"413":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-5","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type     | Description                                                         |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `defaultValue` | `string` | The text in the box. Leave `value` out to let the composer keep it. |","table":"table-0"},"414":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-6","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                 |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | --------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(value) => void` | Called as the text changes. |","table":"table-0"},"415":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-7","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | The placeholder text. Becomes `Listening…` while dictating. |","table":"table-0"},"416":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-8","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                              | Description                                                     |\n| ---------- | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSubmit` | `({ text, attachments }) => void` | Called when the person sends. The box clears itself afterwards. |","table":"table-0"},"417":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-9","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name              | Type                     | Description                                                         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `busy` / `onStop` | `boolean` / `() => void` | The agent is answering: Send turns into Stop, which calls `onStop`. |","table":"table-0"},"418":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-10","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name     | Type        | Description                           |\n| -------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `thread` | `ReactNode` | The conversation shown above the box. |","table":"table-0"},"419":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-11","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name                                 | Type                   | Description                                                                   |\n| ------------------------------------ | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `attachments` / `defaultAttachments` | `ComposerAttachment[]` | Chips above the text. `loading` holds Send; `error` shows red with Try again. |","table":"table-0"},"420":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-12","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name                  | Type                    | Description                    |\n| --------------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `onAttachmentsChange` | `(attachments) => void` | Called when a chip is removed. |","table":"table-0"},"421":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-13","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type                                   | Description                                |\n| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `addOptions` / `onAdd` | `ComposerOption[]` / `(value) => void` | What the attach menu offers, and the pick. |","table":"table-0"},"422":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-14","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name      | Type            | Description                                 |\n| --------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRetry` | `(key) => void` | Called by Try again on a failed attachment. |","table":"table-0"},"423":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-15","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name                                       | Type                          | Description                                                       |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `contexts` / `context` / `onContextChange` | `ComposerOption[]` / `string` | What the agent works on. The chip only shows when there are some. |","table":"table-0"},"424":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-16","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name                              | Type                          | Description                                            |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `modes` / `mode` / `onModeChange` | `ComposerOption[]` / `string` | What the agent may do. Defaults to Ask, Edit and Plan. |","table":"table-0"},"425":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-17","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name        | Type         | Description                                                           |\n| ----------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDictate` | `() => void` | Called by the microphone. The mic button only shows when this is set. |","table":"table-0"},"426":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-18","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name                             | Type                 | Description                                                     |\n| -------------------------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `dictating` / `dictationSeconds` | `boolean` / `number` | Swaps the toolbar for the dictation bar and the clock it shows. |","table":"table-0"},"427":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-19","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#properties","content":"| Name             | Type             | Description                                                              |\n| ---------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onDictationEnd` | `(keep) => void` | Called by Cancel (`false`, text goes back) or Done (`true`, text stays). |","table":"table-0"},"428":{"id":"/docs/components/composer-20","page_id":"/docs/components/composer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/composer#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The box\nsits on a surface with a soft shadow and the shared tokens drive its chips, menus and the accent\nSend button, so it reads against the stage; in Soft the box and its pills are rounder."},"429":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","type":"page","content":"Context meter","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-meter"},"430":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-0","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter","content":"How full the context is and what fills it, with a Compact action to free room."},"431":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-1","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-meter#usage","content":"Usage"},"432":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-2","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"Properties"},"433":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-3","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/context-meter#theming","content":"Theming"},"434":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-4","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter","content":"A context meter is a pill with a ring that shows how full the context window is. It opens a panel\nwith one bar split by kind, a legend whose rows list what is in each part, and a Compact button\nthat summarises older turns to free room. The ring turns orange past a warning share, and a message\nline fades in with a warning or a result."},"435":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-5","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name    | Type            | Description                                                                                                                  |\n| ------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parts` | `ContextPart[]` | What fills the context. Each has a `key`, a `label`, its `tokens`, an optional `color`, and optional `items` shown on hover. |","table":"table-0"},"436":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-6","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                             |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `limit` | `number` | The size of the context window, in tokens, like 200000. |","table":"table-0"},"437":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-7","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                    |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `warnAt` | `number` | From this share of the limit (0 to 1) the ring turns orange. Defaults to 0.85. |","table":"table-0"},"438":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-8","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                          |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | `string` | A line under the legend. Crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"439":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-9","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name          | Type         | Description                                                            |\n| ------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messageTone` | `warn \\| ok` | warn shows it in orange with a warning sign, ok in green with a check. |","table":"table-0"},"440":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-10","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                     |\n| ----------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `compacted` | `boolean` | Set once compacted: the button turns into Undo. |","table":"table-0"},"441":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-11","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hint` | `string` | The quiet line beside the button. Defaults to \"Summarises older turns\". |","table":"table-0"},"442":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-12","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                        |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the panel is open. Leave it out to let the pill toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"443":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-13","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name                    | Type       | Description                                                                |\n| ----------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCompact` / `compact` | `callback` | Called by Compact. Return a promise and the button spins until it settles. |","table":"table-0"},"444":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-14","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name              | Type       | Description                    |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `onUndo` / `undo` | `callback` | Called by Undo once compacted. |","table":"table-0"},"445":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-15","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#properties","content":"| Name                          | Type       | Description                          |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onOpenChange` / `openChange` | `callback` | Fires when the panel opens or shuts. |","table":"table-0"},"446":{"id":"/docs/components/context-meter-16","page_id":"/docs/components/context-meter","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/context-meter#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the pill, the bar and the panel are squared off; in Soft they are rounded. The ring takes\nthe accent mark and the warning mark past the warning share, and the bar segments take the part\npalette (blue, teal, violet, grey) from the tokens unless a part sets its own color."},"447":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","type":"page","content":"Decision prompt","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt"},"448":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-0","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","content":"The agent asks a few quick questions before it starts."},"449":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-1","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#usage","content":"Usage"},"450":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-2","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"Properties"},"451":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-3","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#theming","content":"Theming"},"452":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-4","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","content":"The agent asks a few quick questions before it starts — one at a time, with a row of\noptions for each. Number keys pick, **Enter** continues and **Skip** lets the agent decide.\nOnce every question is answered the body settles into a summary and a line that says the\nagent is getting going; pass `started` to settle that line with a check."},"453":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-5","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                 | Description                             |\n| ----------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `questions` | `DecisionQuestion[]` | The questions the agent asks, in order. |","table":"table-0"},"454":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-6","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                 | Description                                                                                                              |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `answers` | `(number \\| null)[]` | The answers so far — an option's index, or `null` for a skipped question. Leave it out to let Continue and Skip fill it. |","table":"table-0"},"455":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-7","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name             | Type                 | Description                                           |\n| ---------------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultAnswers` | `(number \\| null)[]` | The answers the prompt starts with when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"456":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-8","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name              | Type                | Description                                                                         |\n| ----------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onAnswersChange` | `(answers) => void` | Called whenever the answers change (a pick, or a skip). Angular: `(answersChange)`. |","table":"table-0"},"457":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-9","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                | Description                                                    |\n| ------------ | ------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onComplete` | `(answers) => void` | Called once every question is answered. Angular: `(complete)`. |","table":"table-0"},"458":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-10","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                                |\n| -------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `skippedLabel` | `string` | What the summary says for a skipped question. Defaults to `Agent decides`. |","table":"table-0"},"459":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-11","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                                                    |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `startLabel` | `string` | The line under the summary while the agent gets going. Defaults to `Starting`. |","table":"table-0"},"460":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-12","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                     |\n| --------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `started` | `boolean` | The agent has got going: the summary line settles with a check. |","table":"table-0"},"461":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-13","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `startedLabel` | `string` | What that line says once started. Defaults to `startLabel`. |","table":"table-0"},"462":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-14","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"463":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-15","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `question.label` | `string` | A short name for the question in the summary, like \"Scope\". |","table":"table-0"},"464":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-16","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                         |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `option.detail` | `string` | Quiet text at the end of the row, like \"3 frames\" or \"Recommended\". |","table":"table-0"},"465":{"id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt-17","page_id":"/docs/components/decision-prompt","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/decision-prompt#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). It sits\nflat in the chat thread by default; set `bare` to `false` to give it its own surface card. The active\nstep dot and the picked option's key badge take the accent tint, so the prompt reads against the stage\nin either theme; in Soft the card, options and pills are rounder."},"466":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","type":"page","content":"Design review","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-review"},"467":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-0","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review","content":"A design review on its way out — checks run, a teammate reviews and the agent answers, then you pick how it ships."},"468":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-1","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-review#usage","content":"Usage"},"469":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-2","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"Properties"},"470":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-3","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-review#theming","content":"Theming"},"471":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-4","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review","content":"Something the agent made, laid out for sign-off. One column runs the `checks`; the other holds the\n`messages` — a teammate's verdict, the agent's reply — oldest first. The `phase` carries it from\n`review` to `approved` (the Ship button turns on), then `shipping`, and finally `live` or\n`scheduled`. Beside the Ship button a menu picks how it ships from your `options`."},"472":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-5","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                    |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | What is up for review, like \"Pricing page v4\". |","table":"table-0"},"473":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-6","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description               |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The line under the title. |","table":"table-0"},"474":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-7","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                             |\n| ------ | ---------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `IconName` | The header mark. Defaults to `palette`. |","table":"table-0"},"475":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-8","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name     | Type            | Description                                                             |\n| -------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `checks` | `ReviewCheck[]` | The Checks column: `{ label; state: wait \\| run \\| ok \\| bad; note? }`. |","table":"table-0"},"476":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-9","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name       | Type              | Description                                                                  |\n| ---------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messages` | `ReviewMessage[]` | The review so far, oldest first: who, an optional verdict tag, and the text. |","table":"table-0"},"477":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-10","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                                  | Description                                                                                                |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `phase` | `review \\| approved \\| shipping \\| live \\| scheduled` | Where it is. `approved` turns the Ship button on; `live`/`scheduled` replace the buttons with a done line. |","table":"table-0"},"478":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-11","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                              |\n| ------ | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `note` | `string` | The line beside the Ship button, like \"Waiting on Maya\". |","table":"table-0"},"479":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-12","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                           |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `waitingLabel` | `string` | Shown in the review column before anyone has written. |","table":"table-0"},"480":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-13","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name      | Type           | Description                                                   |\n| --------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `options` | `ShipOption[]` | The ways it can ship, picked from the menu beside the button. |","table":"table-0"},"481":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-14","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type     | Description                                        |\n| -------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `option` / `defaultOption` | `string` | The picked option key, controlled or uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"482":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-15","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name             | Type            | Description                     |\n| ---------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `onOptionChange` | `(key) => void` | The picked ship option changed. |","table":"table-0"},"483":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-16","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name     | Type               | Description                                          |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onShip` | `(option) => void` | The Ship button was pressed, with the chosen option. |","table":"table-0"},"484":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-17","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                              |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `doneLabel` | `string` | Replaces the chosen label on the done line once it is live or scheduled. |","table":"table-0"},"485":{"id":"/docs/components/design-review-18","page_id":"/docs/components/design-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-review#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a `--vo-panel` surface; the header mark, the verdict tags and the checks' ok/bad glyphs all\ntake their colours from the theme tokens (`--vo-ok`, `--vo-warn`, `--vo-bad`, `--vo-pb`), and the\nShip button follows the accent, so the whole review reads against either theme. Once it is live the\nheader mark shifts to the ok tint."},"486":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","type":"page","content":"Design tuner","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-tuner"},"487":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-0","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner","content":"Tweak a component by hand or let the agent tune it."},"488":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-1","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#usage","content":"Usage"},"489":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-2","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"Properties"},"490":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-3","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#theming","content":"Theming"},"491":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-4","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner","content":"A live preview beside a few sliders, with a button that hands the tuning to the agent. Drag a\nslider — or arrow-key it — to tweak the sample card by hand, or press **Tune with agent** and it\nwalks each value to a target, turns the row it is moving accent, and drops a note on what it\nchanged. Each slider sets a `--vo-<key>` variable on the preview, so the card reshapes live."},"492":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-5","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name     | Type           | Description                                                                       |\n| -------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `params` | `TunerParam[]` | The sliders. Defaults to radius, padding, spacing and shadow for the sample card. |","table":"table-0"},"493":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-6","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                     | Description                                                                      |\n| -------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `values` | `Record<string, number>` | The value of each slider by key. Leave it out to let the sliders keep their own. |","table":"table-0"},"494":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-7","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                                                            |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onValuesChange` | `(values) => void` | Fires with the values by key whenever a slider or the agent moves one. |","table":"table-0"},"495":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-8","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | What is being tuned, like `\"Pricing card\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"496":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-9","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | Quiet line beside the title, like `\"Edited by you\"` or `\"Agent is tuning\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"497":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-10","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                   |\n| -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `active` | `string` | Key of the slider the agent is moving now; its value turns the accent colour. |","table":"table-0"},"498":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-11","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name     | Type      | Description                                                     |\n| -------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tuning` | `boolean` | The agent is tuning: the button thinks and stops taking clicks. |","table":"table-0"},"499":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-12","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                             |\n| ------ | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `note` | `ReactNode` | What the agent changed and why, shown above the button. |","table":"table-0"},"500":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-13","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `actionLabel` | `string` | The button's label, like `\"Tune with agent\"` or `\"Tune again\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"501":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-14","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"| Name     | Type         | Description                                  |\n| -------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onTune` | `() => void` | Fires when the agent-tune button is pressed. |","table":"table-0"},"502":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-15","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#properties","content":"A `TunerParam` is `{ key, label, min, max, value, unit?, decimals? }`: `key` names the `--vo-<key>`\nvariable the preview reads, `unit` is appended to whole numbers (like `px`), and `decimals` shows\nand sets the value with that many decimals instead of rounding."},"503":{"id":"/docs/components/design-tuner-16","page_id":"/docs/components/design-tuner","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/design-tuner#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npreview sits on a chip-tinted stage; the slider fill and knob, the accent CTA and the agent's note\nall draw from the theme tokens, and the sample card's own radius, padding, spacing and shadow are\nexactly what the sliders drive. The agent respects `prefers-reduced-motion`, snapping to the tuned\nvalues instead of walking them."},"504":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","type":"page","content":"Details panel","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/details-panel"},"505":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-0","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel","content":"Properties of a run you can change in place."},"506":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-1","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/details-panel#usage","content":"Usage"},"507":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-2","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"Properties"},"508":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-3","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/details-panel#theming","content":"Theming"},"509":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-4","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel","content":"A details panel shows a record's properties in folding sections and lets you edit them in\nplace. Each `section` holds `rows`: a `select` row picks its value from a small menu (with a\ncoloured dot, an avatar or a plain chevron), a `number` row rolls to its new value, a `tags`\nrow carries labels and an optional add button, and a plain row just shows its `value`. The\naccent flashes behind a value when it changes. A `copyValue` adds a copy button beside the\ntitle."},"510":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-5","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The title at the top, like \"Pricing page redesign\". |","table":"table-0"},"511":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-6","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                    |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `kind` | `string` | A short type tag before the title, like \"RUN\". |","table":"table-0"},"512":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-7","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `copyValue` | `string` | Adds a copy button that copies this, like a run ID. |","table":"table-0"},"513":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-8","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                           |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `copyLabel` | `string` | The copy button's tooltip. Defaults to \"Copy run ID\". |","table":"table-0"},"514":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-9","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                    | Description                                                   |\n| ---------- | ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sections` | `DetailsPanelSection[]` | The folding sections, each a `key`, a `title` and its `rows`. |","table":"table-0"},"515":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-10","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                                                                                        |\n| ------ | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `string[]` | Keys of the open sections. Leave it out to let the headers toggle them; every section starts open. |","table":"table-0"},"516":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-11","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                           |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open) => void` | Called when the open sections change. |","table":"table-0"},"517":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-12","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                               | Description                                            |\n| ---------- | ---------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `row.type` | `text \\| select \\| number \\| tags` | What the row shows. A plain `text` row is the default. |","table":"table-0"},"518":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-13","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name             | Type                                           | Description                                                             |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `select.options` | `{ value; label; detail?; color?; avatar? }[]` | The menu choices, with a dot (`color`), an `avatar` or a plain chevron. |","table":"table-0"},"519":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-14","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type              | Description                          |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `select.onValueChange` | `(value) => void` | Called when the row's value changes. |","table":"table-0"},"520":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-15","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                               |\n| -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `number.value` | `number` | The value, which rolls into view and whenever it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"521":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-16","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name            | Type            | Description                                                                         |\n| --------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `number.format` | `(n) => string` | Turns the number into text. Defaults to a rounded number with thousands separators. |","table":"table-0"},"522":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-17","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                 | Description                                                       |\n| ----------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tags.tags` | `{ label; tone? }[]` | The labels; `tone` tints a chip. Later tags enter with the panel. |","table":"table-0"},"523":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-18","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#properties","content":"| Name         | Type         | Description                                                        |\n| ------------ | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `tags.onAdd` | `() => void` | Shows an add button after the labels and fires when it is pressed. |","table":"table-0"},"524":{"id":"/docs/components/details-panel-19","page_id":"/docs/components/details-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/details-panel#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npanel sits on a surface; values hover and flash with the accent tint, dots and avatars take\nthe hue tokens, and the folding sections draw from the shared `fold` and popover tokens, so\neverything reads against either theme. In Soft the panel, menus and chips are rounder."},"525":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","type":"page","content":"Donut chart","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/donut-chart"},"526":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart","content":"Where the agent's time went, by kind of task."},"527":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#usage","content":"Usage"},"528":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"Properties"},"529":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#theming","content":"Theming"},"530":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart","content":"A donut chart shows a whole split into parts: a ring of `segments` that draw in one by one, with a\nlegend beside it. Each segment takes a `label` and a `value`, and gets a colour from the chart\npalette unless you pass one. The middle shows the total with its `label` and `unit`; hovering a\nsegment or its legend row highlights both and shows that one in the middle instead."},"531":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                  | Description                                           |\n| ---------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `segments` | `DonutChartSegment[]` | The ring's parts. Each is `{ label, value, color? }`. |","table":"table-0"},"532":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                            |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | Under the total in the middle, like \"Agent time\". Defaults to `Total`. |","table":"table-0"},"533":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                             |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `unit` | `string` | After every value, like `h` in \"14.2h\". |","table":"table-0"},"534":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                    | Description                                           |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `(n: number) => string` | Writes a value. Defaults to one decimal, like `14.2`. |","table":"table-0"},"535":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type             | Description                                                                             |\n| -------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `active` | `number \\| null` | Index of the highlighted segment, or `null`. Leave it out to let hovering highlight it. |","table":"table-0"},"536":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"| Name            | Type             | Description                                    |\n| --------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultActive` | `number \\| null` | The highlight to start with when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"537":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"| Name             | Type                              | Description                                                                                      |\n| ---------------- | --------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onActiveChange` | `(index: number \\| null) => void` | Fires when the highlighted segment changes (Angular: `activeChange`; Flutter: `onActiveChange`). |","table":"table-0"},"538":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#properties","content":"A `DonutChartSegment` is `{ label: string; value: number; color?: string }`; `color` defaults to the\nchart palette (`--vo-c1..c6`) in order."},"539":{"id":"/docs/components/donut-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/donut-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/donut-chart#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Segment\ncolours come from the chart palette tokens (`--vo-c1..c6`), the card sits on a surface, and the\nlegend hover tint and the centre text read from the theme tokens. The arcs sweep in and the total\ncounts up on load; with `prefers-reduced-motion` the ring appears already drawn."},"540":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","type":"page","content":"Draft review","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/draft-review"},"541":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-0","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review","content":"An email the agent drafted, to check and edit before it sends."},"542":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-1","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/draft-review#usage","content":"Usage"},"543":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-2","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"Properties"},"544":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-3","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/draft-review#theming","content":"Theming"},"545":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-4","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review","content":"An email the agent drafted, laid out like the email it is: who it goes to, the `subject`, the `body`\nand any `attachments`. Check and edit it, then send now or later — the menu beside the button picks\n`when` — or `discard` it. A `warning` can stop it before it sends, like an attachment the message\nmentions but nothing attached, and after sending there is a short window to `undo`. The `phase` drives\nwhat the footer shows."},"546":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-5","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                              |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The bold first line. Defaults to \"Draft from the agent\". |","table":"table-0"},"547":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-6","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                       |\n| ---------- | -------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The quieter line under the title. |","table":"table-0"},"548":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-7","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name | Type               | Description                                    |\n| ---- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `to` | `DraftRecipient[]` | Who it goes to: `{ name; initials?; color? }`. |","table":"table-0"},"549":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-8","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                               |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subject` | `string` | The subject line. Editable when `onSubjectChange` is set. |","table":"table-0"},"550":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-9","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                        |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `body` | `string` | The message as the agent wrote it. Stays editable; read edits from `onBodyChange`. |","table":"table-0"},"551":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-10","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name          | Type                | Description                                      |\n| ------------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `attachments` | `DraftAttachment[]` | Files on the draft: `{ name; size?; loading? }`. |","table":"table-0"},"552":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-11","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                | Description                                                |\n| --------- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `warning` | `{ text; actions }` | A problem to settle before it sends, with its own buttons. |","table":"table-0"},"553":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-12","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                                         | Description                   |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `phase` | `draft \\| sending \\| undo \\| sent \\| scheduled \\| discarded` | Drives what the footer shows. |","table":"table-0"},"554":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-13","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name          | Type           | Description                                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `sendOptions` | `SendOption[]` | The \"when to send\" menu: `{ key; label; detail? }`. `now` sends straight away. |","table":"table-0"},"555":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-14","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name                               | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ---------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendOption` / `defaultSendOption` | `string` | The picked option's key, controlled or uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"556":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-15","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                            |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `undoLeft` | `number` | Seconds left to undo, shown while the phase is `undo`. |","table":"table-0"},"557":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-16","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name     | Type               | Description                                                        |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSend` | `(option) => void` | Called when Send (or Schedule) is pressed, with the chosen option. |","table":"table-0"},"558":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-17","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name        | Type         | Description                   |\n| ----------- | ------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `onDiscard` | `() => void` | Called by the Discard button. |","table":"table-0"},"559":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-18","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#properties","content":"| Name     | Type         | Description                                                                              |\n| -------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onUndo` | `() => void` | Takes it back: undoes a send, cancels a scheduled one, or brings back a discarded draft. |","table":"table-0"},"560":{"id":"/docs/components/draft-review-19","page_id":"/docs/components/draft-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/draft-review#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the card shadow; the warning uses the warn tint, a sent draft the ok tint, and\na scheduled one the blue \"preview\" tint — all from the theme tokens. In Soft the card, chips and pills\nare rounder."},"561":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","type":"page","content":"Error recovery","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/error-recovery"},"562":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-0","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery","content":"A failed step with retry, skip or hand over to a person."},"563":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-1","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#usage","content":"Usage"},"564":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-2","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"Properties"},"565":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-3","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#theming","content":"Theming"},"566":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-4","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery","content":"A run that hit an error, with the steps around it and a choice of how the agent should carry on.\nEach `step` carries a `state` — `done`, `fail`, `run`, `wait`, `skip` or `hand` — that picks its\nglyph, and an optional `note` under it that crossfades when it changes. The `options` are the ways\nthe agent can continue; pick one and press Continue, and the choices fold away."},"567":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-5","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | What the agent was doing, like \"Sync the pipeline to Sheets\". |","table":"table-0"},"568":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-6","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | Where the run stands, like \"Stopped at step 2\". Crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"569":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-7","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                                                                         |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `RecoveryStep[]` | The steps around the failure. Each has a `label`, a `state` and an optional `note`. |","table":"table-0"},"570":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-8","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                                          | Description                                                                                         |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `step.state` | `done \\| fail \\| run \\| wait \\| skip \\| hand` | Picks the glyph: a check, a red alert, a spinner, a quiet dot, a struck-through skip or a hand-off. |","table":"table-0"},"571":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-9","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `step.note` | `string` | The quiet line under the step, like \"Done in 8s\" or the error. Crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"572":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-10","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                                   |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `question` | `string` | The question above the choices. Defaults to \"How should the agent continue?\". |","table":"table-0"},"573":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-11","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name      | Type               | Description                                                 |\n| --------- | ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `options` | `RecoveryOption[]` | The ways the agent can carry on, each a `{ value, label }`. |","table":"table-0"},"574":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-12","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type     | Description                                                                  |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `defaultValue` | `string` | The chosen option, controlled or uncontrolled. Defaults to the first option. |","table":"table-0"},"575":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-13","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                               |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(value) => void` | Called when a different choice is picked. |","table":"table-0"},"576":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-14","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name         | Type              | Description                                             |\n| ------------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onContinue` | `(value) => void` | Called with the chosen option when Continue is pressed. |","table":"table-0"},"577":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-15","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                              |\n| --------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `continueLabel` | `string` | The label on the confirm button. Defaults to \"Continue\". |","table":"table-0"},"578":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-16","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether the choices show. Leave it out and they fold away once Continue is pressed. |","table":"table-0"},"579":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-17","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                                  |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open) => void` | Called when the choices fold open or closed. |","table":"table-0"},"580":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-18","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"581":{"id":"/docs/components/error-recovery-19","page_id":"/docs/components/error-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/error-recovery#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The step\nglyphs take their colour from the theme tokens — a green check, a red alert, a plum hand-off — and\nthe rail between steps, the selected choice and the Continue pill all draw from the same tokens, so\nthe whole block reads against either background; in Soft the choices and the pill are rounder."},"582":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","type":"page","content":"Eval results","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/eval-results"},"583":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-0","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results","content":"An eval run case by case, against the run before."},"584":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-1","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/eval-results#usage","content":"Usage"},"585":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-2","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"Properties"},"586":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-3","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/eval-results#theming","content":"Theming"},"587":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-4","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results","content":"An eval suite's latest run: one bar segment per case, the pass count against the run before, and\nthe cases — all of them, or only the failed ones. The `Run evals` button spins while the suite runs\nand the count reads `Running 3 of 8`. A failed case opens to show what was `expected` and what it\n`got`, with a `fix` button that reruns just that case."},"588":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-5","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                  |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The suite's name, like \"Pricing copy evals\". |","table":"table-0"},"589":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-6","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                                                     |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The line under the title, like \"Copy agent · 8 cases · run 2h ago\". Crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"590":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-7","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name    | Type         | Description                                                                                           |\n| ------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cases` | `EvalCase[]` | One per case: `id`, `name`, `status`, and (for a failure) `time`, `expected`, `got`, `source`, `fix`. |","table":"table-0"},"591":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-8","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name    | Type         | Description          |\n| ------- | ------------ | -------------------- |\n| `onRun` | `() => void` | Adds the run button. |","table":"table-0"},"592":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-9","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                                                |\n| --------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `running` | `boolean` | Whether the whole suite is running: the button spins and the count reads \"Running 3 of 8\". |","table":"table-0"},"593":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-10","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                      |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `runLabel` | `string` | The run button's label. Defaults to \"Run evals\". |","table":"table-0"},"594":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-11","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                                                   |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `previousPassed` | `number` | How many passed the run before. Once the run settles, a tag compares with it. |","table":"table-0"},"595":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-12","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type          | Description                                             |\n| -------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `filter` / `defaultFilter` | `all \\| fail` | Which cases show: all of them, or only the failed ones. |","table":"table-0"},"596":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-13","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type       | Description                                                                      |\n| ---------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `string[]` | Ids of the failed cases that are open. Leave it out to let each one open itself. |","table":"table-0"},"597":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-14","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| `EvalCase` | Type                                | Description                                       |\n| ---------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status`   | `queued \\| running \\| pass \\| fail` | How the case did; picks its glyph and bar colour. |","table":"table-1"},"598":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-15","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| `EvalCase` | Type     | Description                                                |\n| ---------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `time`     | `string` | How long it took, like \"0.9s\", shown once it has a result. |","table":"table-1"},"599":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-16","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| `EvalCase`                    | Type     | Description                                                                               |\n| ----------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `expected` / `got` / `source` | `string` | For a failed case: what should have come back, what did, and where the answer comes from. |","table":"table-1"},"600":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-17","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#properties","content":"| `EvalCase` | Type                 | Description                                                             |\n| ---------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fix`      | `{ label; onClick }` | A white button under a failed case's details, like \"Use $24 and rerun\". |","table":"table-1"},"601":{"id":"/docs/components/eval-results-18","page_id":"/docs/components/eval-results","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/eval-results#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface with the card shadow; pass and fail take the `--vo-ok` and `--vo-bad` tokens for\ntheir glyphs and bar segments, and a failed case tints with `--vo-bad-bg`, so it all reads against\nthe stage. In Soft the panel, pills and segmented control are rounder."},"602":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","type":"page","content":"Feedback sheet","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet"},"603":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-0","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","content":"Rate an answer and tell the agent what missed."},"604":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-1","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#usage","content":"Usage"},"605":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-2","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"Properties"},"606":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-3","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#theming","content":"Theming"},"607":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-4","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","content":"A feedback sheet sits under an answer in a chat thread. The thumbs rate it; a thumbs down\nopens a sheet with quick `reasons` and a free-text box so the person can say what missed.\nSend shows a spinner, then the sheet folds away and a thank-you line lands. A thumbs up just\nnotes it. It is `bare` by default so it reads flat under a message; set it to `false` for a\ncard of its own."},"608":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-5","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type                   | Description                                     |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `children` / `message` | `ReactNode` / `string` | The answer being rated, shown above the thumbs. |","table":"table-0"},"609":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-6","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                     | Description                                                                      |\n| -------- | ------------------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `rating` | `'up' \\| 'down' \\| null` | Whether the answer was rated good or bad. Leave it out to let the thumbs set it. |","table":"table-0"},"610":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-7","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                    |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `onRatingChange` | `(rating) => void` | Called when the thumbs change. |","table":"table-0"},"611":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-8","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                               |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the reasons sheet is open. Leave it out and thumbs down opens it. |","table":"table-0"},"612":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-9","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name       | Type       | Description                                                |\n| ---------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `selected` | `string[]` | The reasons picked. Leave it out to let the chips keep it. |","table":"table-0"},"613":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-10","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `comment` | `string` | What is written in the box. Leave it out to let the box keep it. |","table":"table-0"},"614":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-11","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ---------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `question` | `string` | The heading of the sheet that opens on thumbs down. |","table":"table-0"},"615":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-12","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name      | Type       | Description                 |\n| --------- | ---------- | --------------------------- |\n| `reasons` | `string[]` | Quick reasons to pick from. |","table":"table-0"},"616":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-13","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description          |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | The box placeholder. |","table":"table-0"},"617":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-14","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `note` | `string` | A quiet note beside the buttons, like who sees the feedback. |","table":"table-0"},"618":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-15","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                     |\n| --------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `sending` | `boolean` | Shows the spinner on Send, for a scripted demo. |","table":"table-0"},"619":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-16","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name   | Type               | Description                                                                   |\n| ------ | ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sent` | `Feedback \\| null` | What was sent, which shows the thank-you line. Leave it out and Send sets it. |","table":"table-0"},"620":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-17","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                                  | Description                                                                                        |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSubmit` | `(feedback) => void \\| Promise<void>` | Called with what the person picked and wrote. Return a promise to show a spinner until it settles. |","table":"table-0"},"621":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-18","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat under a message in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"622":{"id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet-19","page_id":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/feedback-sheet#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nactive bad thumb and the thank-you line take their tints from the `--vo-bad` and `--vo-ok` tokens,\nthe selected chips from the accent, and the box line from the field tokens, so the sheet reads\nagainst the stage; in Soft the chips, box and buttons are rounder."},"623":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","type":"page","content":"Field extraction","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-extraction"},"624":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-0","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction","content":"The agent pulls fields out of a document and shows where each came from."},"625":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-1","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#usage","content":"Usage"},"626":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-2","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"Properties"},"627":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-3","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#theming","content":"Theming"},"628":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-4","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction","content":"The agent reads a document on the left and lists the fields it found on the right, each with\nhow sure it is. A new field slides in and its source region on the page lights up for a moment,\nso you can see where each value came from. A field the agent is unsure of (`confidence` under\n`0.6`) asks the person to check it — they type the value into the field itself and confirm with\nEnter or by clicking away. The Send button waits until every field is sure or checked."},"629":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-5","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#usage","content":"Wrap the parts of the page a field comes from in a zone, and tie each field to its zone with a\nmatching `key`/`field`. The zone lights up while its field is read, hovered or checked."},"630":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-6","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                                                           |\n| ------ | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `page` | `ReactNode` | The page being read, on the left. Wrap the parts the fields come from in `FieldZone`. |","table":"table-0"},"631":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-7","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name     | Type               | Description                                                                                    |\n| -------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fields` | `ExtractedField[]` | The fields found so far, in order. Each new one slides in and its zone lights up for a moment. |","table":"table-0"},"632":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-8","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                                                  |\n| --------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `reading` | `boolean` | A scan line passes down the page each time this turns true, and Send waits while it is true. |","table":"table-0"},"633":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-9","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                     |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The quiet line by the title, like \"Reading page 1\". Crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"634":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-10","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `checkHint` | `string` | Replaces the status while a field is being checked. |","table":"table-0"},"635":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-11","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                   | Description                                                              |\n| ------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onFix` | `(key, value) => void` | Called when a checked field is confirmed with Enter or by clicking away. |","table":"table-0"},"636":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-12","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The heading over the field list. Defaults to \"Extracted fields\". |","table":"table-0"},"637":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-13","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| ----------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sendLabel` | `string` | The button under the fields. It waits until every field is sure or checked. |","table":"table-0"},"638":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-14","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                      | Description                                                                    |\n| ----------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `sendState` | `idle \\| sending \\| sent` | `idle` shows `sendLabel`, `sending` a spinner, `sent` a check and `sentLabel`. |","table":"table-0"},"639":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-15","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                               |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `sentLabel` | `string` | The label once the fields have been sent. |","table":"table-0"},"640":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-16","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name     | Type         | Description                                            |\n| -------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSend` | `() => void` | Called when Send is pressed while every field is sure. |","table":"table-0"},"641":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-17","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name                 | Type     | Description                                         |\n| -------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ExtractedField.key` | `string` | Ties the field to the `FieldZone` it was read from. |","table":"table-0"},"642":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-18","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name                        | Type     | Description                                                |\n| --------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ExtractedField.confidence` | `number` | 0 to 1. Under `0.6` the field asks the person to check it. |","table":"table-0"},"643":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-19","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name                        | Type     | Description                                         |\n| --------------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ExtractedField.suggestion` | `string` | What the value starts as when the person checks it. |","table":"table-0"},"644":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-20","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                               |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ExtractedField.fixed` | `boolean` | The person has checked it. Shows \"Fixed\" with a full bar. |","table":"table-0"},"645":{"id":"/docs/components/field-extraction-21","page_id":"/docs/components/field-extraction","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/field-extraction#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npage is drawn as paper — white ink-on-paper in light mode, a dark document in dark mode — while\nthe rest of the component follows the theme tokens. A highlighted source region tints and rings\nwith the accent, and an unsure one with the warning tint, so each keeps its contrast against the\nink; in Soft the document, panel and buttons are rounder."},"646":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","type":"page","content":"Funnel chart","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart"},"647":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","content":"Signup to paid, with the biggest drop called out by the agent."},"648":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#usage","content":"Usage"},"649":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"Properties"},"650":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#theming","content":"Theming"},"651":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","content":"A funnel chart shows how many people reach each `stage` in order. Each bar grows in a moment\nafter the chart appears, the stage that loses the largest share of the one before it is marked\nin red, and the agent's `insight` sits below. With more than one `view`, a segment switch redraws\nthe bars top to bottom and crossfades the note."},"652":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description            |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Like \"Signup to paid\". |","table":"table-0"},"653":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type       | Description                                                 |\n| -------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stages` | `string[]` | The stages in order, like \"Signed up\" then \"Opened a file\". |","table":"table-0"},"654":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                | Description                                                                   |\n| ------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `views` | `FunnelChartView[]` | One set of numbers per view. With more than one, a switch picks between them. |","table":"table-0"},"655":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `view` | `string` | Key of the view shown. Leave it out to let the switch change it. |","table":"table-0"},"656":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                 |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `defaultView` | `string` | Defaults to the first view. |","table":"table-0"},"657":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name           | Type            | Description                          |\n| -------------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onViewChange` | `(key) => void` | Called when the switch picks a view. |","table":"table-0"},"658":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `shareLabel` | `string` | Ends a stage's tip, like \"of signups\" in \"51.8% of signups\". |","table":"table-0"},"659":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `startLabel` | `string` | The first stage's tip. Defaults to \"Starting point\". |","table":"table-0"},"660":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type            | Description                                            |\n| -------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `format` | `(n) => string` | Writes a count. Defaults to whole numbers like 12,400. |","table":"table-0"},"661":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description          |\n| ---------- | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `view.key` | `string` | Identifies the view. |","table":"table-0"},"662":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                  |\n| ------------ | -------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `view.label` | `string` | On the switch, like \"Teams\". |","table":"table-0"},"663":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name          | Type       | Description                            |\n| ------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `view.values` | `number[]` | How many reached each stage, in order. |","table":"table-0"},"664":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                      |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `view.insight` | `string` | The agent's note under the funnel for this view. |","table":"table-0"},"665":{"id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/funnel-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/funnel-chart#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface and the bars run from the first chart colour (`--vo-c1`, the accent) down to the\nnext (`--vo-c2`), so each stage reads a shade apart; the biggest drop uses the bad tone and the\nagent's note tints with the accent — all from the theme tokens. In the default style the bars carry\na light accent edge on the track; in Soft they are flat fills."},"666":{"id":"/docs/components/grid","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","type":"page","content":"Grid","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/grid"},"667":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-0","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid","content":"A responsive grid you drop cards or any other components into — a fixed column count or an auto-fit pack, with a gutter and per-child column spans."},"668":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-1","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/grid#usage","content":"Usage"},"669":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-2","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/grid#properties","content":"Properties"},"670":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-3","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/grid#theming","content":"Theming"},"671":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-4","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid","content":"A grid is a layout primitive for arranging cards or any other components. Give it a fixed column\ncount with `cols`, or set `fit` to pack as many columns as fit at a minimum width (`min`) so it\nreflows on its own with no breakpoints. `gap` sets the gutter. A child spans more than one column\nwith `span` (`2`, `3`, `4`) or the full row with `span=\"full\"`. The grid is its own container, so it\ncollapses to one column when it gets narrow — whatever the page around it does."},"672":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-5","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cols` | `number` | A fixed column count. Ignored when `fit` is set. `3` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"673":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-6","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid#properties","content":"| Name  | Type      | Description                                                                 |\n| ----- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `fit` | `boolean` | Pack as many columns as fit at `min` width, reflowing with no column count. |","table":"table-0"},"674":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-7","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid#properties","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ----- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `min` | `string` | Minimum column width when `fit` is set. `200px` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"675":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-8","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid#properties","content":"| Name  | Type            | Description                                                          |\n| ----- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `gap` | `1–8 \\| string` | The gutter: a core spacing step or a raw CSS length. `4` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"676":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-9","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid#properties","content":"| Name                | Type                  | Description                                              |\n| ------------------- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `span` (on a child) | `2 \\| 3 \\| 4 \\| full` | Make a child span more than one column, or the full row. |","table":"table-0"},"677":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-10","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid#properties","content":"In React and Flutter a spanning child is wrapped in `GridItem` / `VoGridItem`; in Angular it carries\nthe `gridItem` directive."},"678":{"id":"/docs/components/grid-11","page_id":"/docs/components/grid","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/grid#theming","content":"The grid is pure layout — it adds no color, shadow or border of its own, so the children it holds\n(cards, charts, tables) carry the look. Spacing flows through the shared `--vo-s-*` tokens. It works\nunchanged in light and dark and in both the Soft and Blueprint styles."},"679":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","type":"page","content":"Health score","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/health-score"},"680":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-0","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score","content":"A design system score made of a few checks you can open."},"681":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-1","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/health-score#usage","content":"Usage"},"682":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-2","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"Properties"},"683":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-3","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/health-score#theming","content":"Theming"},"684":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-4","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score","content":"One score for a design system, with the checks behind it. A half-gauge shows the overall score\n(green from 90, the accent from 80, red below). Point at a check — or tab to it — and the gauge\nswings to that check's score and names it; leave the list and it swings back. Open a check to see\nwhy, and, when it is `fixable` and you pass `onFix`, fix it from there: the button spins until your\npromise settles, then you update the check's `score` and `detail`."},"685":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-5","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                 | Description                  |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `checks` | `HealthScoreCheck[]` | The checks behind the score. |","table":"table-0"},"686":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-6","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                             |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Beside the gauge. Defaults to `\"Design system health\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"687":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-7","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                             |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `score` | `number` | The gauge score. Defaults to the average of the checks. |","table":"table-0"},"688":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-8","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                         |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to a line built from the checks. |","table":"table-0"},"689":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-9","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                                                                    |\n| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `open` | `string[]` | The open checks, by key (controlled). Leave out to let each row toggle itself. |","table":"table-0"},"690":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-10","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name          | Type       | Description                              |\n| ------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultOpen` | `string[]` | The checks open at first (uncontrolled). |","table":"table-0"},"691":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-11","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                       | Description                                 |\n| -------------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open: string[]) => void` | Called when the set of open checks changes. |","table":"table-0"},"692":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-12","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                | Description                                                                                                     |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onFix` | `(check, index) => void \\| Promise` | A check's Fix button. Return a promise and it spins until it settles; then update the check's score and detail. |","table":"table-0"},"693":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-13","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                  |\n| ----------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `check.key` | `string` | Identifies the check. Defaults to its label. |","table":"table-0"},"694":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-14","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------- |\n| `check.label` | `string` | Like \"Contrast\". |","table":"table-0"},"695":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-15","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `check.score` | `number` | 0 to 100. From 90 green, from 80 the accent, below that red. |","table":"table-0"},"696":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-16","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                               |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `check.detail` | `string` | One line under the check when it is open. |","table":"table-0"},"697":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-17","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#properties","content":"| Name            | Type      | Description                                          |\n| --------------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `check.fixable` | `boolean` | Adds a Fix button to the open check (needs `onFix`). |","table":"table-0"},"698":{"id":"/docs/components/health-score-18","page_id":"/docs/components/health-score","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/health-score#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card,\nrows, bars and gauge track all come from the theme tokens; the gauge fill follows the score (its green\nand red are the component's own `--vo-hs-ok` / `--vo-hs-bad`, the accent in between), and an open or\nhovered row picks up the row tint. In Soft the card and the Fix pill are rounder."},"699":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","type":"page","content":"Human handoff","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/human-handoff"},"700":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-0","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff","content":"The agent hands a conversation to a person, with what they need to pick it up."},"701":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-1","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#usage","content":"Usage"},"702":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-2","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"Properties"},"703":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-3","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#theming","content":"Theming"},"704":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-4","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff","content":"The agent passes a conversation to a person: why it handed off (`reason`), who has it (`assignee`,\nwith a `people` list for **Reassign**), when the reply is due (`secondsLeft` counts down and the bar\nempties, turning orange under five minutes), the `summary` and `facts` they need to pick it up, and\nthe `message` the customer was told (editable in place when you pass `onMessageChange`). A `status`\nrow at the foot says where it stands — neutral while it waits, amber when the person can't take it,\ngreen once they have."},"705":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-5","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `reason` | `string` | Why the agent handed off, like \"Refund over $500 needs a person\". |","table":"table-0"},"706":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-6","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                    | Description                                                     |\n| ---------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `assignee` | `HandoffPerson \\| null` | Who has it, or `null` while the agent is still finding someone. |","table":"table-0"},"707":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-7","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                 | Description                                     |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `finding` | `{ title; detail? }` | The two lines shown while `assignee` is `null`. |","table":"table-0"},"708":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-8","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name     | Type              | Description                                                         |\n| -------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `people` | `HandoffPerson[]` | The people it can go to instead. Leave it out to hide **Reassign**. |","table":"table-0"},"709":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-9","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name         | Type               | Description                                  |\n| ------------ | ------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onReassign` | `(person) => void` | Called when a row is picked in **Reassign**. |","table":"table-0"},"710":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-10","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                                             |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `secondsLeft` | `number` | Seconds until the reply is due. Whole minutes; orange under five; overdue at 0 or less. |","table":"table-0"},"711":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-11","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                                    |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `targetSeconds` | `number` | The whole window, for the bar and the \"15 min target\" line. Defaults to `900`. |","table":"table-0"},"712":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-12","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                          |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `summary` | `string` | What the person needs to pick it up. |","table":"table-0"},"713":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-13","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                 | Description                               |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `facts` | `{ label; value }[]` | A few key facts, as label and value rows. |","table":"table-0"},"714":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-14","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name   | Type                               | Description                       |\n| ------ | ---------------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `link` | `{ label; href?; onClick?; tip? }` | A link to the whole conversation. |","table":"table-0"},"715":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-15","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                       |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `message` | `string` | What the agent told the customer. |","table":"table-0"},"716":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-16","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                      |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `messageLabel` | `string` | The label over the message, like \"Sent to Dana\". |","table":"table-0"},"717":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-17","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name              | Type             | Description                                                                           |\n| ----------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onMessageChange` | `(text) => void` | Adds **Edit**: the message turns editable, and **Save** calls this with the new text. |","table":"table-0"},"718":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-18","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name     | Type      | Description                           |\n| -------- | --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `edited` | `boolean` | Adds \"· edited\" to the message label. |","table":"table-0"},"719":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-19","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"| Name     | Type            | Description                                                                               |\n| -------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `HandoffStatus` | The foot row: `tone` (`wait \\| warn \\| ok`), `title`, `detail?` and an optional `person`. |","table":"table-0"},"720":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-20","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#properties","content":"`HandoffPerson` is `{ name; initials?; color?; team?; presence?; tone?: ok \\| warn }` — `name` is the\nkey, `tone` puts a green or orange dot before the presence."},"721":{"id":"/docs/components/human-handoff-21","page_id":"/docs/components/human-handoff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/human-handoff#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface; the countdown bar, the presence dot and the foot row take their colours from the\n`--vo-*` tokens — amber from the warn tokens under five minutes or when the person is out, green from\nthe ok tokens once they have it. The two columns stack when the card is narrow."},"722":{"id":"/docs/components/icon","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"page","content":"Icon","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon"},"723":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-0","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon","content":"A line icon by name — or your own SVG — that takes the text colour and themes for free."},"724":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-1","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon#usage","content":"Usage"},"725":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-2","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"Properties"},"726":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-3","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/icon#theming","content":"Theming"},"727":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-4","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon","content":"Draw an icon by its `name`, or pass your own `path` / SVG for a glyph the set does not have. Icons\nuse `currentColor`, so they take the colour of the surrounding text; `size` ranges from `xs` to `xl`."},"728":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-5","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                                                                 |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `name` | `string` | A canonical icon name (e.g. `chevron-right`, `circle-check`). Any of ~5,200 resolves. Optional when you pass `path` or SVG. |","table":"table-0"},"729":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-6","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"| Name   | Type                      | Description                                         |\n| ------ | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `size` | `xs \\| s \\| m \\| l \\| xl` | Rendered size: 12 · 14 · 16 (default) · 18 · 24 px. |","table":"table-0"},"730":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-7","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `path` | `string` | A custom SVG path (`d` of one `<path>`) drawn on the 24×24 grid. |","table":"table-0"},"731":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-8","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"| Name               | Type             | Description                                                                        |\n| ------------------ | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `svg` / `children` | `markup / nodes` | Custom SVG shapes for a glyph the set does not have. Takes precedence over `name`. |","table":"table-0"},"732":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-9","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                                                               |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | An accessible label. With it the icon is announced as an image; without it it is decorative (hidden from assistive tech). |","table":"table-0"},"733":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-10","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"| Name                              | Type          | Description                                                                     |\n| --------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `color` (Flutter) / `style` (web) | `Color / CSS` | Tint the icon. By default it inherits `currentColor` from the surrounding text. |","table":"table-0"},"734":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-11","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#properties","content":"Only the ~113 names the library itself uses are compiled into each bundle; every other name resolves\non demand on the web. On Angular and Flutter, names outside the compiled set are drawn by passing\n`path` or `svg`, so any of the ~5,200 icons — and your own — render everywhere."},"735":{"id":"/docs/components/icon-12","page_id":"/docs/components/icon","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/icon#theming","content":"An icon has no colour of its own: it strokes with `currentColor`, so it matches the text it sits in\nand switches with light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) automatically. Set a colour by styling the\nelement (web) or the `color` parameter (Flutter). The 24×24 grid, 1.75 stroke width and round caps\nare shared across all four frameworks, so the same glyph looks identical in each."},"736":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","type":"page","content":"Image generation","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image-generation"},"737":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-0","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation","content":"A prompt with styles, shape and count, pictures that resolve out of grain, and a gallery of earlier ones."},"738":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-1","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image-generation#usage","content":"Usage"},"739":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-2","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"Properties"},"740":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-3","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/image-generation#theming","content":"Theming"},"741":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-4","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation","content":"Image generation is a prompt with style chips, a shape and how many pictures, and an optional\nmodel; the pictures it makes resolve the way an image model works — Composing (a grid of dots in\nthe picture's colours grows out of grain), Adding detail (the blur lifts while a scan line sweeps\ndown and leaves the picture behind it) and Upscaling (the last softness and grain go). Every\npicture moves at its own speed, one can fail with Retry, and a finished one can be upscaled,\nvaried, downloaded, opened larger or used as a reference. Beside it sit a gallery of earlier\npictures, newest first, and a few style presets; narrower, they take the feed's place under a\nCreate / Gallery / Styles switch. `onGenerate` makes the pictures and reports how far each has come."},"742":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-5","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The project, shown after the section in the header. |","table":"table-0"},"743":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-6","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                         |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `section` | `string` | The first part of the header. Defaults to `Images`. |","table":"table-0"},"744":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-7","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type     | Description                                              |\n| -------------------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `prompt` / `defaultPrompt` | `string` | The prompt in the composer (controlled or uncontrolled). |","table":"table-0"},"745":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-8","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name     | Type       | Description                                                                        |\n| -------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `styles` | `string[]` | The style chips under the prompt. Defaults to Editorial, Poster, Surreal and 35mm. |","table":"table-0"},"746":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-9","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name                                       | Type       | Description            |\n| ------------------------------------------ | ---------- | ---------------------- |\n| `selectedStyles` / `defaultSelectedStyles` | `string[]` | The chips that are on. |","table":"table-0"},"747":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-10","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type                 | Description          |\n| ------------------------ | -------------------- | -------------------- |\n| `shape` / `defaultShape` | `1:1 \\| 3:4 \\| 16:9` | The picture's shape. |","table":"table-0"},"748":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-11","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type     | Description                               |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `count` / `defaultCount` | `number` | How many pictures Generate makes, 1 to 4. |","table":"table-0"},"749":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-12","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name     | Type           | Description                                                  |\n| -------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `models` | `ImageModel[]` | The models in the model menu. Leave it out to hide the menu. |","table":"table-0"},"750":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-13","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name      | Type               | Description                                                              |\n| --------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `gallery` | `GeneratedImage[]` | Earlier pictures, newest first. Pictures made here join them at the top. |","table":"table-0"},"751":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-14","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                 | Description                                       |\n| --------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `presets` | `ImageStylePreset[]` | The Styles tab. Picking one sets the style chips. |","table":"table-0"},"752":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-15","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                        | Description                                                                                                      |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onGenerate` | `(request, update) => void` | Makes the pictures: call `update(slot, …)` for each one as it goes. Also called for Retry and Vary with count 1. |","table":"table-0"},"753":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-16","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                      | Description                                                                                          |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onAction` | `(action, image) => void` | Called for each action on a picture (`upscale`, `download`, `reference`, `like`, `dislike`, `copy`). |","table":"table-0"},"754":{"id":"/docs/components/image-generation-17","page_id":"/docs/components/image-generation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/image-generation#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npanels sit on a surface with the card shadow; a picture's placeholder gradient and the scan line\nread against either theme. In Blueprint the dots are square cells and the picture shows through\nthem at half strength with a hard scan line in the accent's mark; in Soft the composer, chips and\ntiles are rounder. With reduced motion a picture fades in once it is done rather than resolving\nstep by step."},"755":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","type":"page","content":"Inline text diff","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff"},"756":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-0","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","content":"The agent's edits to a piece of copy, accepted or rejected one by one."},"757":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-1","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#usage","content":"Usage"},"758":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-2","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"Properties"},"759":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-3","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#theming","content":"Theming"},"760":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-4","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","content":"A piece of copy with the agent's edits marked inline — the old words struck, the suggestion added.\nEach edit opens a small toolbar to `accept` or `reject` it, and the header takes the rest all at\nonce. An edit the agent isn't sure of is tinted and shows a `note` above its buttons. Once every edit\nis decided, the buttons give way to a short `doneLabel`."},"761":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-5","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                             |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | What the copy is, like \"Pricing intro\". |","table":"table-0"},"762":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-6","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name    | Type         | Description                                                    |\n| ------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `parts` | `TextPart[]` | The copy in order: plain strings, with the edits between them. |","table":"table-0"},"763":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-7","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                           | Description                                                                                 |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `decisions` | `Record<string, EditDecision>` | Controlled map of what was decided for each edit, by key. Leave an edit out while it waits. |","table":"table-0"},"764":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-8","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name               | Type                           | Description                         |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |\n| `defaultDecisions` | `Record<string, EditDecision>` | The uncontrolled initial decisions. |","table":"table-0"},"765":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-9","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name                | Type                  | Description                                                     |\n| ------------------- | --------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDecisionsChange` | `(decisions) => void` | Called whenever the decisions change, with the full map by key. |","table":"table-0"},"766":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-10","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                    |\n| ----------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `doneLabel` | `string` | The line that replaces the buttons once every edit is decided. |","table":"table-0"},"767":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-11","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                                           | Description                      |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `labels` | `{ accept?; reject?; acceptAll?; rejectAll? }` | Overrides for the button labels. |","table":"table-0"},"768":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-12","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                               |\n| --------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `TextEdit.from` | `string` | The words the copy has now, shown struck. |","table":"table-0"},"769":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-13","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                           |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `TextEdit.to` | `string` | The words the agent suggests instead. |","table":"table-0"},"770":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-14","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                                                    |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `TextEdit.note` | `string` | Why the agent isn't sure of this one; the edit is marked and the note shows above its buttons. |","table":"table-0"},"771":{"id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff-15","page_id":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/inline-text-diff#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The struck\nand added words tint from the `--vo-del` and `--vo-add` tokens, an unsure edit uses the `--vo-warn`\ntokens, and the toolbar sits on a raised surface with the pop shadow — so it all reads against the\ndark stage; in Soft the card and its pills are rounder."},"772":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","type":"page","content":"Launch checklist","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist"},"773":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-0","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","content":"The agent checks a design before it ships, and fixes what fails."},"774":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-1","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#usage","content":"Usage"},"775":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-2","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"Properties"},"776":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-3","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#theming","content":"Theming"},"777":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-4","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","content":"A launch checklist runs the pre-flight checks before something ships. Each check is a row with a\nglyph — a waiting ring, a spinner while it runs, a pass or a fail — plus a `label` and a quiet\n`note`. A progress bar across the top carries one segment per check, tinted as each result lands.\nA failed check shows a **Fix** button; the `status` line defaults to a count, \"Checking\" while one\nruns, then what is left to fix or \"All clear, ready to ship\"."},"778":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-5","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The line above the checks, like \"Ready to ship pricing?\". |","table":"table-0"},"779":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-6","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name     | Type            | Description                                        |\n| -------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `checks` | `LaunchCheck[]` | The checks, one row and one progress segment each. |","table":"table-0"},"780":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-7","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                                         |\n| -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to a count, \"Checking\" while one runs, then what is left to fix. |","table":"table-0"},"781":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-8","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                                   | Description                                                                                       |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `action` | `{ label; icon?; accent?; disabled? }` | The button beside the title, like Run checks, Run again or Ship it. `accent` tints the ship step. |","table":"table-0"},"782":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-9","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                    |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"783":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-10","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `check.label` | `string` | What is checked, like \"Contrast meets AA\". |","table":"table-0"},"784":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-11","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name          | Type                       | Description                                         |\n| ------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `check.state` | `wait \\| run \\| ok \\| bad` | Not run yet, checking or fixing, passed, or failed. |","table":"table-0"},"785":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-12","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `check.note` | `string` | The quiet line under the label, or what is wrong. |","table":"table-0"},"786":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-13","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#properties","content":"| Name          | Type         | Description                                                                                                    |\n| ------------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `check.onFix` | `() => void` | React: shows a Fix button on a failed check. Angular uses `canFix` + `(fix)`; Flutter uses `canFix` + `onFix`. |","table":"table-0"},"787":{"id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist-14","page_id":"/docs/components/launch-checklist","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/launch-checklist#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nprogress segments and glyphs take their colour from the theme tokens — `--vo-ok` for a pass,\n`--vo-bad` for a fail, the accent mark while running — so results read the same on either\nbackground; in Soft the rows and buttons are rounder. The glyph crossfades in as each state lands,\nand the bar transition is skipped under `prefers-reduced-motion`."},"788":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","type":"page","content":"Line chart","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/line-chart"},"789":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart","content":"Two series over time with a hover readout and toggles."},"790":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/line-chart#usage","content":"Usage"},"791":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"Properties"},"792":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/line-chart#theming","content":"Theming"},"793":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart","content":"A line chart plots a few `series` over the same `points` in time. The first series is the main one —\na solid line with a soft fill — and the rest are dashed, to compare against. The lines draw in from\nthe left while the big number counts up; move the pointer over the chart for a readout that follows\nthe cursor, and use the legend to toggle a series off (one always stays on)."},"794":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | The name over the big number, like \"Active editors\". |","table":"table-0"},"795":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                | Description                                                                              |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `series` | `LineChartSeries[]` | The series to plot. The first is the main one (solid, with a fill); the rest are dashed. |","table":"table-0"},"796":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type       | Description                                                      |\n| -------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `points` | `string[]` | One name per point, shown in the hover readout, like the months. |","table":"table-0"},"797":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                                                    |\n| ------ | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `axis` | `string[]` | Labels spread along the bottom. Defaults to every other point. |","table":"table-0"},"798":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type               | Description                                                                                     |\n| ------- | ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `range` | `[number, number]` | The values at the bottom and top of the chart. Defaults to the data's range with a little room. |","table":"table-0"},"799":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `unit` | `string` | What the values count, like \"editors\" in \"1,620 editors\". |","table":"table-0"},"800":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `compareLabel` | `string` | Ends the readout's comparison of the first two series, like \"vs last year\". |","table":"table-0"},"801":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                    | Description                                           |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `(n: number) => string` | Writes a value. Defaults to whole numbers like 1,620. |","table":"table-0"},"802":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name                         | Type       | Description                                                                             |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `visible` / `defaultVisible` | `string[]` | Keys of the series shown. Leave out to let the legend toggle them; one always stays on. |","table":"table-0"},"803":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name              | Type                       | Description                             |\n| ----------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `onVisibleChange` | `(keys: string[]) => void` | Fires when the legend toggles a series. |","table":"table-0"},"804":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                    |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `series[].key` | `string` | Names the series in `visible`. |","table":"table-0"},"805":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                           |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `series[].label` | `string` | The legend's label, like \"This year\". |","table":"table-0"},"806":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name              | Type       | Description                        |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `series[].values` | `number[]` | One value per point, oldest first. |","table":"table-0"},"807":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                   |\n| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `series[].color` | `string` | Overrides the palette colour for that series. |","table":"table-0"},"808":{"id":"/docs/components/line-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/line-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/line-chart#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The first\nline and its fill use the accent; the rest take the chart palette (`--vo-c2`, `--vo-c3`, …). The grid\nlines, the pointer rule and the dark tooltip pill all come from the theme tokens, so the chart reads\non either background. In Flutter the lines are drawn with a `CustomPainter` and the draw-in and\ncount-up run on an `AnimationController`."},"809":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","type":"page","content":"Live answer","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/live-answer"},"810":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-0","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer","content":"Answers that stream in with numbered sources and next steps."},"811":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-1","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/live-answer#usage","content":"Usage"},"812":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-2","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"Properties"},"813":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-3","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/live-answer#theming","content":"Theming"},"814":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-4","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer","content":"A live answer is a question and the reply that streams in beneath it, word by word. A `[1]` after a\nword turns into a numbered citation you can hover or pin, which lights up its entry in the sources\nlist. Each turn moves through `waiting`, `thinking`, `answering` and `done`; once it is `done` it\ngains the copy, rate and retry actions, the sources toggle and — on the last turn — the suggested\n`followUps`. Picking a follow-up adds a new turn below, so the thread grows instead of being replaced."},"815":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-5","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name    | Type           | Description                                         |\n| ------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `turns` | `AnswerTurn[]` | The thread: a question and its answer, newest last. |","table":"table-0"},"816":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-6","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name        | Type       | Description                                                              |\n| ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `followUps` | `string[]` | Suggested next questions, shown under the last answer once it is `done`. |","table":"table-0"},"817":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-7","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                 | Description                        |\n| ------------ | -------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onFollowUp` | `(question) => void` | Called when a follow-up is picked. |","table":"table-0"},"818":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-8","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name      | Type              | Description                                                              |\n| --------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onRetry` | `(index) => void` | Adds a Try again button under each answer; called with the turn's index. |","table":"table-0"},"819":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-9","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                      | Description                                                     |\n| -------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRate` | `(index, rating) => void` | Called when an answer is rated `good`, `bad` or back to `null`. |","table":"table-0"},"820":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-10","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                    | Description                                                            |\n| -------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCopy` | `(index, text) => void` | Called after an answer is copied, with its text without the citations. |","table":"table-0"},"821":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-11","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name            | Type               | Description                                                      |\n| --------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSourceClick` | `(source) => void` | Called when a source in the list is clicked, besides pinning it. |","table":"table-0"},"822":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-12","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                                       | Description                                                                                                           |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `turn.state` | `waiting \\| thinking \\| answering \\| done` | `waiting` shows nothing, `thinking` the Thinking line, `answering` streams the text, `done` adds sources and actions. |","table":"table-0"},"823":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-13","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `turn.text` | `string` | The answer so far. `[1]` after a word cites source 1; a blank line starts a new paragraph. |","table":"table-0"},"824":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-14","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name            | Type       | Description                                                             |\n| --------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `turn.thoughts` | `string[]` | What the agent did before it answered, under a toggle that counts them. |","table":"table-0"},"825":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-15","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                                                                         |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `turn.sources` | `AnswerSource[]` | The sources, each with its number `n`, `title`, `detail`, badge `mark` and `color`. |","table":"table-0"},"826":{"id":"/docs/components/live-answer-16","page_id":"/docs/components/live-answer","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/live-answer#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nanswer text, the question bubble, the citation chips and the sources list all draw from the theme\ntokens, so an active citation and its source row share the one accent tint; in Soft the chips and\nfollow-up buttons are rounder."},"827":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","type":"page","content":"Metric insight","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metric-insight"},"828":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-0","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight","content":"A number, its trend, and the agent's read on why it moved."},"829":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-1","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#usage","content":"Usage"},"830":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-2","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"Properties"},"831":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-3","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#theming","content":"Theming"},"832":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-4","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight","content":"A metric with its trend line, a one-line read on why it moved, and a breakdown of what moved it.\nA range switch (`7d` / `30d` / `90d`) re-rolls the big number and the change tag and redraws the\nline in place; the pointer reads off the nearest point; a marker sits where a release happened; and\n**Why did it move?** opens a breakdown of the drivers behind the change. Set `explaining` while you\nfetch those drivers and the button shows the agent \"Looking into it\"."},"833":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-5","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                              |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | The metric's name, like \"Trial to paid\". |","table":"table-0"},"834":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-6","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name     | Type            | Description                   |\n| -------- | --------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `ranges` | `MetricRange[]` | The ranges to switch between. |","table":"table-0"},"835":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-7","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                        |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `range` | `string` | The range on show, by key. Leave it out to let the switch pick it. |","table":"table-0"},"836":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-8","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                            |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `defaultRange` | `string` | The range the switch starts on. Defaults to the first. |","table":"table-0"},"837":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-9","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name            | Type            | Description                   |\n| --------------- | --------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `onRangeChange` | `(key) => void` | Fires when the range changes. |","table":"table-0"},"838":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-10","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                | Description                                                                        |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `(value) => string` | Formats the large number and the hovered point. Defaults to one decimal and a `%`. |","table":"table-0"},"839":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-11","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                 | Description                                   |\n| -------------- | -------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `formatChange` | `(change) => string` | Formats the change. Defaults to `\"+8.1 pts\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"840":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-12","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name      | Type             | Description                                                                       |\n| --------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `drivers` | `MetricDriver[]` | What moved the number, under \"Why did it move?\". Leave it out to hide the button. |","table":"table-0"},"841":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-13","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name         | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `explaining` | `boolean` | Shows \"Looking into it\" and keeps the breakdown shut while you fetch the drivers. |","table":"table-0"},"842":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-14","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                              |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the breakdown is open. Leave it out to let the button toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"843":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-15","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name          | Type      | Description                                             |\n| ------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether the breakdown starts open. Defaults to `false`. |","table":"table-0"},"844":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-16","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                          |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open) => void` | Fires when the breakdown is toggled. |","table":"table-0"},"845":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-17","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name          | Type                                                                               | Description                                                                                                                                                |\n| ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `MetricRange` | `{ key; label; points: number[]; value; change; insight; marker?: { at; label } }` | One range: its switch label, its values (oldest first), the number and change, the one-line insight, and an optional chart marker (`at` is 0 to 1 across). |","table":"table-0"},"846":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-18","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                         | Description                                                      |\n| -------------- | ---------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `MetricDriver` | `{ label; percent; color? }` | One contributor to the change. `percent` is its share, 0 to 100. |","table":"table-0"},"847":{"id":"/docs/components/metric-insight-19","page_id":"/docs/components/metric-insight","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/metric-insight#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the panel shadow; the line, the area fill and the marker all take the accent\nmark, the change tag tints green or red from the theme's `ok`/`bad` tokens, and the driver bars take\ntheir own colours (or the accent), so the whole thing reads against the stage in either mode."},"848":{"id":"/docs/components/modal","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"page","content":"Modal","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal"},"849":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-0","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"A centred dialog over a dimmed backdrop, closed by the backdrop, a button or Escape, with focus and page scroll kept in check."},"850":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-1","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#usage","content":"Usage"},"851":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-2","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"Properties"},"852":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-3","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/modal#theming","content":"Theming"},"853":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-4","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal","content":"A modal is a centred dialog over a dimmed backdrop. It closes on the backdrop, its corner close\nbutton or Escape; while it is open the page scroll is locked and focus is held inside the panel,\nreturning to the trigger when it closes. Give it a `title` and optional `subtitle`, a body, and an\noptional `footer` row of buttons. `size` is `sm` (420px), `md` (560px, the default) or `lg` (820px)."},"854":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-5","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                     |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the modal is on screen. |","table":"table-0"},"855":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-6","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name      | Type         | Description                                         |\n| --------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onClose` | `() => void` | Called by the backdrop, the close button or Escape. |","table":"table-0"},"856":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-7","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                                                                   |\n| ------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `ReactNode` | The heading at the top. Leave it out for a bare panel (then set `ariaLabel`). |","table":"table-0"},"857":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-8","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name       | Type        | Description                     |\n| ---------- | ----------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `ReactNode` | A quieter line under the title. |","table":"table-0"},"858":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-9","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name     | Type        | Description                            |\n| -------- | ----------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `footer` | `ReactNode` | A row of buttons pinned to the bottom. |","table":"table-0"},"859":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-10","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name   | Type             | Description                                           |\n| ------ | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `size` | `sm \\| md \\| lg` | How wide the panel may grow. `md` (560px) by default. |","table":"table-0"},"860":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-11","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                                            |\n| ----------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hideClose` | `boolean` | Hide the corner close button (Escape and the backdrop still close it). |","table":"table-0"},"861":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-12","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                       |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `disableBackdropClose` | `boolean` | Keep the modal open when the backdrop is clicked. |","table":"table-0"},"862":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-13","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ariaLabel` | `string` | For screen readers when there is no visible `title`. |","table":"table-0"},"863":{"id":"/docs/components/modal-14","page_id":"/docs/components/modal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/modal#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nuses the active theme's raised surface, text and shadow tokens; the backdrop dims with the ink token.\nMotion is paused for readers who prefer reduced motion — the dialog simply appears instead of rising in."},"864":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","type":"page","content":"Model picker","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/model-picker"},"865":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-0","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker","content":"Pick a model by speed, quality and cost, and how hard it thinks."},"866":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-1","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/model-picker#usage","content":"Usage"},"867":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-2","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"Properties"},"868":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-3","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/model-picker#theming","content":"Theming"},"869":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-4","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker","content":"A trigger names the picked model and how hard it thinks, over the open list of\n`models`. Each shows its `speed`, `quality` and `cost` as five-step meters, with the\nreal numbers (`speedDetail`, `qualityDetail`, `costDetail`) on hover. The thinking\neffort sits under them as a small dropdown. A model that can't take the request can\nset a `status` of `checking` or `busy` and offer a way out through `suggestion` — a\nshort notice with its own buttons, the last one filled."},"870":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-5","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name     | Type            | Description                |\n| -------- | --------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `models` | `ModelOption[]` | The models to choose from. |","table":"table-0"},"871":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-6","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` | `string` | The picked model's id. Leave it out to let the list hold its own. |","table":"table-0"},"872":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-7","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                          |\n| -------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultValue` | `string` | The picked model's id to start on when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"873":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-8","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name            | Type           | Description                                                                 |\n| --------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(id) => void` | Called when a row is picked, busy or not, so you can check the model first. |","table":"table-0"},"874":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-9","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name      | Type               | Description                                                  |\n| --------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `efforts` | `ThinkingEffort[]` | The thinking efforts. Defaults to Off, Low, Medium and High. |","table":"table-0"},"875":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-10","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type     | Description                                           |\n| -------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `effort` / `defaultEffort` | `string` | The picked effort's label, controlled or to start on. |","table":"table-0"},"876":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-11","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                     |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| `onEffortChange` | `(effort) => void` | Called when the effort changes. |","table":"table-0"},"877":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-12","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                                      | Description                                                                        |\n| ------------ | ----------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `suggestion` | `{ text; actions: { label; onClick }[] }` | A way out when the picked model can't take the request. The last button is filled. |","table":"table-0"},"878":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-13","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `note` | `string` | The confirmation under the picker, shown with a green check. |","table":"table-0"},"879":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-14","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | The label beside the trigger. Defaults to \"Model for this chat\". |","table":"table-0"},"880":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-15","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                                                             |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether the list is open. Leave it out to let the trigger and Escape open and close it. |","table":"table-0"},"881":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-16","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                           |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open) => void` | Called when the list opens or closes. |","table":"table-0"},"882":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-17","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name                             | Type     | Description                                          |\n| -------------------------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ModelOption.speed/quality/cost` | `number` | Each from 1 to 5. For cost, 5 is the most expensive. |","table":"table-0"},"883":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-18","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#properties","content":"| Name                 | Type                        | Description                                                                              |\n| -------------------- | --------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ModelOption.status` | `ready \\| checking \\| busy` | `checking` spins beside the name; `busy` turns the row amber, both showing `statusText`. |","table":"table-0"},"884":{"id":"/docs/components/model-picker-19","page_id":"/docs/components/model-picker","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/model-picker#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style\n(`data-style=\"soft\"`). The trigger and panel sit on a surface with the card shadow;\neach model's tile takes its own `color` with a letter colour that reads on it, the\npicked row's filled meters take the accent, and a busy row and its notice take the\nwarn tint — all from the theme tokens, so it reads against the dark stage."},"885":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"page","content":"Number field","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field"},"886":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field","content":"Type a number or step it with minus and plus, with a unit, limits, and a word when a value is nudged to fit."},"887":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#usage","content":"Usage"},"888":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"Properties"},"889":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/number-field#theming","content":"Theming"},"890":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field","content":"Type a number, or step it with the minus and plus buttons (hold to repeat). Give it a `min`, `max`\nand `step`, an optional `unit`, and it clamps an out-of-range value and says so — \"Set to 100 (max)\"."},"891":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                          |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` | `number` | The current value (controlled). Leave out for an uncontrolled field. |","table":"table-0"},"892":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| -------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultValue` | `number` | The starting value when uncontrolled. Defaults to `min`, else 0. |","table":"table-0"},"893":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `min` / `max` | `number` | The limits. Out-of-range input is clamped, with a brief note. |","table":"table-0"},"894":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `step` | `number` | How much the buttons and the arrow keys change the value. 1 by default. |","table":"table-0"},"895":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                            |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `unit` | `string` | A unit shown after the number, like `px`, `%` or `GB`. |","table":"table-0"},"896":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description              |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------ |\n| `label` | `string` | A label above the field. |","table":"table-0"},"897":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                                  |\n| ------ | ---------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `size` | `sm \\| md` | `sm` is compact, `md` (the default) roomier. |","table":"table-0"},"898":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name       | Type      | Description                           |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `disabled` | `boolean` | Greys the field out and blocks input. |","table":"table-0"},"899":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-13","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type       | Description                                        |\n| -------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onChange` / `valueChange` | `callback` | Called with the clamped value whenever it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"900":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-14","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#properties","content":"Type freely, then it settles on blur or Enter; the up and down arrow keys step by `step`, and the\nminus/plus buttons repeat while held."},"901":{"id":"/docs/components/number-field-15","page_id":"/docs/components/number-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/number-field#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The field,\nits hairline and the steppers all draw from the shared `--vo-*` tokens; the number is set in the\ntabular-numerals face so digits don't jitter as they change."},"902":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","type":"page","content":"OTP field","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/otp-field"},"903":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-0","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field","content":"A one-time code, one box per digit, that auto-advances and fills from a paste."},"904":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-1","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/otp-field#usage","content":"Usage"},"905":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-2","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"Properties"},"906":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-3","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/otp-field#theming","content":"Theming"},"907":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-4","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field","content":"A one-time code as a row of single-character boxes. Typing auto-advances, Backspace steps back, the\narrows move between boxes, and pasting a full code fills them all at once. Set `status` to show the\ncode as verified or rejected."},"908":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-5","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                  |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `length` | `number` | How many boxes / characters. Six by default. |","table":"table-0"},"909":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-6","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                  |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` | `string` | The current code, up to `length` characters. |","table":"table-0"},"910":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-7","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"| Name                                     | Type       | Description                                                      |\n| ---------------------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onChange` / `valueChange` / `onChanged` | `callback` | Fires with the new value as the person types, pastes or deletes. |","table":"table-0"},"911":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-8","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type       | Description                                            |\n| ------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onComplete` / `complete` | `callback` | Fires once the last box is filled, with the full code. |","table":"table-0"},"912":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-9","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                                   |\n| --------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `numeric` | `boolean` | Only digits may be entered, and a paste keeps just its digits. On by default. |","table":"table-0"},"913":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-10","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                          | Description                                    |\n| -------- | ----------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `default \\| success \\| error` | Tints the boxes green or red and shows a mark. |","table":"table-0"},"914":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-11","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#properties","content":"| Name       | Type      | Description                           |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `disabled` | `boolean` | Greys the boxes out and blocks input. |","table":"table-0"},"915":{"id":"/docs/components/otp-field-12","page_id":"/docs/components/otp-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/otp-field#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Boxes use\nthe field tokens, the accent for focus, and the success/danger tokens for `status`; in Blueprint the\nboxes are squared off, in Soft they are rounded. The code is set in the monospace token."},"916":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","type":"page","content":"Permission gate","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/permission-gate"},"917":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-0","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate","content":"The agent asks before it touches something new."},"918":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-1","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#usage","content":"Usage"},"919":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-2","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"Properties"},"920":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-3","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#theming","content":"Theming"},"921":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-4","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate","content":"The agent asks before it acts: one card with the question, the `scopes` to tick, and a footer\nwith how long the grant lasts (`durations`) and the two answers. Once allowed it gives way to a\nshorter result row — a spinner while the agent is `working`, a green check when done — with a\nRevoke button; declining shows an undoable notice. A follow-up ask mid-run (`followUp`) turns the\nicon tile amber."},"922":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-5","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                                          |\n| ------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `ReactNode` | The question, like \"Allow the agent to edit Figma?\". |","table":"table-0"},"923":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-6","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name       | Type        | Description  |\n| ---------- | ----------- | ------------ |\n| `subtitle` | `ReactNode` | Why it asks. |","table":"table-0"},"924":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-7","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                                      |\n| ------ | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `ReactNode` | The glyph in the tile beside the question. Defaults to a shield. |","table":"table-0"},"925":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-8","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                | Description                                                         |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `scopes` | `PermissionScope[]` | The things to allow: `{ key, label, detail?, risk?, riskDetail? }`. |","table":"table-0"},"926":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-9","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type       | Description                                                                        |\n| ------------------------ | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `defaultValue` | `string[]` | Keys of the ticked scopes. Leave `value` out to let the checkboxes hold their own. |","table":"table-0"},"927":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-10","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name            | Type             | Description                          |\n| --------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onValueChange` | `(keys) => void` | Fires when the ticked scopes change. |","table":"table-0"},"928":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-11","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name        | Type       | Description                                                                             |\n| ----------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `durations` | `string[]` | How long the grant lasts, in the footer dropdown. Defaults to This task, Today, Always. |","table":"table-0"},"929":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-12","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name              | Type                     | Description                                     |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `durationDetails` | `Record<string, string>` | The quiet line under each duration in its menu. |","table":"table-0"},"930":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-13","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name                           | Type     | Description          |\n| ------------------------------ | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `duration` / `defaultDuration` | `string` | The picked duration. |","table":"table-0"},"931":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-14","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type                            | Description                                                      |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` / `defaultStatus` | `asking \\| allowed \\| declined` | Which view shows. Leave `status` out to let the buttons move it. |","table":"table-0"},"932":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-15","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                                  | Description                                                         |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onAllow` | `(keys, duration) => void \\| Promise` | Called on Allow; the button spins until a returned promise settles. |","table":"table-0"},"933":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-16","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name                                | Type         | Description                                     |\n| ----------------------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDecline` / `onRevoke` / `onUndo` | `() => void` | Called by the decline, Revoke and Undo buttons. |","table":"table-0"},"934":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-17","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name                             | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| -------------------------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `allowedTitle` / `allowedDetail` | `string` | The two lines on the allowed row, like \"Done. 6 frames edited\". |","table":"table-0"},"935":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-18","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                                        |\n| --------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `working` | `boolean` | The agent is still working: a spinner on a neutral row instead of the green check. |","table":"table-0"},"936":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-19","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                                            |\n| ------ | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `meta` | `ReactNode` | Quiet text at the end of the allowed row, like an elapsed time \"0:04\". |","table":"table-0"},"937":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-20","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name       | Type      | Description                                                             |\n| ---------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `followUp` | `boolean` | A follow-up ask mid-run, for one more scope: the icon tile turns amber. |","table":"table-0"},"938":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-21","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `declineLabel` | `string` | The decline button. Defaults to \"Not now\". |","table":"table-0"},"939":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-22","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name                               | Type        | Description            |\n| ---------------------------------- | ----------- | ---------------------- |\n| `declinedTitle` / `declinedDetail` | `ReactNode` | Shown after declining. |","table":"table-0"},"940":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-23","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"941":{"id":"/docs/components/permission-gate-24","page_id":"/docs/components/permission-gate","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/permission-gate#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The scopes,\nfooter and result row all draw from the shared `--vo-*` tokens: the ticked box and primary button take\nthe accent, the risk tag and the follow-up tile the warn tint, and the allowed row the ok tint; in Soft\nthe card, pills and tick boxes are rounder."},"942":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","type":"page","content":"Plan review","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/plan-review"},"943":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-0","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review","content":"A plan the agent proposes before it starts — edit a step, skip it, add one, then approve."},"944":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-1","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/plan-review#usage","content":"Usage"},"945":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-2","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"Properties"},"946":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-3","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/plan-review#theming","content":"Theming"},"947":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-4","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review","content":"The plan an agent posts before it starts work: each step is a line you can rewrite, skip (it stays,\nstruck through) or add to. The footer's **Approve plan** hands it off; from there the numbers turn\ninto a spinner, a check, or a retry clock, and a step can open a quiet line under it reporting what it\nfound or what it waits on. In `review` the steps are editable; in `running` the agent works through\nthem; in `done` the footer offers **See changes**."},"948":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-5","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                             |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Like \"Plan: redesign the pricing page\". |","table":"table-0"},"949":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-6","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type               | Description                                                                                            |\n| ------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `steps` | `PlanReviewStep[]` | The steps. Leave it out (with `defaultSteps`) to let the person edit, skip and add steps on their own. |","table":"table-0"},"950":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-7","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name           | Type               | Description                          |\n| -------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------ |\n| `defaultSteps` | `PlanReviewStep[]` | The initial steps when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"951":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-8","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                                          |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onStepsChange` | `(steps) => void` | Emitted whenever the list changes (edit, skip, add). |","table":"table-0"},"952":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-9","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                        | Description                                                                |\n| ------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `phase` | `review \\| running \\| done` | `review` (steps editable), `running` (agent works through them) or `done`. |","table":"table-0"},"953":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-10","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                                      |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `status` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to how many steps are left in and roughly how long they take. |","table":"table-0"},"954":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-11","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `note` | `string` | The quiet line in the footer. Defaults to a hint for each phase. |","table":"table-0"},"955":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-12","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                                       |\n| ------ | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `meta` | `ReactNode` | Quiet text at the end of the header, like an elapsed time \"0:04\". |","table":"table-0"},"956":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-13","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name        | Type         | Description                               |\n| ----------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `onApprove` | `() => void` | The **Approve plan** button, in `review`. |","table":"table-0"},"957":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-14","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name               | Type         | Description                                  |\n| ------------------ | ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRequestChanges` | `() => void` | The **Ask for changes** button, in `review`. |","table":"table-0"},"958":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-15","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name     | Type         | Description                        |\n| -------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onStop` | `() => void` | The **Stop** button, in `running`. |","table":"table-0"},"959":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-16","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name           | Type         | Description                            |\n| -------------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onSeeChanges` | `() => void` | The **See changes** button, in `done`. |","table":"table-0"},"960":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-17","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"961":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-18","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name           | Type      | Description                                                 |\n| -------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `step.skipped` | `boolean` | Left out of the plan; it stays in the list, struck through. |","table":"table-0"},"962":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-19","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name          | Type      | Description                      |\n| ------------- | --------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `step.edited` | `boolean` | Marks a step the person rewrote. |","table":"table-0"},"963":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-20","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                   | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------------ | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `step.state` | `run \\| retry \\| done` | `run` while the agent works on it, `retry` while it waits out a problem, `done` once it has. |","table":"table-0"},"964":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-21","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `step.detail` | `string` | The line the step reports under it. Opens and crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"965":{"id":"/docs/components/plan-review-22","page_id":"/docs/components/plan-review","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/plan-review#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). It sits\nflat in a chat thread by default; set `bare={false}` for a card of its own. The step numbers, the\nrunning tint, the amber retry and the green done mark all come from the theme tokens, so each state\nreads at a glance, and in Soft the rows and buttons are rounder."},"966":{"id":"/docs/components/progress","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","type":"page","content":"Progress","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress"},"967":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-0","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress","content":"A run's progress three ways — a ring for the whole run, segments for its steps and a bar for the step in hand — with controls and an optional meter that warns as it fills."},"968":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-1","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress#usage","content":"Usage"},"969":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-2","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"Properties"},"970":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-3","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/progress#theming","content":"Theming"},"971":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-4","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress","content":"Progress shows a long run three ways at once: a ring for the whole run, a segment per step, and a\nbar for how far the step in hand has got. The `state` colours it — grey while indeterminate or\npaused, the accent while running, red with a Retry on error, green when complete — and the controls\nfollow (Pause, Resume, Run again). An optional `meter` underneath warns in words as it fills."},"972":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-5","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                               |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The run's name, like \"Indexing the docs\". |","table":"table-0"},"973":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-6","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                                      | Description                                  |\n| ------- | --------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `state` | `indeterminate \\| running \\| paused \\| error \\| complete` | Colours the run and picks the control shown. |","table":"table-0"},"974":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-7","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                               |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `ProgressStep[]` | The steps, each `{ label, unit, total }`. |","table":"table-0"},"975":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-8","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                 |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `step` | `number` | The step in hand, from `0`. |","table":"table-0"},"976":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-9","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                   |\n| -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `stepProgress` | `number` | How far the step in hand has got, `0` to `1`. |","table":"table-0"},"977":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-10","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                             |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `valueText` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to \"Step 3 of 5, …\". |","table":"table-0"},"978":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-11","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `error` | `string` | What failed, shown over the bar while `state` is `error`. |","table":"table-0"},"979":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-12","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name                                             | Type       | Description                                |\n| ------------------------------------------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `onPause` / `onResume` / `onRetry` / `onRestart` | `callback` | The controls, wired to the matching state. |","table":"table-0"},"980":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-13","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"| Name    | Type            | Description                                                |\n| ------- | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `meter` | `ProgressMeter` | A meter under the run, with thresholds that warn in words. |","table":"table-0"},"981":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-14","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#properties","content":"A `ProgressMeter` is `{ label, value, max, unit?, warnAt?, dangerAt?, dangerLabel?, note? }`: it\nreads \"On track\" until `value / max` crosses `warnAt` (\"Running low\") and then `dangerAt` (the\n`dangerLabel`, or \"Almost out\")."},"982":{"id":"/docs/components/progress-15","page_id":"/docs/components/progress","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/progress#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the ring, segments and bar are squared off with hairline tracks; in Soft they are rounded\nwith a softer fill. The state colours and the meter's warn and danger bands come from the theme, so\nthey read correctly on either background."},"983":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","type":"page","content":"Prompt library","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-library"},"984":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-0","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library","content":"Saved prompts with blanks to fill in before they go to the agent."},"985":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-1","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#usage","content":"Usage"},"986":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-2","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"Properties"},"987":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-3","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#theming","content":"Theming"},"988":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-4","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library","content":"The studio's saved prompts, each with blanks written as `{key}`. Opening one lays its blanks out as\nfields — typed, or picked from a short list — and the prompt fills in as they change: filled blanks\ntake the accent colour, empty ones read by name. A prompt can't be used until every blank has a\nvalue; try it empty and each missing blank turns red and says what it needs."},"989":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-5","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name      | Type            | Description                |\n| --------- | --------------- | -------------------------- |\n| `prompts` | `SavedPrompt[]` | The saved prompts to list. |","table":"table-0"},"990":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-6","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The list's heading. Defaults to \"Prompt library\". |","table":"table-0"},"991":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-7","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The line under the title, like \"Shared with Visuno Studio\". |","table":"table-0"},"992":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-8","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name   | Type             | Description                                                                                   |\n| ------ | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `string \\| null` | The open prompt's id, or `null` for the list. Leave it out to let the component hold its own. |","table":"table-0"},"993":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-9","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name          | Type             | Description                                |\n| ------------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `defaultOpen` | `string \\| null` | The id to open at first when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"994":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-10","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                           | Description                                                 |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(id: string \\| null) => void` | Called when a prompt opens or the list comes back (`null`). |","table":"table-0"},"995":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-11","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                     | Description                                                                           |\n| -------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `values` | `Record<string, string>` | The open prompt's blanks, by key. A picked blank left out starts on its first option. |","table":"table-0"},"996":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-12","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                              |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `onValuesChange` | `(values) => void` | Called whenever a blank's value changes. |","table":"table-0"},"997":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-13","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                             | Description                                                 |\n| ------- | -------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onUse` | `(text, prompt, values) => void` | Called with the filled prompt once every blank has a value. |","table":"table-0"},"998":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-14","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name     | Type         | Description                            |\n| -------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onUndo` | `() => void` | Called when the used notice is undone. |","table":"table-0"},"999":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-15","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type     | Description                                     |\n| ---------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `SavedPrompt.template` | `string` | The prompt, with each blank written as `{key}`. |","table":"table-0"},"1000":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-16","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name                 | Type                          | Description                   |\n| -------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `SavedPrompt.blanks` | `Record<string, PromptBlank>` | The blanks, keyed by `{key}`. |","table":"table-0"},"1001":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-17","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name                | Type     | Description                                                                           |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PromptBlank.label` | `string` | The field's label. Lowercased, it also stands in the prompt while the blank is empty. |","table":"table-0"},"1002":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-18","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type     | Description                                     |\n| ------------------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `PromptBlank.placeholder` | `string` | For a typed blank: the hint in the empty field. |","table":"table-0"},"1003":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-19","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name                  | Type       | Description                                                              |\n| --------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `PromptBlank.options` | `string[]` | For a picked blank: the choices, in a dropdown that starts on the first. |","table":"table-0"},"1004":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-20","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#properties","content":"| Name                | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `PromptBlank.error` | `string` | What the field says when used empty. Defaults to \"Fill in the \\<label\\>\". |","table":"table-0"},"1005":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-library-21","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-library","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-library#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface, the prompt on a chip, and a filled blank takes the accent tint (`--vo-accent-bg`)\nwhile an empty one is outlined and a needed one turns `--vo-bad` — all from the theme tokens, so it\nreads in either mode; in Soft the card, fields and pills are rounder."},"1006":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","type":"page","content":"Prompt starters","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters"},"1007":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-0","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","content":"Suggested tasks that fill the composer in one click."},"1008":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-1","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#usage","content":"Usage"},"1009":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-2","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"Properties"},"1010":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-3","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#theming","content":"Theming"},"1011":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-4","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","content":"Prompt starters are suggested first prompts shown as cards, two to a row. Picking one writes its\nfull `prompt` into the field word by word and marks the card as picked; pressing Send emits the\nprompt and clears the field with a sent line. Pass `onShuffle` to add a Shuffle button and swap in\nanother set of `starters` — a new set staggers the cards in again."},"1012":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-5","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name       | Type        | Description                                                                  |\n| ---------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `starters` | `Starter[]` | The starters to show, two to a row. Pass a new set to stagger them in again. |","table":"table-0"},"1013":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-6","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                                                             |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` | `string \\| null` | The title of the picked starter. Leave it out to let the cards pick it. |","table":"table-0"},"1014":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-7","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                             |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultValue` | `string \\| null` | Initial picked title when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"1015":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-8","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name            | Type                              | Description                                                     |\n| --------------- | --------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(title: string \\| null) => void` | Called with the picked starter's title, or `null` when cleared. |","table":"table-0"},"1016":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-9","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                       | Description                                  |\n| -------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSend` | `(prompt: string) => void` | Called with the prompt when Send is pressed. |","table":"table-0"},"1017":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-10","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name        | Type         | Description                                                                         |\n| ----------- | ------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onShuffle` | `() => void` | Adds a Shuffle button under the field. Swap in another set of starters when called. |","table":"table-0"},"1018":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-11","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                            |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | The field's empty text. Defaults to `Pick a starter or type your own`. |","table":"table-0"},"1019":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-12","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                                  |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sentLabel` | `string` | Shown in the field once the prompt is sent. Defaults to `Sent to the agent`. |","table":"table-0"},"1020":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-13","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name           | Type       | Description      |\n| -------------- | ---------- | ---------------- |\n| `Starter.icon` | `IconName` | The card's icon. |","table":"table-0"},"1021":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-14","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                                                                 | Description       |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| `Starter.tone` | `blue \\| purple \\| green \\| orange \\| red \\| yellow \\| pink \\| teal` | Colours the icon. |","table":"table-0"},"1022":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-15","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                       |\n| --------------- | -------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `Starter.title` | `string` | A few words, like \"Audit a page\". |","table":"table-0"},"1023":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-16","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name                  | Type     | Description                     |\n| --------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `Starter.description` | `string` | One quiet line under the title. |","table":"table-0"},"1024":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-17","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                           |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `Starter.prompt` | `string` | The full prompt it writes into the field when picked. |","table":"table-0"},"1025":{"id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters-18","page_id":"/docs/components/prompt-starters","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/prompt-starters#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The cards\nsit on a chip fill that lifts to a surface with a faint ring when picked; the field is a pill on a\nsurface with the shared shadow, and the Send button uses the accent tokens (a disabled hatch until a\nstarter is picked). All colours, radii and spacing come from the `--vo-*` tokens."},"1026":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","type":"page","content":"Proposal card","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/proposal-card"},"1027":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-0","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card","content":"A suggested change with confidence, alternatives and undo."},"1028":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-1","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#usage","content":"Usage"},"1029":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-2","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"Properties"},"1030":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-3","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#theming","content":"Theming"},"1031":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-4","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card","content":"A proposal card is a change the agent proposes, posted in the thread. It shows a `from` value\nchanging to the chosen option, a confidence meter that fills in a moment after the card appears\nand then follows the chosen option, and the other `options` behind an \"other options\" fold. Accept,\nNot now and Undo move it between `open`, `accepted` and `dismissed`. By default it sits flat in a\nchat thread; set `bare` to `false` to give it a card of its own."},"1032":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-5","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                     |\n| ------- | ----------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `ReactNode` | What the agent wants to change. |","table":"table-0"},"1033":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-6","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name       | Type        | Description                          |\n| ---------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `subtitle` | `ReactNode` | Where, like \"Pricing, frame 2 of 3\". |","table":"table-0"},"1034":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-7","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                               |\n| ------ | ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `icon` | `IconName` | The icon in the tile. Defaults to a wand. |","table":"table-0"},"1035":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-8","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name   | Type            | Description                                    |\n| ------ | --------------- | ---------------------------------------------- |\n| `from` | `ProposalValue` | How it is now — a swatch, its label and a tag. |","table":"table-0"},"1036":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-9","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name      | Type               | Description                                   |\n| --------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `options` | `ProposalOption[]` | The changes on offer, the agent's pick first. |","table":"table-0"},"1037":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-10","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type     | Description                                                                         |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `defaultValue` | `number` | Index of the option shown as the change. Leave `value` out to let the list pick it. |","table":"table-0"},"1038":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-11","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                           |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(index) => void` | Called when another option is chosen. |","table":"table-0"},"1039":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-12","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether the other options are listed. Leave `open` out to let the toggle open them. |","table":"table-0"},"1040":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-13","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                   |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open) => void` | Called when the fold toggles. |","table":"table-0"},"1041":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-14","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name                       | Type                            | Description                                                 |\n| -------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` / `defaultStatus` | `open \\| accepted \\| dismissed` | Leave `status` out to let Accept, Not now and Undo move it. |","table":"table-0"},"1042":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-15","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                     |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| `onStatusChange` | `(status) => void` | Called when the status changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1043":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-16","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                      | Description                                           |\n| ---------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onAccept` | `(option, index) => void` | Called with the chosen option when Accept is pressed. |","table":"table-0"},"1044":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-17","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type         | Description                 |\n| ---------------------- | ------------ | --------------------------- |\n| `onDismiss` / `onUndo` | `() => void` | Called by Not now and Undo. |","table":"table-0"},"1045":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-18","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                       |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `acceptedLabel` | `string` | Shown once accepted, like \"Applied to 3 buttons\". |","table":"table-0"},"1046":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-19","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description           |\n| ---------------- | -------- | --------------------- |\n| `dismissedLabel` | `string` | Shown once dismissed. |","table":"table-0"},"1047":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-20","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name              | Type     | Description                        |\n| ----------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `confidenceLabel` | `string` | Label beside the confidence meter. |","table":"table-0"},"1048":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-21","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"1049":{"id":"/docs/components/proposal-card-22","page_id":"/docs/components/proposal-card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/proposal-card#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The diff\nchip, confidence meter and tags take their colours from the theme tokens — the current value reads as\n`bad` and the options as `ok` by default — and the icon tile uses the accent tint, so the card reads\nagainst the dark stage; in Soft the swatches, tile and pills are rounder."},"1050":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","type":"page","content":"Radar chart","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radar-chart"},"1051":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart","content":"This run against the baseline on six eval scores, with the weak ones flagged."},"1052":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#usage","content":"Usage"},"1053":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"Properties"},"1054":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#theming","content":"Theming"},"1055":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart","content":"A radar chart compares a run with its baseline on a handful of eval scores: the baseline draws itself\nas an outline, then this run grows out of the middle filled over it, on grey scale rings. Each axis\ntakes a `label`, this run's `value` and the `baseline` it is measured against, both 0 to 100; a score\nunder `weakBelow` is flagged \"Weak\". Pointing at or tabbing to an axis shows its two scores and the\nchange in the line below, and the legend shows and hides either series (one always stays)."},"1056":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type          | Description                                                                               |\n| ------ | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `axes` | `RadarAxis[]` | Five to seven axes, clockwise from the top. Each is `{ label, short?, value, baseline }`. |","table":"table-0"},"1057":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                  |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The bold heading. Defaults to `Eval scores`. |","table":"table-0"},"1058":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ---------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The quieter line beside the title, like \"Run 48 against run 41\". |","table":"table-0"},"1059":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"| Name           | Type               | Description                                                                    |\n| -------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `seriesLabels` | `[string, string]` | The legend's names for the two series. Defaults to `['This run', 'Baseline']`. |","table":"table-0"},"1060":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                             |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `weakBelow` | `number` | A score under this is flagged \"Weak\". Defaults to `70`. |","table":"table-0"},"1061":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                                                                          |\n| ------ | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `note` | `ReactNode` | The note under the chart, shown while no axis is pointed at. Defaults to the average and its change. |","table":"table-0"},"1062":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pulse` | `number` | An axis to call out once the chart is drawn: its label pulses (by index). |","table":"table-0"},"1063":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#properties","content":"A `RadarAxis` is `{ label: string; short?: string; value: number; baseline: number }`; `short` is\nshown instead of `label` on a narrow card, and `value`/`baseline` are 0 to 100."},"1064":{"id":"/docs/components/radar-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/radar-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radar-chart#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). This run\nand the baseline take the chart palette tokens (`--vo-c1`, `--vo-c2`), the rings and spokes read from\nthe line tokens, and the card, the \"Weak\" tag and the readout line come from the theme tokens. The\nbaseline draws itself and this run's fill scales in from the middle on load; with\n`prefers-reduced-motion` the chart appears already drawn."},"1065":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","type":"page","content":"Radial goals","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radial-goals"},"1066":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-0","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals","content":"Each agent's share of its own target as a ring, with the overall score in the middle."},"1067":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-1","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#usage","content":"Usage"},"1068":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-2","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"Properties"},"1069":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-3","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#theming","content":"Theming"},"1070":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-4","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals","content":"Radial goals are concentric rings, one per agent, each its share of its own target. The overall\nscore sits in the middle. Past the target a ring goes round again from the top, with a marker where\nit ends, so an agent that is ahead reads as a second lap. Hovering or focusing a ring — or its\nlegend row — dims the rest and rolls the middle to that agent's share. A `ranges` switch (like Week\nand Month) repaints every ring."},"1071":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-5","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"| Name    | Type           | Description                                                                                       |\n| ------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `goals` | `RadialGoal[]` | Two to five agents, outermost first. Three read best — the fewer the rings, the thicker they are. |","table":"table-0"},"1072":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-6","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                               |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The heading above the rings. Defaults to `\"Agent goals\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"1073":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-7","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to `\"N of M on target\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"1074":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-8","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                 | Description                                                              |\n| -------- | -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `ranges` | `{ value; label }[]` | The period switch options, like Week and Month. Leave out for no switch. |","table":"table-0"},"1075":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-9","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `range` | `string` | The selected range value (controlled). Leave out to let the switch pick it. |","table":"table-0"},"1076":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-10","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"| Name            | Type                      | Description                                              |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRangeChange` | `(range: string) => void` | Called with the new range value when the switch changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1077":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-11","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#properties","content":"Each `RadialGoal` carries a `key`, a `label` (like \"Support agent\"), a `unit` (what it counts, like\n\"tickets\"), the `value` done, its `target`, and an optional `color`. The share is `value / target`;\nat or past the target the ring's row shows an \"on target\" chip, and the ring draws a second lap with\na marker. Colours fall back to the chart palette (the accent, then green, orange, violet and red)."},"1078":{"id":"/docs/components/radial-goals-12","page_id":"/docs/components/radial-goals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/radial-goals#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The ring\ntracks use the chip token and the laps and dots use the chart palette, so the rings read on either\nsurface; the \"on target\" chip uses the ok tokens. In Soft the panel and the legend rows are rounder.\nRespecting `prefers-reduced-motion`, the sweep and the middle readout settle without animating."},"1079":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","type":"page","content":"Reasoning trail","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail"},"1080":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-0","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","content":"The agent's plan, notes, sources or edits, under a header it can fold away."},"1081":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-1","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#usage","content":"Usage"},"1082":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-2","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"Properties"},"1083":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-3","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#theming","content":"Theming"},"1084":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-4","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","content":"A reasoning trail is the structured record the agent leaves after it thinks: a plan it works\nthrough, the notes it took, the sources it read, or the edits it made. Pick what it shows with\n`view`. The header counts the seconds and shimmers while the run is live, folds the trail away, and\nsettles on \"Reasoned for Ns\" once it finishes."},"1085":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-5","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                           |\n| --------- | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `running` | `boolean` | Shimmers the title and counts the seconds while true. |","table":"table-0"},"1086":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-6","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                         |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds to show. Leave it out to let the trail count while it runs. |","table":"table-0"},"1087":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-7","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                     |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Header text. Defaults to \"Reasoning\" while running and \"Reasoned for Ns\" after. |","table":"table-0"},"1088":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-8","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name   | Type         | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------ | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `plan` | `PlanStep[]` | The plan. Each step has a `label`, an optional `detail`, and a `state` of done, now or next. |","table":"table-0"},"1089":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-9","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name    | Type       | Description                      |\n| ------- | ---------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `notes` | `string[]` | The agent's notes, one per line. |","table":"table-0"},"1090":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-10","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name      | Type       | Description                                                                                 |\n| --------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sources` | `Source[]` | The files and links it read. Each has a `label`, an optional `kind`, and an optional `tip`. |","table":"table-0"},"1091":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-11","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `edits` | `Edit[]` | The changed files. Each has a `file`, an optional `detail`, and `removed` and `added` lines. |","table":"table-0"},"1092":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-12","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name   | Type                                | Description                                                          |\n| ------ | ----------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `view` | `plan \\| notes \\| sources \\| edits` | Which part to show. Leave it out to start on the first one there is. |","table":"table-0"},"1093":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-13","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                          |\n| ------ | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the trail is open. Leave it out to let the header toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"1094":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-14","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set false to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"1095":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-15","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name                          | Type       | Description                        |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onViewChange` / `viewChange` | `callback` | Fires when the shown view changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1096":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-16","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#properties","content":"| Name                          | Type       | Description                          |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `onOpenChange` / `openChange` | `callback` | Fires when the trail opens or folds. |","table":"table-0"},"1097":{"id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail-17","page_id":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/reasoning-trail#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the header, chips and edit blocks are squared off with hairline edges; in Soft they are\nrounded. The timeline rail, the pulse on the current step, and the shimmer on the title all take\ntheir colors from the tokens; added and removed lines use the add and remove colors."},"1098":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","type":"page","content":"Response versions","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/response-versions"},"1099":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-0","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions","content":"Regenerate an answer and flip between versions."},"1100":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-1","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/response-versions#usage","content":"Usage"},"1101":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-2","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"Properties"},"1102":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-3","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/response-versions#theming","content":"Theming"},"1103":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-4","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions","content":"An answer with its earlier versions a click away. The arrows page through every `versions` entry\n(oldest first); a different version fades the old text out, then the new one arrives word by word.\nThe regenerate button calls `onRegenerate` so you can add a version and show it, and the copy button\ncopies the version on screen. While `streaming` is set the new words fade in as they arrive, paging\nwaits, and the `status` beside the buttons shimmers."},"1104":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-5","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name     | Type        | Description                                                             |\n| -------- | ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `prompt` | `ReactNode` | The person's message the answer replies to, shown as a bubble above it. |","table":"table-0"},"1105":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-6","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name       | Type       | Description                                       |\n| ---------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `versions` | `string[]` | Every version of the answer so far, oldest first. |","table":"table-0"},"1106":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-7","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                 |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `version` | `number` | Which version is showing. Leave it out to let the arrows page through them. |","table":"table-0"},"1107":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-8","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultVersion` | `number` | The version shown at first when `version` is left out. Defaults to `0`. |","table":"table-0"},"1108":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-9","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name              | Type              | Description                                     |\n| ----------------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `onVersionChange` | `(index) => void` | Called when the arrows move to another version. |","table":"table-0"},"1109":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-10","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                                                                    |\n| ----------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `streaming` | `boolean` | The version showing is still being written. New words fade in as they arrive and paging waits. |","table":"table-0"},"1110":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-11","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                               |\n| -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | Quiet text beside the buttons, like \"Writing a new version\". It shimmers while streaming. |","table":"table-0"},"1111":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-12","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name           | Type         | Description                                                                                               |\n| -------------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRegenerate` | `() => void` | Called by the regenerate button. Add a version and show it to answer it. Leave it out to hide the button. |","table":"table-0"},"1112":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-13","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name     | Type             | Description                                               |\n| -------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCopy` | `(text) => void` | Called with the text after it is copied to the clipboard. |","table":"table-0"},"1113":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-14","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"1114":{"id":"/docs/components/response-versions-15","page_id":"/docs/components/response-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/response-versions#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The prompt\nbubble, the muted count and status, and the icon buttons all take their colour from the theme tokens;\neach new word fades in, the regenerate glyph turns a full circle, and copy flips to a check in the\n`--vo-ok` colour. Reduced motion drops the word fade, the spin and the status shimmer."},"1115":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","type":"page","content":"Rewrite toolbar","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar"},"1116":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","content":"Select a sentence and let the agent rewrite it in place."},"1117":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#usage","content":"Usage"},"1118":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"Properties"},"1119":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#theming","content":"Theming"},"1120":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","content":"Click a sentence in the document and a small toolbar offers rewrites — `Clearer`, `Shorter`,\n`Friendlier` by default. Pick one and `onRewrite` is called; while it works the toolbar says\nRewriting, then the answer is written in beside the old sentence word by word, struck-through\nold against the new. Keep it with Accept or put it back with Undo. The toolbar sits above the\nsentence, or under it when above would cover the header."},"1121":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                              |\n| ------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `ReactNode` | The document's name shown in the header. |","table":"table-0"},"1122":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-6","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `kind` | `string` | The file type tag in front of the name. Defaults to `DOC`. |","table":"table-0"},"1123":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-7","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name                             | Type       | Description                                               |\n| -------------------------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sentences` / `defaultSentences` | `string[]` | The text, one sentence each, so a click picks a sentence. |","table":"table-0"},"1124":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-8","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name                | Type                  | Description                                            |\n| ------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSentencesChange` | `(sentences) => void` | Called with every sentence once a rewrite is accepted. |","table":"table-0"},"1125":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-9","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name                           | Type             | Description                                              |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `selected` / `defaultSelected` | `number \\| null` | Index of the sentence with the toolbar on it, or `null`. |","table":"table-0"},"1126":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-10","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name               | Type              | Description                                |\n| ------------------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSelectedChange` | `(index) => void` | Called when the selected sentence changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1127":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-11","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name      | Type              | Description                                                         |\n| --------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `actions` | `RewriteAction[]` | The toolbar's buttons. Defaults to Clearer, Shorter and Friendlier. |","table":"table-0"},"1128":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-12","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                                                     | Description                                                             |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRewrite` | `(sentence, action, index) => Promise<string> \\| string` | Writes the new sentence. If it rejects, the sentence is left as it was. |","table":"table-0"},"1129":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-13","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                        | Description                                                                      |\n| ------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onAsk` | `(sentence, index) => void` | The wand at the end of the toolbar. Left out, it rewrites with the first action. |","table":"table-0"},"1130":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-14","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `askLabel` | `string` | The tip on the wand. Defaults to `Ask the agent`. |","table":"table-0"},"1131":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-15","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `askShortcut` | `string` | The shortcut shown in that tip. Defaults to `⌘K`. |","table":"table-0"},"1132":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-16","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#properties","content":"| Name  | Type                   | Description                                                                |\n| ----- | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ref` | `RewriteToolbarHandle` | Drive it from a shortcut or demo: `rewrite(action)`, `accept()`, `undo()`. |","table":"table-0"},"1133":{"id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar-17","page_id":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rewrite-toolbar#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ndocument sits on a surface panel; the floating toolbar uses the ink/on-ink tokens so it reads as a\ndark pill over the text, and the picked sentence tints with `--vo-sel`. The struck-through old text\nuses the bad token for its line, and the new words fade and de-blur in as they arrive."},"1134":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","type":"page","content":"Rich text editor","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor"},"1135":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-0","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","content":"A minimal editor with an inline AI menu that streams a suggestion to accept or discard."},"1136":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-1","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#usage","content":"Usage"},"1137":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-2","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"Properties"},"1138":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-3","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#theming","content":"Theming"},"1139":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-4","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","content":"A minimal editor for a draft an agent helps with: a formatting toolbar (heading, bold, italic,\ninline code, link, lists and quote), the text, and a quiet foot with the word count and undo. Select\ntext and press **Ask AI** — or `⌘J`/`Ctrl+J`, or type `/` on a new line — and a suggestion streams in\nbeside the text, the old words struck through and the new ones arriving word by word, to accept with\n`Tab` (or `Enter`) or discard with `Esc`. Pass your own `ai` to call a model; the default streams a\ncanned demo."},"1140":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-5","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#usage","content":"Pass your model as `ai` to replace the demo writer — return a string, a promise, or an async\niterable of chunks to stream the suggestion in as the model answers."},"1141":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-6","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                                            |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `defaultValue` | `string` | The text as HTML: paragraphs, one heading level (`h2`), lists, quotes, and inside them bold, italic, inline code and links. Anything else is cleaned out, as on paste. |","table":"table-0"},"1142":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-7","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name                         | Type             | Description                                                                                   |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` / `onChange` | `(html) => void` | Called with the HTML after each change the person makes. Not while a suggestion is on screen. |","table":"table-0"},"1143":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-8","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | Shown while the editor is empty. |","table":"table-0"},"1144":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-9","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | The text box's accessible name. Defaults to `Draft`. |","table":"table-0"},"1145":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-10","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                                            |\n| ------ | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `hint` | `ReactNode` | The quiet hint beside the word count, on wide editors. |","table":"table-0"},"1146":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-11","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name | Type                  | Description                                                                                                                |\n| ---- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ai` | `RichTextAi \\| false` | Writes the AI's suggestions. Defaults to a demo that streams canned text; pass your model call, or `false` to hide the AI. |","table":"table-0"},"1147":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-12","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                 | Description                                                                               |\n| ----------- | -------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `aiActions` | `RichTextAiAction[]` | The AI menu. Defaults to Improve writing, Make shorter, Fix grammar and Continue writing. |","table":"table-0"},"1148":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-13","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                                   | Description                                        |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSuggestion` | `({ action, text, accepted }) => void` | Called when a suggestion is accepted or discarded. |","table":"table-0"},"1149":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-14","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#properties","content":"| Name  | Type                   | Description                                                                                                                                                          |\n| ----- | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ref` | `RichTextEditorHandle` | A handle to drive the editor: `focus`, `getHTML`, `getText`, `setHTML`, `select`, `type`, `newLine`, `format`, `openAi`, `ask`, `accept`, `discard`, `undo`, `redo`. |","table":"table-0"},"1150":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-15","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The editor\nkeeps one height so it sits still, and its quiet text (word count, placeholder, struck words) comes up\ntoward the foreground in dark mode to stay legible. The suggestion's new words use the accent tint with\na blur-in that is reduced to an instant reveal under `prefers-reduced-motion`. In Soft the toolbar's\nactive format and the suggestion pick up a hairline of the accent mark."},"1151":{"id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor-16","page_id":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/rich-text-editor#theming","content":"The Flutter port approximates the contenteditable surface (which the web uses natively): the body is a\nread-oriented rich view driven through a `RichTextEditorController`, with the same toolbar, word count\nand streamed Ask-AI flow. See the file header for the full list of approximations."},"1152":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","type":"page","content":"Run cost","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-cost"},"1153":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-0","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost","content":"Live credit and token spend against a budget, with a cap the agent pauses at."},"1154":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-1","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-cost#usage","content":"Usage"},"1155":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-2","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"Properties"},"1156":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-3","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-cost#theming","content":"Theming"},"1157":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-4","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost","content":"A run cost shows the credits a run has used against its budget, as a number and a meter. A cap\nmarks where the agent pauses, drawn as a line across the bar; when the spend reaches it the status\nturns amber and the run pauses. The breakdown under the bar shows the tokens and tool calls behind\nthe number, and the button starts, stops, resumes or raises the cap by status."},"1158":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-5","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description          |\n| ------ | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `used` | `number` | Credits used so far. |","table":"table-0"},"1159":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-6","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                  |\n| -------- | -------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `budget` | `number` | The whole budget, like 2000. |","table":"table-0"},"1160":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-7","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                            |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `capAt` | `number` | Where the agent pauses, as a percentage of the budget. Defaults to 90. |","table":"table-0"},"1161":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-8","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name    | Type      | Description                                                      |\n| ------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `capOn` | `boolean` | Whether the cap is on. Leave it out to let the switch change it. |","table":"table-0"},"1162":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-9","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                                            | Description                               |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `idle \\| running \\| stopped \\| paused \\| spent` | running is blue, paused amber, spent red. |","table":"table-0"},"1163":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-10","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                  |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `statusLabel` | `string` | Words in the status tag. Defaults by status. |","table":"table-0"},"1164":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-11","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name   | Type           | Description                                                        |\n| ------ | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `rows` | `RunCostRow[]` | The breakdown under the bar; each row has a `label` and a `value`. |","table":"table-0"},"1165":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-12","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                              |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `actionLabel` | `string` | Words on the button. Defaults by status. |","table":"table-0"},"1166":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-13","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                 |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Defaults to \"Credits used\". |","table":"table-0"},"1167":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-14","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set false to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"1168":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-15","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name                  | Type       | Description           |\n| --------------------- | ---------- | --------------------- |\n| `onAction` / `action` | `callback` | Called by the button. |","table":"table-0"},"1169":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-16","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#properties","content":"| Name                        | Type       | Description                        |\n| --------------------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onCapChange` / `capChange` | `callback` | Fires when the cap switch changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1170":{"id":"/docs/components/run-cost-17","page_id":"/docs/components/run-cost","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-cost#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bar, the tag and the toggle are squared off; in Soft they are rounded. The fill takes\nthe accent mark while running and the warning mark once paused at the cap, and the status tag tints\nto match its state, all from the tokens."},"1171":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","type":"page","content":"Run queue","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-queue"},"1172":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-0","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue","content":"A queue of agent jobs in three parts — the one running with its steps and progress, the ones up next, and the ones done — with a compact toggle."},"1173":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-1","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-queue#usage","content":"Usage"},"1174":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-2","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"Properties"},"1175":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-3","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-queue#theming","content":"Theming"},"1176":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-4","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue","content":"A run queue shows a batch of agent jobs moving through three parts. The job running is raised on\nits own card with its agent, its steps, a progress bar and the time left. The jobs up next wait\nbelow, each with when it should start, and the jobs done sit under them with how long each took and\na green tick. A failed step turns its job red and offers a Retry; a Detailed / Compact switch folds\nthe running job's steps away; and once every job is done a summary takes the running job's place."},"1177":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-5","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                                                                                                               |\n| ------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `jobs` | `RunJob[]` | The jobs in the queue. Each has a title, an agent, an icon, a state, an optional progress, a time, a note, and its steps. |","table":"table-0"},"1178":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-6","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                            |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The queue's name over its status line. |","table":"table-0"},"1179":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-7","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                           |\n| -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | Overrides the status line. Defaults to \"1 of 4 done\" or \"All 4 done\". |","table":"table-0"},"1180":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-8","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                             |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `summary` | `string` | The line under \"All N jobs done\" once every job is done, like \"18.4s in all · 1 retry\". |","table":"table-0"},"1181":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-9","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                  | Description                                                                                       |\n| --------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `density` | `detailed \\| compact` | detailed lists the running job's steps, compact folds them away. Left out, the switch changes it. |","table":"table-0"},"1182":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-10","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name                                | Type       | Description                                       |\n| ----------------------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDensityChange` / `densityChange` | `callback` | Fires when the Detailed / Compact switch changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1183":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-11","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name                | Type       | Description                                                                                                          |\n| ------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRetry` / `retry` | `callback` | Called by a failed step's Retry button with the job's and the step's index. Without it, failed steps show no button. |","table":"table-0"},"1184":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-12","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                 |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread, with no card. False by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1185":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-13","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#properties","content":"A `RunJob` state is queued, running, failed, or done. A `RunStep` has a label, a state, and an\noptional meta shown once the step is done. Progress defaults to the share of a job's steps that are\ndone."},"1186":{"id":"/docs/components/run-queue-14","page_id":"/docs/components/run-queue","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-queue#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the running job gets a hairline in the accent and the progress bars fill in steps. A\nfailed job turns red with a hatched fill; the step glyphs are a spinner while running, a tick when\ndone, and a cross on failure."},"1187":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","type":"page","content":"Run summary","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-summary"},"1188":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-0","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary","content":"What the agent did, what changed and what needs you."},"1189":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-1","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-summary#usage","content":"Usage"},"1190":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-2","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"Properties"},"1191":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-3","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/run-summary#theming","content":"Theming"},"1192":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-4","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary","content":"A run summary closes out an agent run: a title glyph and a quiet subtitle, a line on what the run\ndid, and `stats` that count up from zero. Under them, `changes` list the files the run touched and\n`needs` carry what is still on the person, each with an optional action button. \"Undo all\" greys out\nthe changes and swaps the glyph; leave `undone` out to let the button toggle it, or control it."},"1193":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-5","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                    |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The title while the changes stand. Defaults to `Run complete`. |","table":"table-0"},"1194":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-6","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                          |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `undoneTitle` | `string` | The title once the changes are undone. Defaults to `Changes undone`. |","table":"table-0"},"1195":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-7","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The quiet line under the title, like `Finished in 12m 40s`. |","table":"table-0"},"1196":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-8","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name      | Type        | Description                   |\n| --------- | ----------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `summary` | `ReactNode` | One line on what the run did. |","table":"table-0"},"1197":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-9","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                                                                 |\n| ------- | ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stats` | `RunStat[]` | `{ label; value; prefix?; suffix?; decimals? }` — each counts up from zero. |","table":"table-0"},"1198":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-10","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name      | Type          | Description                                                                   |\n| --------- | ------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `changes` | `RunChange[]` | `{ file; added; removed }` — the files the run changed, under \"What changed\". |","table":"table-0"},"1199":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-11","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                                                                        |\n| ------- | ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `needs` | `RunNeed[]` | `{ key; text; action?: { label; onClick; busy? } }` — what is left for the person. |","table":"table-0"},"1200":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-12","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name     | Type      | Description                                                               |\n| -------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `undone` | `boolean` | Whether the changes are undone. Leave it out to let \"Undo all\" toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"1201":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-13","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                                       |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onUndoneChange` | `(undone) => void` | Fires when \"Undo all\" / \"Redo\" toggles the state. |","table":"table-0"},"1202":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-14","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name        | Type         | Description                                               |\n| ----------- | ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDetails` | `() => void` | Adds a button in the corner that opens the run's details. |","table":"table-0"},"1203":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-15","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name            | Type         | Description                      |\n| --------------- | ------------ | -------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChanges` | `() => void` | The main button, \"Open changes\". |","table":"table-0"},"1204":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-16","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat thread (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"1205":{"id":"/docs/components/run-summary-17","page_id":"/docs/components/run-summary","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/run-summary#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The glyph,\nthe `+`/`−` diffs and the \"Needs you\" dot all take their colour from the theme tokens (`--vo-ok`,\n`--vo-add`, `--vo-del`, `--vo-warn-mark`), so the summary reads the same against any surface; in Soft\nthe card and its pills are rounder."},"1206":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","type":"page","content":"Scatter chart","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart"},"1207":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-0","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","content":"Every run as a dot by cost and eval score, sized by tokens, with quadrants and a drag to select."},"1208":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-1","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#usage","content":"Usage"},"1209":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-2","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"Properties"},"1210":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-3","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#theming","content":"Theming"},"1211":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-4","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","content":"A scatter chart plots every `run` as a dot by its `x` (cost along the bottom) and `y` (eval score up\nthe side), sized by its `size` (tokens). Each `series` has a colour and a shape, so it reads without\ncolour too. Dashed median lines cut the plot into four named `quadrants`; pointing snaps to the\nnearest run and shows a tooltip, and a drag draws a box that selects the runs in it. Pass `ringed`\nids to circle outliers, and an `onAsk` handler to add \"Ask the agent why\" to a selection."},"1212":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-5","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type           | Description                                                          |\n| ------ | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `runs` | `ScatterRun[]` | Each run is a dot: `id`, `series`, `x` (along), `y` (up) and `size`. |","table":"table-0"},"1213":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-6","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type              | Description                                                                    |\n| -------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `series` | `ScatterSeries[]` | `key`, `label`, optional `color` and `shape` (`circle \\| square \\| triangle`). |","table":"table-0"},"1214":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-7","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                      |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `title` | `string` | The bold heading. Defaults to \"Cost vs quality\". |","table":"table-0"},"1215":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-8","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                        |\n| ---------- | -------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `subtitle` | `string` | The quieter line beside the title. |","table":"table-0"},"1216":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-9","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name                  | Type               | Description                    |\n| --------------------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------ |\n| `xDomain` / `yDomain` | `[number, number]` | The `[min, max]` of each axis. |","table":"table-0"},"1217":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-10","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name                | Type       | Description                                                                          |\n| ------------------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `xTicks` / `yTicks` | `number[]` | Where the labels and gridlines go. A narrow chart keeps the two ends and the middle. |","table":"table-0"},"1218":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-11","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name                | Type     | Description                          |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| `xTitle` / `yTitle` | `string` | The axis titles, clear of the ticks. |","table":"table-0"},"1219":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-12","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name                                 | Type            | Description                                           |\n| ------------------------------------ | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `formatX` / `formatY` / `formatSize` | `(n) => string` | Writes the axis values and the tooltip's token count. |","table":"table-0"},"1220":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-13","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                               | Description                                                                                    |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `quadrants` | `[string, string, string, string]` | The four names the medians make, from the top left, clockwise. A narrow chart leaves them out. |","table":"table-0"},"1221":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-14","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                   | Description                                  |\n| -------- | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `ringed` | `(string \\| number)[]` | Runs to ring, like outliers the agent found. |","table":"table-0"},"1222":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-15","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                         |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `note` | `string` | The line under the chart while nothing is selected. |","table":"table-0"},"1223":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-16","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                   | Description                                                                 |\n| ---------- | ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `selected` | `(string \\| number)[]` | The selected runs, by id. Leave it out to let the chart hold the selection. |","table":"table-0"},"1224":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-17","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name               | Type            | Description                            |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onSelectedChange` | `(ids) => void` | Fires when the drag selection changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1225":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-18","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                  | Description                                                     |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onAsk` | `(runs) => string \\| Promise<string>` | Adds \"Ask the agent why\" to a selection; the answer streams in. |","table":"table-0"},"1226":{"id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart-19","page_id":"/docs/components/scatter-chart","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/scatter-chart#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The dots\ntake the chart palette (`--vo-c1`…`--vo-c6`); the gridlines, axes, median lines and the selection box\nare mixed from the line and foreground tokens, and the tooltip sits on the ink token — so the chart\nreads on either theme without any hard-coded colours."},"1227":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","type":"page","content":"Score breakdown","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown"},"1228":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-0","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","content":"A score out of 100 whose gauge is split by what goes into it, with the weakest part flagged and a fix to try."},"1229":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-1","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#usage","content":"Usage"},"1230":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-2","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"Properties"},"1231":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-3","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#theming","content":"Theming"},"1232":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-4","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","content":"A single score out of 100, with a half-circle gauge split into one segment per `factor`, each\nsized by its `weight` and filled by the points it `earned`. The rows under it say what each earned\nand why; the weakest factor is flagged in words, and an `improvable` row offers **Improve**, which\nasks the agent (`onImprove`) for a proposal you can **Apply** to lift that factor's points — and the\nwhole score with it."},"1233":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-5","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name      | Type            | Description                                            |\n| --------- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `factors` | `ScoreFactor[]` | The parts of the score; their `weight`s add up to 100. |","table":"table-0"},"1234":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-6","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The gauge label and heading. Defaults to `\"Quality score\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"1235":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-7","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ---------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `previous` | `number` | Last period's score, for the change shown beside the band word. |","table":"table-0"},"1236":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-8","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                           |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `since` | `string` | What the change is measured against. Defaults to `\"since last week\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"1237":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-9","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type       | Description                                   |\n| ---------------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `string[]` | The open rows, by key (controlled / initial). |","table":"table-0"},"1238":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-10","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                       | Description                       |\n| -------------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open: string[]) => void` | Fires when a row opens or closes. |","table":"table-0"},"1239":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-11","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                                      | Description                                                              |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onImprove` | `(factor) => ScoreProposal \\| Promise<…>` | Called by **Improve**; while it waits the row says the agent is looking. |","table":"table-0"},"1240":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-12","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                         | Description                                                   |\n| --------- | ---------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onApply` | `(factor, proposal) => void` | Called by **Apply**; update the factor's `earned` and `note`. |","table":"table-0"},"1241":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-13","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `improvingLabel` | `string` | What the row says while the agent works. Defaults to `\"Looking into it\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"1242":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-14","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name                              | Type     | Description                                |\n| --------------------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `factor.weight` / `factor.earned` | `number` | The points a factor can earn and did earn. |","table":"table-0"},"1243":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-15","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `factor.note` | `string` | The agent's one-line note, like `\"Median reply 6.4s, target under 4s\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"1244":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-16","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name                | Type      | Description                                 |\n| ------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `factor.improvable` | `boolean` | Adds an **Improve** button to the open row. |","table":"table-0"},"1245":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-17","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `factor.detail` | `string` | A line shown first in the open row, like what was changed. |","table":"table-0"},"1246":{"id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown-18","page_id":"/docs/components/score-breakdown","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/score-breakdown#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The gauge\nsegments and the row swatches use the chart palette (`--vo-c1`…`--vo-c6`); the band chip, the Weakest\nflag and the proposal card tint from the theme tokens (`--vo-ok`, `--vo-warn`, `--vo-surface`,\n`--vo-line`), so the breakdown reads on either background. In Soft the rows and buttons are rounder."},"1247":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","type":"page","content":"Search input","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/search-input"},"1248":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-0","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input","content":"Search with scoped filters, recent queries and an inline agent answer."},"1249":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-1","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/search-input#usage","content":"Usage"},"1250":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-2","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"Properties"},"1251":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-3","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/search-input#theming","content":"Theming"},"1252":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-4","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input","content":"A search field with a leading icon and a clear button. Optional scope chips narrow the search; a\ndropdown shows recent queries while the field is empty and live results as you type, with an\noptional agent answer on top. Press Enter to search, or pick a result."},"1253":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-5","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type                  | Description                                                       |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `onValueChange` | `string` / `callback` | The text in the field. Omit `value` to let the component keep it. |","table":"table-0"},"1254":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-6","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | Placeholder shown while the field is empty. |","table":"table-0"},"1255":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-7","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name     | Type            | Description                                                                                                       |\n| -------- | --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `scopes` | `SearchScope[]` | Scope chips before the field. The active one narrows the search. Each has a `value`, optional `label` and `icon`. |","table":"table-0"},"1256":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-8","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type                  | Description               |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| `scope` / `onScopeChange` | `string` / `callback` | The active scope's value. |","table":"table-0"},"1257":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-9","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name      | Type             | Description                                                                                    |\n| --------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `results` | `SearchResult[]` | Live results for the current query. Each has a `value`, optional `label`, `detail` and `icon`. |","table":"table-0"},"1258":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-10","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name     | Type       | Description                                      |\n| -------- | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `recent` | `string[]` | Earlier queries, shown while the field is empty. |","table":"table-0"},"1259":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-11","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name     | Type   | Description                                                        |\n| -------- | ------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `answer` | `node` | The agent's answer for the current query, shown above the results. |","table":"table-0"},"1260":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-12","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                      |\n| --------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `loading` | `boolean` | Shows a spinner in the field while results load. |","table":"table-0"},"1261":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-13","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                     | Description                                |\n| ---------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSearch` | `(query, scope) => void` | Called on submit (Enter) or a recent pick. |","table":"table-0"},"1262":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-14","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name       | Type              | Description                                     |\n| ---------- | ----------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSelect` | `(value) => void` | Called with a result's value when it is picked. |","table":"table-0"},"1263":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-15","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#properties","content":"| Name      | Type       | Description                       |\n| --------- | ---------- | --------------------------------- |\n| `onClear` | `callback` | Called when the field is cleared. |","table":"table-0"},"1264":{"id":"/docs/components/search-input-16","page_id":"/docs/components/search-input","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/search-input#theming","content":"The field, scope chips and dropdown all draw from the shared `--vo-*` tokens, so they work in light\nand dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The field shows focus\nwith its own edge (no extra ring); the agent answer sits on a faint accent tint."},"1265":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","type":"page","content":"Segmented Control","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Dates"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-control"},"1266":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-0","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control","content":"One choice from a few views or options, with a white knob that slides to the picked one. Works as tabs or as a radio group, fully keyboard driven."},"1267":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-1","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#usage","content":"Usage"},"1268":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-2","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#properties","content":"Properties"},"1269":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-3","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#theming","content":"Theming"},"1270":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-4","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control","content":"A segmented control picks one of a few options. A white knob slides to the picked one. As `tabs`\n(the default) it switches a panel; as a `radio` group it sets an option. The arrow keys move along\nand pick, and Home and End jump to the ends. The `label` is required and names the group for screen\nreaders."},"1271":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-5","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                                    | Description                           |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `options` | `{ value: string; label: ReactNode }[]` | The choices, in order, left to right. |","table":"table-0"},"1272":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-6","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type     | Description                                                                   |\n| ------------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `defaultValue` | `string` | The picked value. Pass `value` with `onValueChange` for a controlled control. |","table":"table-0"},"1273":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-7","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#properties","content":"| Name            | Type                      | Description                                     |\n| --------------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(value: string) => void` | Fires with the new value when the pick changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1274":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-8","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | Names the group for screen readers, like `View`. Required. |","table":"table-0"},"1275":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-9","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#properties","content":"| Name | Type            | Description                                                                    |\n| ---- | --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `as` | `tabs \\| radio` | `tabs` (the default) when it switches a panel, `radio` when it sets an option. |","table":"table-0"},"1276":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-10","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#properties","content":"| Name | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                        |\n| ---- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `id` | `string` | Ties the tabs to their panel: give the panel an id of the form \"id-panel\" and point its aria-labelledby at \"id-value\". Defaults to a generated id. |","table":"table-0"},"1277":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-control-11","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-control","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-control#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ntrack and sliding knob take the active theme's surface and accent colors; in Blueprint the control\nis squared off, in Soft it is a pill with a rounder knob."},"1278":{"id":"/docs/components/slider","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","type":"page","content":"Slider","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/slider"},"1279":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-0","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider","content":"A value or a range on a stepped or continuous track, with named stops and an agent-recommended mark."},"1280":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-1","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/slider#usage","content":"Usage"},"1281":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-2","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"Properties"},"1282":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-3","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/slider#theming","content":"Theming"},"1283":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-4","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider","content":"Drag a thumb to set a value, or two thumbs for a `[low, high]` range. Give it discrete `step`s and\na labelled scale with `stops`, and mark a suggested value with `recommended`. Keyboard works too —\narrows step, Page keys jump by ten, Home/End go to the ends."},"1284":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-5","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `min` / `max` | `number` | The ends of the track. `0` and `100` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1285":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-6","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `step` | `number` | Step between values. `1` by default; `0` for a continuous track. |","table":"table-0"},"1286":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-7","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type                  | Description                                       |\n| ------------------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` / `onValueChange` | `number` / `callback` | A single thumb. The value and its change handler. |","table":"table-0"},"1287":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-8","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name                      | Type                            | Description                           |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `range` / `onRangeChange` | `[number, number]` / `callback` | Two thumbs for a `[low, high]` range. |","table":"table-0"},"1288":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-9","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                 | Description                                                                        |\n| ------- | -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stops` | `{ value, label }[]` | A labelled scale drawn under the track. Click a stop to jump to it (single value). |","table":"table-0"},"1289":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-10","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                            |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `recommended` | `number` | A value marked on the track as the agent's suggestion. |","table":"table-0"},"1290":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-11","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name        | Type      | Description                                         |\n| ----------- | --------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| `showValue` | `boolean` | Shows the value in a bubble above the active thumb. |","table":"table-0"},"1291":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-12","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                | Description                                           |\n| -------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `format` | `(value) => string` | Formats the displayed value, e.g. `` v => `$${v}` ``. |","table":"table-0"},"1292":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-13","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name       | Type      | Description                                |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `disabled` | `boolean` | Turns off interaction and dims the slider. |","table":"table-0"},"1293":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-14","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                     |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | Accessible name for the slider. |","table":"table-0"},"1294":{"id":"/docs/components/slider-15","page_id":"/docs/components/slider","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/slider#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The fill\nand thumbs take the accent, the rail and ticks the field/line tokens, and the recommended mark the\naccent's ring colour — all from `--vo-*`, so it recolours with the theme automatically."},"1295":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","type":"page","content":"Source stack","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/source-stack"},"1296":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-0","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack","content":"Everything the agent read, folded into one quiet pill."},"1297":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-1","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/source-stack#usage","content":"Usage"},"1298":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-2","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"Properties"},"1299":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-3","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/source-stack#theming","content":"Theming"},"1300":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-4","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack","content":"An answer with its sources folded into one quiet pill. Open the pill to see each source as a row —\nits favicon, where it came from and a small bar for how much it counted — and use the filter chips\nto pick by `kind` (`web`, `file`, `figma`, …). Each source takes a `title`, a `host`, a `relevance`\nfrom 0 to 1, a `mark` for the favicon square and its `color`; give one an `onOpen` and it grows an\nopen button on hover. Leave `open` and `filter` out to let the pill and chips drive themselves."},"1301":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-5","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type                   | Description                                           |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `children` / `message` | `ReactNode` / `string` | The answer the sources back up, shown above the pill. |","table":"table-0"},"1302":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-6","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name      | Type            | Description                                        |\n| --------- | --------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sources` | `StackSource[]` | The sources, drawn as rows when the stack is open. |","table":"table-0"},"1303":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-7","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name      | Type             | Description                                                      |\n| --------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `filters` | `SourceFilter[]` | The chips above the list. Defaults to All, Web, Files and Figma. |","table":"table-0"},"1304":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-8","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `filter` | `string` | The chosen filter. Leave it out to let the chips switch it. |","table":"table-0"},"1305":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-9","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `defaultFilter` | `string` | The filter to start on when uncontrolled. Defaults to `all`. |","table":"table-0"},"1306":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-10","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name             | Type               | Description                   |\n| ---------------- | ------------------ | ----------------------------- |\n| `onFilterChange` | `(filter) => void` | Called when a chip is picked. |","table":"table-0"},"1307":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-11","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                       |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the list is open. Leave it out to let the pill toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"1308":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-12","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name          | Type      | Description                                                    |\n| ------------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether it starts open when uncontrolled. Defaults to `false`. |","table":"table-0"},"1309":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-13","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                            |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open) => void` | Called when the pill toggles the list. |","table":"table-0"},"1310":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-14","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                                       |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.kind` | `string` | What kind of source it is; the chips pick by this, like `web`, `file` or `figma`. |","table":"table-0"},"1311":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-15","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description        |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `source.title` | `string` | The source's name. |","table":"table-0"},"1312":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-16","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                        |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.host` | `string` | Where it came from, like `baymard.com` or `Drive`. |","table":"table-0"},"1313":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-17","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name               | Type     | Description                   |\n| ------------------ | -------- | ----------------------------- |\n| `source.relevance` | `number` | 0 to 1, drawn as a small bar. |","table":"table-0"},"1314":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-18","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                    |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `source.mark` | `string` | One to three letters in the favicon square, like `B` or `CSV`. |","table":"table-0"},"1315":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-19","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                         |\n| -------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `source.color` | `string` | The favicon colour, any CSS colour. |","table":"table-0"},"1316":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-20","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#properties","content":"| Name            | Type         | Description                              |\n| --------------- | ------------ | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `source.onOpen` | `() => void` | Adds an open button that shows on hover. |","table":"table-0"},"1317":{"id":"/docs/components/source-stack-21","page_id":"/docs/components/source-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/source-stack#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The pill\nand rows ride the shared `--vo-*` tokens; the filter chips are white with a dimmed edge that steps up\non the picked one, and the relevance bars fill with `--vo-accent-mark`. In Soft the chips and rows are\nrounder. The entrance stagger and the one-time auto-open are skipped under reduced motion."},"1318":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","type":"page","content":"Stat cards","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/stat-cards"},"1319":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-0","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards","content":"A row of KPIs, each with its change against the period before and a sparkline, with a period switch that rolls the numbers and redraws the lines."},"1320":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-1","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#usage","content":"Usage"},"1321":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-2","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"Properties"},"1322":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-3","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#theming","content":"Theming"},"1323":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-4","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards","content":"Stat cards are a row of numbers that matter. Each card has an icon, a label, the value in large\ntype, its change against the period before (green from zero, red below), and a sparkline in its own\ncolour. A `period` switch along the top rolls the numbers to their new values and redraws every\nline."},"1324":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-5","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"| Name    | Type              | Description                                                                                                         |\n| ------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `stats` | `StatCardsStat[]` | The cards. Each has an `icon`, `label`, one `values` entry per period, and optional `prefix`, `suffix` and `color`. |","table":"table-0"},"1325":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-6","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                | Description                                                                           |\n| --------- | ------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `periods` | `StatCardsPeriod[]` | The switch options. Each has a `label` and an optional `compare` line shown on hover. |","table":"table-0"},"1326":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-7","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                           |\n| -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `period` | `number` | The period on show, by index. Leave it out to let the switch pick it. |","table":"table-0"},"1327":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-8","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultPeriod` | `number` | The period shown first when uncontrolled. Defaults to `0`. |","table":"table-0"},"1328":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-9","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"| Name             | Type                       | Description                                        |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onPeriodChange` | `(period: number) => void` | Called with the new index when the switch changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1329":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-10","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"| Name         | Type               | Description                                                               |\n| ------------ | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sparkRange` | `[number, number]` | The bottom and top of every sparkline. Defaults to each card's own range. |","table":"table-0"},"1330":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-11","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#properties","content":"Each `StatCardsStat` carries `values: { value, change, points }[]` — one entry per period, in the\nsame order as `periods` — where `value` is the number, `change` is the percent against the period\nbefore, and `points` is the sparkline oldest first."},"1331":{"id":"/docs/components/stat-cards-12","page_id":"/docs/components/stat-cards","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/stat-cards#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the cards are squared off with hairline borders; in Soft they are rounded panels with a\nsofter shadow. The sparkline colours fall back to the chart palette (the accent, then violet, green\nand orange) unless a card sets its own `color`."},"1332":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","type":"page","content":"Status pill","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/status-pill"},"1333":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-0","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill","content":"One live line for what an agent is doing right now, fading between its states and resizing to fit them."},"1334":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-1","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/status-pill#usage","content":"Usage"},"1335":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-2","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"Properties"},"1336":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-3","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/status-pill#theming","content":"Theming"},"1337":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-4","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill","content":"A status pill shows a single line of what the agent is up to. Its `state` picks the glyph and\ncolour — `thinking`, `reading` and `working` shimmer while they run — and a new `state`, `label`,\n`file` or `action` fades the old line out before the new one arrives. The `bar` variant is taller\nand draws a `progress` track along its bottom."},"1338":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-5","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                        |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `label` | `string` | What the agent is doing, in a few words. Required. |","table":"table-0"},"1339":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-6","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                                        | Description                                                                             |\n| ------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `state` | `idle \\| thinking \\| reading \\| working \\| waiting \\| done` | Picks the glyph and colour. `thinking`, `reading` and `working` shimmer while they run. |","table":"table-0"},"1340":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-7","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `meta` | `string` | Quiet detail after the label, like \"2 of 4\". Changing only this does not restart the pill. |","table":"table-0"},"1341":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-8","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"| Name   | Type                              | Description                  |\n| ------ | --------------------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `file` | `{ name: string; type?: string }` | A file chip after the label. |","table":"table-0"},"1342":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-9","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                                     | Description                                               |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `action` | `{ label: string; onClick: () => void }` | A button at the end, for when the agent needs the person. |","table":"table-0"},"1343":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-10","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| ---------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `progress` | `number` | 0 to 100, drawn as a track along the bottom of the `bar` variant. |","table":"table-0"},"1344":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-11","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#properties","content":"| Name      | Type          | Description                                                                      |\n| --------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `variant` | `pill \\| bar` | `pill` hugs its content; `bar` is taller and leaves room for the progress track. |","table":"table-0"},"1345":{"id":"/docs/components/status-pill-12","page_id":"/docs/components/status-pill","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/status-pill#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The pill\nsits on a surface with the shared shadow, so it picks up the theme's surface and token colours; in\nSoft it is rounder, and in dark it reads against the dark stage."},"1346":{"id":"/docs/components/steering","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","type":"page","content":"Steering","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Review and approve"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/steering"},"1347":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-0","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering","content":"Change the agent's course while it works, without starting over."},"1348":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-1","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/steering#usage","content":"Usage"},"1349":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-2","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"Properties"},"1350":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-3","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/steering#theming","content":"Theming"},"1351":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-4","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering","content":"Steering shows a run you can nudge while it works: its `steps`, the log of what you told it and\nwhat it said back, and a message box. A message waits for the step in progress, then the agent\ntakes it up from the next one — so you change its course without starting over. When your steer\ntouches work already done, the agent raises an amber heads-up with `actions` (like *Leave it* or\n*Redo the Pro card*) and settles on an `answer` once you choose."},"1352":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-5","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                       |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The run's goal, like \"Redesign the pricing page\". |","table":"table-0"},"1353":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-6","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name    | Type          | Description                                               |\n| ------- | ------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `SteerStep[]` | The steps of the run, each `queued`, `running` or `done`. |","table":"table-0"},"1354":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-7","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name       | Type             | Description                                           |\n| ---------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `messages` | `SteerMessage[]` | What you sent and what the agent said back, in order. |","table":"table-0"},"1355":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-8","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name     | Type             | Description                                                                                                          |\n| -------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSend` | `(text) => void` | Called with the text when a message is sent. Add it to `messages` as `queued`, then mark it `applied` once taken up. |","table":"table-0"},"1356":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-9","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `value` | `string` | The message being written. Leave it out to let the box keep its own draft. |","table":"table-0"},"1357":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-10","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                  |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(value) => void` | Called as the draft changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1358":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-11","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                                                       |\n| ------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | Defaults to \"Steer the agent while it works\", and \"The run has finished\" once every step is done. |","table":"table-0"},"1359":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-12","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| -------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The line under the title. Defaults to \"Step 2 of 4\", or \"Done\". |","table":"table-0"},"1360":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-13","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                              |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds to show as `m:ss`. Leave it out to let the clock count until every step is done. |","table":"table-0"},"1361":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-14","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name      | Type              | Description                                                                                      |\n| --------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `summary` | `string \\| false` | Shown once every step is done. Defaults to \"Done in 0:14 · 1 change from you\"; `false` hides it. |","table":"table-0"},"1362":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-15","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name        | Type                                       | Description                                  |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `SteerStep` | `{ id; title; detail?; status; fromYou? }` | A step; `fromYou` tags one your steer added. |","table":"table-0"},"1363":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-16","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                                                   | Description                                                                   |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `SteerMessage` | `{ id; from; text; state?; warn?; actions?; answer? }` | A log line; the agent's can carry an amber `warn`, `actions` and an `answer`. |","table":"table-0"},"1364":{"id":"/docs/components/steering-17","page_id":"/docs/components/steering","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/steering#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the panel shadow; the running glyph spins in the accent, a done step turns\nthe tick green, your messages sit in a chip bubble on the right, and the agent's heads-up tints\namber until you answer it. All colours, radii and spacing come from the theme tokens, so in Soft the\ncard, pills and message box are rounder."},"1365":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","type":"page","content":"Step Loader","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/step-loader"},"1366":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-0","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader","content":"A named-steps progress list with a loader beside the running step, a track that fills as steps finish, and an expandable list of every step."},"1367":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-1","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/step-loader#usage","content":"Usage"},"1368":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-2","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/step-loader#properties","content":"Properties"},"1369":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-3","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/step-loader#theming","content":"Theming"},"1370":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-4","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader","content":"A step loader shows an agent's work as named steps. The step running now sits beside a small\nloader; a track below fills as steps finish; and the row expands to the full list, each line\nswitching to its `done` text once complete. When `current` reaches the number of steps, every step\nis done and the row shows the `doneLabel`."},"1371":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-5","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                 | Description                                                                           |\n| ------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `{ label: string; done?: string }[]` | The steps. `label` shows while running, `done` once finished (falls back to `label`). |","table":"table-0"},"1372":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-6","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                     |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `current` | `number` | Index of the step running now. `steps.length` or more means every step is done. |","table":"table-0"},"1373":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-7","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                            | Description                                                   |\n| -------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `loader` | `radar \\| dots \\| ring \\| bars` | The loader glyph beside the running step. `radar` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1374":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-8","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `doneLabel` | `string` | Label once every step is done. `Ready for review` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-9","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                                               |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether the full list is open. Leave `open` out to let the row toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-10","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader#properties","content":"| Name           | Type       | Description                                  |\n| -------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `callback` | Fires when the row opens or closes the list. |","table":"table-0"},"1377":{"id":"/docs/components/step-loader-11","page_id":"/docs/components/step-loader","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/step-loader#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ntrack and loader take the accent color from the active theme; in Soft the row and track are softer\nand more rounded than in Blueprint."},"1378":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","type":"page","content":"Task table","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/task-table"},"1379":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-0","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table","content":"Agent tasks in a sortable table with bulk actions."},"1380":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-1","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/task-table#usage","content":"Usage"},"1381":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-2","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"Properties"},"1382":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-3","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/task-table#theming","content":"Theming"},"1383":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-4","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table","content":"Agent tasks in a table you can sort by any column. Pick rows with the checkboxes — or the\nselect-all in the header — and the header turns into what you can do to the selection: `pause`,\n`retry` or `cancel`. Rows glide to their new places when the order changes, cancelled rows slide\naway, and when the last task is gone the table says so."},"1384":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-5","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                                           |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tasks` | `Task[]` | The tasks to show. Each has an `id`, `name`, `status`, `agent`, `cost` and `updated`. |","table":"table-0"},"1385":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-6","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                          |\n| ------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The name in the header. Defaults to `\"Agent tasks\"`. |","table":"table-0"},"1386":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-7","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                            |\n| --------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `summary` | `string` | The quiet line beside the name. Defaults to a count of tasks and how many are running. |","table":"table-0"},"1387":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-8","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name                           | Type       | Description                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `selected` / `defaultSelected` | `string[]` | The ids of the selected tasks. Leave `selected` out to let the checkboxes and rows drive it. |","table":"table-0"},"1388":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-9","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name               | Type            | Description                        |\n| ------------------ | --------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onSelectedChange` | `(ids) => void` | Called when the selection changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1389":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-10","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type             | Description                                                             |\n| ---------------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sort` / `defaultSort` | `{ key; desc? }` | The column the rows are sorted by. Defaults to `updated`, newest first. |","table":"table-0"},"1390":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-11","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                         |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `onSortChange` | `(sort) => void` | Called when a header sets the sort. |","table":"table-0"},"1391":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-12","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name       | Type                    | Description                                                                                                     |\n| ---------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onAction` | `(action, ids) => void` | A bulk action (`pause` \\| `retry` \\| `cancel`). The selection clears after it; cancelled rows slide away first. |","table":"table-0"},"1392":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-13","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"| Name                    | Type                               | Description                                                          |\n| ----------------------- | ---------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `empty` / `emptyAction` | `ReactNode` / `{ label; onClick }` | What shows when there are no tasks, and an optional button under it. |","table":"table-0"},"1393":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-14","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#properties","content":"`Task.status` is one of `running`, `failed`, `queued`, `paused` or `done`. `Task.agent` is\n`{ name, initials, color }`, where `color` is an avatar token like `var(--vo-av-b)`."},"1394":{"id":"/docs/components/task-table-15","page_id":"/docs/components/task-table","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/task-table#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface and every colour comes from the theme tokens: the status pills tint from the\naccent (Running), `--vo-ok` (Done) and `--vo-bad` (Failed), with Queued and Paused staying muted;\nthe checkbox fills with the accent and its tick springs in. The table reflows into a stacked layout\ninside a narrow card via a container query, so it reads on a phone as well as full width."},"1395":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","type":"page","content":"Terminal stream","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Sources and output"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream"},"1396":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-0","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","content":"Shell commands the agent runs, with their output as it streams in."},"1397":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-1","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#usage","content":"Usage"},"1398":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-2","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"Properties"},"1399":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-3","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#theming","content":"Theming"},"1400":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-4","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","content":"A compact terminal for the shell commands an agent runs: the working directory and how the run is\ngoing in the header, each command with its output streaming in under it and an exit code or a check\nwith how long it took, and a summary at the foot once it is over. Notes and edits sit between the\ncommands — a note the agent writes about what went wrong, and the edit that fixes it. Long output\nfolds to its last lines. The terminal keeps one height (420px) and its output scrolls, staying on\nthe newest line unless the reader has scrolled up."},"1401":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-5","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                    |\n| ----- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cwd` | `string` | The working directory, shown in the header, like `~/acme/web`. |","table":"table-0"},"1402":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-6","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name      | Type              | Description                              |\n| --------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| `entries` | `TerminalEntry[]` | Commands, notes and edits, oldest first. |","table":"table-0"},"1403":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-7","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                                     | Description                                                   |\n| -------- | ---------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `running \\| passed \\| failed \\| stopped` | The run as a whole. Left out, it is derived from the entries. |","table":"table-0"},"1404":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-8","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                       |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `elapsed` | `string` | How long the run has taken, like `0:18`. Shown beside Running and in the summary. |","table":"table-0"},"1405":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-9","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name      | Type              | Description                                                  |\n| --------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `summary` | `string \\| false` | The line at the foot once the run is over. `false` hides it. |","table":"table-0"},"1406":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-10","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                |\n| ------ | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `tail` | `number` | How many lines a folded output keeps showing. Default `4`. |","table":"table-0"},"1407":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-11","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name     | Type         | Description                                  |\n| -------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `onStop` | `() => void` | Adds the Stop button while the run is going. |","table":"table-0"},"1408":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-12","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name     | Type             | Description                                          |\n| -------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onCopy` | `(text) => void` | Called with the whole run as text when it is copied. |","table":"table-0"},"1409":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-13","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| --------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `entry.command` | `string` | A command, like `npm run build`, with its `output` and `status`. |","table":"table-0"},"1410":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-14","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                            | Description                                        |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `entry.output` | `(string \\| { text; tone? })[]` | What it printed; `tone` is `ok`, `bad` or `muted`. |","table":"table-0"},"1411":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-15","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                                 | Description                                            |\n| -------------- | ------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `entry.status` | `running \\| ok \\| failed \\| stopped` | A spinner, a check, an `Exit N` tag, or a Stopped tag. |","table":"table-0"},"1412":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-16","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                                        |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `note.text` | `string` | A line from the agent between commands. The newest shimmers while the run goes on. |","table":"table-0"},"1413":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-17","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                             |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `edit.file` | `string` | A file the agent edits, with its `added`/`removed` counts and a `diff`. |","table":"table-0"},"1414":{"id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream-18","page_id":"/docs/components/terminal-stream","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/terminal-stream#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The output\nis 12px monospace on a 1.8 line height, the state tag and left rail take the accent while the run is\nlive and turn green or red once it is over, and a block cursor blinks after the newest line — all drawn\nfrom the theme tokens. In the Blueprint style the rail thins and the cursor marches; Soft rounds the\ncorners and the scrollbar."},"1415":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","type":"page","content":"Thinking States","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking-states"},"1416":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-0","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states","content":"Ten animated indicators, each a small mark beside a status line that steps through what an agent is doing, with an optional elapsed-seconds counter."},"1417":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-1","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#usage","content":"Usage"},"1418":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-2","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#properties","content":"Properties"},"1419":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-3","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#theming","content":"Theming"},"1420":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-4","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states","content":"A thinking state is a small animated mark beside a status line. Pick one of ten marks with\n`variant`; give it `steps` and, with more than one, they take turns every `interval` unless you\ndrive the index with `current`. An elapsed-seconds counter sits at the end of the line and counts\nby itself unless you set `seconds` or hide it with `seconds={false}`."},"1421":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-5","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states","content":"The marks are `orbit` (a light running round a ring, the line shimmering), `morph` (a rectangle,\ncircle and triangle in turn), `scan` (a column sweeping rows of dots), `stream` (dots filling in,\nthe line typed out behind a caret), `matrix` (a dot grid twinkling at random), `stack` (pages\nshuffling to the front), `pulse` (a core breathing with sonar rings growing out of it), `wave`\n(bars rising and falling in a travelling waveform), `bounce` (three dots hopping in turn) and\n`spiral` (dots lighting up along an inward spiral toward the centre)."},"1422":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-6","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                                                                                       | Description                                  |\n| --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `variant` | `orbit \\| morph \\| scan \\| stream \\| matrix \\| stack \\| pulse \\| wave \\| bounce \\| spiral` | Which indicator to draw. `orbit` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1423":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-7","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#properties","content":"| Name    | Type       | Description                                                                   |\n| ------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `string[]` | The status lines. With more than one they take turns unless `current` is set. |","table":"table-0"},"1424":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-8","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                                        |\n| --------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `current` | `number` | Index of the line to show. Leave it out to let the lines take turns by themselves. |","table":"table-0"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-9","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| ---------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `interval` | `number` | Milliseconds each line shows for when they take turns. `2600` by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1426":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-10","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#properties","content":"| Name      | Type              | Description                                                                             |\n| --------- | ----------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number \\| false` | Seconds shown at the end of the line. Counts by itself when left out; `false` hides it. |","table":"table-0"},"1427":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-states-11","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking-states","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking-states#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nmarks and the typed line use the active theme's accent and text colors; the counter is set in the\nnumeric style. Motion is paused for readers who prefer reduced motion — the line is shown whole\nrather than typed."},"1428":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","type":"page","content":"Thinking","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking"},"1429":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-0","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking","content":"The live trace an agent writes as it works, each step turning green as it finishes, then folded away into a summary."},"1430":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-1","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking#usage","content":"Usage"},"1431":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-2","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"Properties"},"1432":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-3","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thinking#theming","content":"Theming"},"1433":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-4","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking","content":"A thinking trace is the reasoning log an agent writes as it works. Each step arrives on a line that\nspins while it runs and turns into a green check once it finishes, with what it found written under\nit and how long it took at its right. The header counts seconds while it runs; once the last step\nlands it becomes a summary of the work and the trace folds itself away."},"1434":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-5","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                                                                                                                           |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `steps` | `ThinkingStep[]` | The steps the agent has taken so far. Each has a `label`, a `state` of `running`, `retry` or `done`, an optional `result` and `time`. |","table":"table-0"},"1435":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-6","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"| Name      | Type      | Description                                                |\n| --------- | --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `running` | `boolean` | Spins, counts seconds and keeps the trace open while true. |","table":"table-0"},"1436":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-7","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds to show. Leave it out to let it count while running. |","table":"table-0"},"1437":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-8","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The header while it runs, like \"Checking the pricing page\". |","table":"table-0"},"1438":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-9","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                  |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `summary` | `string` | The header once it is done. Defaults to the number of steps. |","table":"table-0"},"1439":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-10","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"| Name               | Type      | Description                                      |\n| ------------------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `collapseWhenDone` | `boolean` | Folds the trace away a moment after it finishes. |","table":"table-0"},"1440":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-11","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#properties","content":"| Name                   | Type      | Description                                                              |\n| ---------------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `open` / `defaultOpen` | `boolean` | Whether the trace is open. Leave `open` out to let the header toggle it. |","table":"table-0"},"1441":{"id":"/docs/components/thinking-12","page_id":"/docs/components/thinking","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thinking#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nrunning step turns in the accent with a soft halo, finished steps and the rail between them turn\ngreen, and a slow step waits in amber. In Blueprint the marks are squared off and the result writes\nin with a plain fade instead of a blur."},"1442":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","type":"page","content":"Thread panel","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thread-panel"},"1443":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-0","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel","content":"Switch between agent threads and reply in place."},"1444":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-1","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#usage","content":"Usage"},"1445":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-2","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"Properties"},"1446":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-3","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#theming","content":"Theming"},"1447":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-4","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel","content":"A thread panel holds several conversations with an agent, one tab each, with a reply field\nunder the open one. The tabs switch which thread is shown and an underline slides to the open\none; switching staggers that thread's messages in, and a later message glides into view. Each\n`agent` message can carry `sources` — the files or pages it used — and a `thinking` message\nshimmers while the agent works on a reply."},"1448":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-5","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name      | Type       | Description                      |\n| --------- | ---------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `threads` | `Thread[]` | The conversations, one tab each. |","table":"table-0"},"1449":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-6","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                        |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `value` | `string` | The id of the open thread. Leave it out to let the tabs switch it. |","table":"table-0"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-7","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultValue` | `string` | The thread open at first when uncontrolled. Defaults to the first thread. |","table":"table-0"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-8","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name            | Type           | Description                             |\n| --------------- | -------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| `onValueChange` | `(id) => void` | Called when a tab opens another thread. |","table":"table-0"},"1452":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-9","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name     | Type                       | Description                                                                                |\n| -------- | -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSend` | `(text, threadId) => void` | Called with the reply and the open thread's id. Add the message to that thread to show it. |","table":"table-0"},"1453":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-10","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                          |\n| ------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `draft` | `string` | The reply being written. Leave it out to let the field keep its own. |","table":"table-0"},"1454":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-11","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                   |\n| -------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultDraft` | `string` | The reply written at first when uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"1455":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-12","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name            | Type             | Description                        |\n| --------------- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| `onDraftChange` | `(text) => void` | Called as the reply field changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1456":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-13","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `placeholder` | `string` | The reply field's placeholder. Defaults to `Reply to the agent`. |","table":"table-0"},"1457":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-14","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                         |\n| ------ | --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Sits flat in a chat column (the default). Set `false` to give it a card of its own. |","table":"table-0"},"1458":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-15","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                                                              |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `Thread.color` | `string` | The dot in front of the title, any CSS colour. Defaults to a quiet grey. |","table":"table-0"},"1459":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-16","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name                    | Type       | Description                                                    |\n| ----------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ThreadMessage.sources` | `Source[]` | Files or pages the agent used, shown as chips above its reply. |","table":"table-0"},"1460":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-17","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type      | Description                                               |\n| ------------------------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `ThreadMessage.thinking` | `boolean` | Shows a shimmering line while the agent works on a reply. |","table":"table-0"},"1461":{"id":"/docs/components/thread-panel-18","page_id":"/docs/components/thread-panel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/thread-panel#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nopen tab's underline uses the accent mark token and the reply field sits on a surface with an\ninset field line, so it reads against the dark stage; in Soft the field is rounder (squircle)."},"1462":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","type":"page","content":"Toast stack","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast-stack"},"1463":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-0","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack","content":"Agent notifications that stack into a deck and fan out on hover."},"1464":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-1","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#usage","content":"Usage"},"1465":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-2","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"Properties"},"1466":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-3","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#theming","content":"Theming"},"1467":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-4","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack","content":"A toast stack collects notifications into a deck: the newest sits in front, older ones peek out\nbehind it. Hover the deck — or move the focus into it — and it fans out into a readable list; move\naway and it folds back up. Each toast takes an `icon`, a `tone` for the badge colour, a `title`, an\noptional `detail` line and a `time`. Pass the toasts oldest-first; dismiss one with its close button."},"1468":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-5","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name     | Type           | Description                               |\n| -------- | -------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `toasts` | `StackToast[]` | Oldest first. The last one sits in front. |","table":"table-0"},"1469":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-6","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name        | Type           | Description                                                                                |\n| ----------- | -------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onDismiss` | `(id) => void` | Called when a toast's close button is pressed. Remove it from `toasts` and it slides away. |","table":"table-0"},"1470":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-7","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name       | Type      | Description                                                              |\n| ---------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `expanded` | `boolean` | Fans the stack out. Leave it out to fan it while the pointer is over it. |","table":"table-0"},"1471":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-8","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name  | Type     | Description                                                                  |\n| ----- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `max` | `number` | How many toasts stay mounted. Older ones drop off the back. Defaults to `6`. |","table":"table-0"},"1472":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-9","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name       | Type               | Description                                                           |\n| ---------- | ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toast.id` | `string \\| number` | Identity of the toast; a new one rises in, a removed one slides away. |","table":"table-0"},"1473":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-10","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name         | Type       | Description                  |\n| ------------ | ---------- | ---------------------------- |\n| `toast.icon` | `IconName` | The icon in the round badge. |","table":"table-0"},"1474":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-11","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                                                           | Description                               |\n| ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `toast.tone` | `neutral \\| ok \\| warn \\| bad \\| merge \\| blue \\| purple \\| …` | Colours the badge. Defaults to `neutral`. |","table":"table-0"},"1475":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-12","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description          |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `toast.title` | `string` | The bold first line. |","table":"table-0"},"1476":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-13","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name           | Type     | Description                     |\n| -------------- | -------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `toast.detail` | `string` | The quiet line under the title. |","table":"table-0"},"1477":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-14","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                                                    |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `toast.time` | `string` | A short time like `now` or `2m`, shown until the close button takes its place. |","table":"table-0"},"1478":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-stack-15","page_id":"/docs/components/toast-stack","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast-stack#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each toast\nsits on a surface with the toast shadow and its badge tint comes from the theme tokens, so the deck\nreads against the dark stage; in Soft the cards are rounder. The fan-out and the arrival and dismiss\nmotion are tuned down when the viewer prefers reduced motion."},"1479":{"id":"/docs/components/toast","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","type":"page","content":"Toast","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast"},"1480":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-0","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast","content":"One toast at a time — a new one rises in while the last one slips away."},"1481":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-1","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast#usage","content":"Usage"},"1482":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-2","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"Properties"},"1483":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-3","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/toast#theming","content":"Theming"},"1484":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-4","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast","content":"A toast is a short message on a surface. Its `tone` picks the icon and colour — `loading` spins —\nand it takes a `title`, an optional `description` and an optional `action` button. Pass a new `id`\nto slide a new toast in and the old one away; keep the same `id` to change the text in place."},"1485":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-5","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                | Description                            |\n| ------- | ------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| `toast` | `ToastData \\| null` | The toast to show, or `null` for none. |","table":"table-0"},"1486":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-6","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"| Name        | Type           | Description                                              |\n| ----------- | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onDismiss` | `(id) => void` | Called by the close button. The toast leaves either way. |","table":"table-0"},"1487":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-7","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"| Name       | Type               | Description                                                                           |\n| ---------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toast.id` | `string \\| number` | A new id slides a new toast in and the old one away. Keep it to change text in place. |","table":"table-0"},"1488":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-8","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                                  | Description                                     |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `toast.tone` | `success \\| error \\| info \\| loading` | Picks the icon and its colour. `loading` spins. |","table":"table-0"},"1489":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-9","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description          |\n| ------------- | -------- | -------------------- |\n| `toast.title` | `string` | The bold first line. |","table":"table-0"},"1490":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-10","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"| Name                | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toast.description` | `string` | The quieter line under the title. Crossfades when it changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1491":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-11","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                                                           | Description                                           |\n| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `toast.action` | `{ label; onClick; variant?: ghost \\| primary \\| ink; busy? }` | A button before the close button, like Undo or Retry. |","table":"table-0"},"1492":{"id":"/docs/components/toast-12","page_id":"/docs/components/toast","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/toast#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the toast shadow and its tone tints come from the theme tokens, so it reads\nagainst the dark stage; in Soft the card and its buttons are rounder."},"1493":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","type":"page","content":"Tool call","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tool-call"},"1494":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-0","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call","content":"Each tool the agent calls, with its input and output."},"1495":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-1","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tool-call#usage","content":"Usage"},"1496":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-2","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"Properties"},"1497":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-3","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tool-call#theming","content":"Theming"},"1498":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-4","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call","content":"The tools an agent calls, shown between its message and its answer. Each call takes a `server`,\na `name` and a `state` — `queued` waits, `running` spins, `done` shows how long it took and what\ncame back. Click a call to fold its `input` and `output` open or shut. The `reply` fades in once\nevery call is done."},"1499":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-5","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name      | Type        | Description                           |\n| --------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `message` | `ReactNode` | The agent's message before the calls. |","table":"table-0"},"1500":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-6","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                                             |\n| ------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `calls` | `ToolCallItem[]` | The tools the agent called, each a row that folds open. |","table":"table-0"},"1501":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-7","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name    | Type        | Description                                                              |\n| ------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `reply` | `ReactNode` | The agent's answer after the calls. It fades in once every call is done. |","table":"table-0"},"1502":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-8","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name   | Type       | Description                                                                   |\n| ------ | ---------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `string[]` | Keys of the calls that are open. Leave it out to let each call toggle itself. |","table":"table-0"},"1503":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-9","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name          | Type       | Description                                          |\n| ------------- | ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultOpen` | `string[]` | The calls open at first when `open` is uncontrolled. |","table":"table-0"},"1504":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-10","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                       | Description                                              |\n| -------------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` | `(open: string[]) => void` | Called with the new open set whenever a call is toggled. |","table":"table-0"},"1505":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-11","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                     |\n| ------------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `call.server` | `string` | The tool's server or namespace, like `billing`. |","table":"table-0"},"1506":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-12","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                |\n| ----------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `call.name` | `string` | The tool's name, like `list_plan_changes`. |","table":"table-0"},"1507":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-13","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name        | Type       | Description                    |\n| ----------- | ---------- | ------------------------------ |\n| `call.icon` | `IconName` | The icon in front of the call. |","table":"table-0"},"1508":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-14","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name         | Type                        | Description                                                        |\n| ------------ | --------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `call.state` | `queued \\| running \\| done` | `queued` waits, `running` spins, `done` shows the time and output. |","table":"table-0"},"1509":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-15","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name            | Type     | Description                                       |\n| --------------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| `call.duration` | `string` | How long it took, like `412 ms`. Shown once done. |","table":"table-0"},"1510":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-16","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name         | Type   | Description                                     |\n| ------------ | ------ | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `call.input` | `Json` | What the agent sent, shown as highlighted JSON. |","table":"table-0"},"1511":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-17","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#properties","content":"| Name          | Type   | Description                      |\n| ------------- | ------ | -------------------------------- |\n| `call.output` | `Json` | What came back, shown once done. |","table":"table-0"},"1512":{"id":"/docs/components/tool-call-18","page_id":"/docs/components/tool-call","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tool-call#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The call\nrows sit on the stage with a chip-tinted icon badge and chip-tinted JSON blocks; keys, strings and\nnumbers take their own palette tokens, and the running spinner and fold motion follow the shared\nease. In Soft the rows and JSON blocks are rounder."},"1513":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","type":"page","content":"Tooltip","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Core"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tooltip"},"1514":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-0","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip","content":"A toolbar whose labels wait a moment, then follow the pointer instantly between buttons, with a richer hover card for people."},"1515":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-1","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tooltip#usage","content":"Usage"},"1516":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-2","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"Properties"},"1517":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-3","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tooltip#theming","content":"Theming"},"1518":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-4","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip","content":"A tooltip is the label that waits a moment under a toolbar button, then follows the pointer\ninstantly as it moves between them. Buttons come in `groups` with a line between, each with a `tip`\nand an optional shortcut (`kbd`). Avatars at the end get a richer card instead — a person's name,\nrole and what they are doing now, with an agent shown by its thinking dots."},"1519":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-5","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"| Name     | Type              | Description                                                                                                      |\n| -------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `groups` | `TooltipTool[][]` | The toolbar's buttons, in groups with a line between. Each tool is `{ key, icon, label, tip?, kbd?, onClick? }`. |","table":"table-0"},"1520":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-6","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"| Name     | Type              | Description                                                                                                      |\n| -------- | ----------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `people` | `TooltipPerson[]` | Avatars at the end. Each is `{ key, initials, color, name, role, status, working? }`; hovering one shows a card. |","table":"table-0"},"1521":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-7","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"| Name   | Type        | Description                     |\n| ------ | ----------- | ------------------------------- |\n| `note` | `ReactNode` | A quiet line under the toolbar. |","table":"table-0"},"1522":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-8","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `cardDelay` | `number` | How long a person card waits before it shows. Defaults to `300`. |","table":"table-0"},"1523":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-9","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"| Name      | Type             | Description                                                                          |\n| --------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `openTip` | `string \\| null` | Shows this tool's tip by key, as if hovered. Leave it out to let the pointer decide. |","table":"table-0"},"1524":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-10","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"| Name       | Type             | Description                                     |\n| ---------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| `openCard` | `string \\| null` | Shows this person's card by key, as if hovered. |","table":"table-0"},"1525":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-11","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#properties","content":"A tool's `tip` overrides its `label` in the tooltip, so set it only when the tip should say more\nthan the button's name; the `kbd` shortcut is shown after it. A person's `working: true` swaps the\ngreen status dot for the agent's thinking dots."},"1526":{"id":"/docs/components/tooltip-12","page_id":"/docs/components/tooltip","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tooltip#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bar and card are squared off with hairline borders; in Soft they are rounded panels.\nThe tooltip itself and the avatar colours (`--vo-av-*`) come from the theme, so they stay legible on\neither background."},"1527":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","type":"page","content":"Top pages","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Charts and tables"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/top-pages"},"1528":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-0","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages","content":"Most visited pages with share of traffic and a quick sort."},"1529":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-1","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/top-pages#usage","content":"Usage"},"1530":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-2","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"Properties"},"1531":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-3","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/top-pages#theming","content":"Theming"},"1532":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-4","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages","content":"A ranked list of a site's most visited pages. Each row shows its rank, title and path, a share bar\nagainst the busiest page, the view count and the percent change (green from `0`, red below). The\nrunning total rolls up, and the `Views` / `Change` sort switch slides the rows into their new order."},"1533":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-5","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name    | Type             | Description                                                    |\n| ------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `pages` | `TopPagesPage[]` | The page rows. Each has `path`, `title`, `views` and `change`. |","table":"table-0"},"1534":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-6","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                           |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | Header text. Defaults to `Top pages`. |","table":"table-0"},"1535":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-7","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                           |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| `period` | `string` | After the total, like `last 30 days`. |","table":"table-0"},"1536":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-8","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                   |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `site` | `string` | Put in front of each path in the row tips, like `visuno.dev`. |","table":"table-0"},"1537":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-9","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name   | Type              | Description                                                         |\n| ------ | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `sort` | `views \\| change` | How the rows are ordered. Leave it out to let the switch change it. |","table":"table-0"},"1538":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-10","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name          | Type              | Description                                                  |\n| ------------- | ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `defaultSort` | `views \\| change` | The order before the switch is touched. Defaults to `views`. |","table":"table-0"},"1539":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-11","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name           | Type             | Description                         |\n| -------------- | ---------------- | ----------------------------------- |\n| `onSortChange` | `(sort) => void` | Fires when the sort switch changes. |","table":"table-0"},"1540":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-12","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                           |\n| ----------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| `page.path` | `string` | The page's path, like `/pricing`. Also the row's key. |","table":"table-0"},"1541":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-13","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description               |\n| ------------ | -------- | ------------------------- |\n| `page.title` | `string` | Its name, like `Pricing`. |","table":"table-0"},"1542":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-14","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name         | Type     | Description                                                       |\n| ------------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `page.views` | `number` | Views over the period; the share bar is against the busiest page. |","table":"table-0"},"1543":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-15","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| ------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `page.change` | `number` | Change in percent, like `24` or `-8`. Green from `0`, red below. |","table":"table-0"},"1544":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-16","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                  |\n| ---------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| `page.tip` | `string` | Shown on hover. Defaults to `site` + `path`. |","table":"table-0"},"1545":{"id":"/docs/components/top-pages-17","page_id":"/docs/components/top-pages","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/top-pages#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the shared shadow; the share bars use the accent mark token, the change chips\nthe `ok` / `bad` tints, and the ranks the mono font — all from the theme tokens, so the list reads\nthe same against either background. In Soft the card and the sort switch are rounder."},"1546":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","type":"page","content":"Trace view","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/trace-view"},"1547":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-0","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view","content":"One agent run as an observability waterfall — every span on a shared time axis, nested under the span that started it, with its tokens and latency."},"1548":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-1","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/trace-view#usage","content":"Usage"},"1549":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-2","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"Properties"},"1550":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-3","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/trace-view#theming","content":"Theming"},"1551":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-4","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view","content":"A trace view lays one agent run out as a waterfall. Every span — an LLM call, a tool call, a\nretrieval, a sub-agent — sits on a shared time axis, nested under the span that started it with a\ntree's guides. Each kind has its own colour, counted in the key. While the run streams, a playhead\nmarks now and running bars glow at their leading edge; a tool call that runs over its budget turns\namber and hatched and is tagged slow. Open any span to see where it sat in the run, its input, its\noutput, its latency and its tokens."},"1552":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-5","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                 |\n| ------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| `title` | `string` | The run's name, shown over the status line. |","table":"table-0"},"1553":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-6","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name    | Type          | Description                                                            |\n| ------- | ------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `spans` | `TraceSpan[]` | The run's top spans, usually one root with everything nested under it. |","table":"table-0"},"1554":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-7","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                                                                                   |\n| ------ | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `time` | `number` | Seconds into the run while it streams in. Spans that start later stay hidden, running ones reach this far. Leave it out once the run is over. |","table":"table-0"},"1555":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-8","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                                               |\n| ------ | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `axis` | `number` | Seconds the time axis covers. Defaults to the run's length, rounded up to a whole second. |","table":"table-0"},"1556":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-9","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name        | Type     | Description                                                                              |\n| ----------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `slowAfter` | `number` | A tool call longer than this many seconds turns amber and is tagged slow. Defaults to 2. |","table":"table-0"},"1557":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-10","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                                |\n| -------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `status` | `string` | Overrides the status line. Defaults to \"Running · 4 spans\", then \"Done · 7 spans, 1 slow\". |","table":"table-0"},"1558":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-11","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name       | Type     | Description                                                                        |\n| ---------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `selected` | `string` | The id of the open span, whose details show under the waterfall. null closes them. |","table":"table-0"},"1559":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-12","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"| Name                                  | Type       | Description                                                           |\n| ------------------------------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onSelectedChange` / `selectedChange` | `callback` | Fires with the id of the span opened, or null when the details close. |","table":"table-0"},"1560":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-13","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#properties","content":"A `TraceSpan` has an `id`, a `name`, a `kind` (agent, llm, tool, or retrieval), a `start` and\n`duration` in seconds, optional `tokens`, optional `input` and `output` strings, and optional\n`children`. An agent span without its own token count adds up every span under it."},"1561":{"id":"/docs/components/trace-view-14","page_id":"/docs/components/trace-view","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/trace-view#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bars square off and running bars switch from a sweeping sheen to a steady stripe. Each\nkind keeps its colour from the chart palette; a slow bar is amber and hatched in every theme."},"1562":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","type":"page","content":"Voice capture","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-capture"},"1563":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-0","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture","content":"Talk to the agent, then fix what it misheard before sending."},"1564":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-1","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#usage","content":"Usage"},"1565":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-2","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"Properties"},"1566":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-3","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#theming","content":"Theming"},"1567":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-4","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture","content":"Speech to text that shows what it heard as it hears it, and lets the person fix the words it was\nunsure of. Each word fades in as it arrives and the wave scrolls while it records. Press Done to\nmove from recording into review, where unsure words are highlighted — tap one to pick from a short\n\"Did you mean\" menu — then Done again to send, or Cancel to drop it. Once recording stops the box\nkeeps its height: the wave freezes as the whole recording and the words stay where they were."},"1568":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-5","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                         | Description                                                                            |\n| ------- | ---------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `words` | `Array<string \\| HeardWord>` | The words heard so far, in order. Add to the end as they arrive and each one fades in. |","table":"table-0"},"1569":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-6","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                                 | Description                                               |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `state` | `listening \\| paused \\| review \\| sent \\| cancelled` | The state. Leave it out to let the buttons move it along. |","table":"table-0"},"1570":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-7","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name           | Type                | Description                                                       |\n| -------------- | ------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `defaultState` | `VoiceCaptureState` | The state to start in when uncontrolled. Defaults to `listening`. |","table":"table-0"},"1571":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-8","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                      |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| `onStateChange` | `(state) => void` | Called whenever the state moves. |","table":"table-0"},"1572":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-9","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| --------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `seconds` | `number` | Seconds recorded. Leave it out to let it count while listening. |","table":"table-0"},"1573":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-10","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                       | Description                                                                                                                       |\n| ------- | -------------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `level` | `number \\| (() => number)` | The input level from 0 to 1, drawn into the wave about 20 times a second. Pass a function to read the microphone on every sample. |","table":"table-0"},"1574":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-11","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                            |\n| -------- | -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `status` | `string` | The status line. Defaults to Listening, Paused, Check what I heard, Sent or Cancelled. |","table":"table-0"},"1575":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-12","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name     | Type             | Description                                                        |\n| -------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `onSend` | `(text) => void` | Called with the checked transcript when Done is pressed in review. |","table":"table-0"},"1576":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-13","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                    | Description                                                |\n| ------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onFix` | `(index, text) => void` | Called when the person picks one of a word's alternatives. |","table":"table-0"},"1577":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-14","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name            | Type         | Description                                                    |\n| --------------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRecordAgain` | `() => void` | Called by Record again, once the capture is sent or cancelled. |","table":"table-0"},"1578":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-15","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name             | Type     | Description        |\n| ---------------- | -------- | ------------------ |\n| `HeardWord.text` | `string` | The word as heard. |","table":"table-0"},"1579":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-16","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#properties","content":"| Name                     | Type       | Description                                                                           |\n| ------------------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `HeardWord.alternatives` | `string[]` | What it might have been instead. Highlights the word and opens a \"Did you mean\" menu. |","table":"table-0"},"1580":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-capture-17","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-capture","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-capture#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface; the recording dot uses the `--vo-bad` tone and pulses, unsure words are tinted\nwith `--vo-hl` (and `--vo-hl-ok` once fixed), and the wave is drawn from the `--vo-fg2`, `--vo-faint`\nand `--vo-muted` tokens, so it reads in either theme. In Soft the panel and its buttons are rounder."},"1581":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","type":"page","content":"Voice orb","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Conversation"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-orb"},"1582":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-0","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb","content":"A hands-free voice chat, with an orb that shows who is talking."},"1583":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-1","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#usage","content":"Usage"},"1584":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-2","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"Properties"},"1585":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-3","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#theming","content":"Theming"},"1586":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-4","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb","content":"A hands-free voice chat on a card. The orb is a lit glass sphere that swells with whoever is\ntalking — the accent colour for you, violet for the agent — with what was said underneath and mute\nand end below. It draws what you pass through `state`, `level` and `caption`; it never opens the\nmicrophone itself. Talking while muted shows a notice, the way calls do."},"1587":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-5","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name    | Type                                                 | Description                                                  |\n| ------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `state` | `idle \\| listening \\| thinking \\| speaking \\| ended` | Where the chat is. `muted` while `listening` shows as Muted. |","table":"table-0"},"1588":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-6","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name    | Type     | Description                                                     |\n| ------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `level` | `number` | How loud whoever is talking is, 0 to 1. The orb swells with it. |","table":"table-0"},"1589":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-7","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name    | Type      | Description                                                                      |\n| ------- | --------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `muted` | `boolean` | Your microphone is off; the mute button is pressed and Listening reads as Muted. |","table":"table-0"},"1590":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-8","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name            | Type              | Description                                        |\n| --------------- | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onMutedChange` | `(muted) => void` | The mute button and the notice's Unmute call this. |","table":"table-0"},"1591":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-9","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name          | Type      | Description                                                                     |\n| ------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `mutedNotice` | `boolean` | Shows \"You're muted\" with an Unmute button, for when someone talks while muted. |","table":"table-0"},"1592":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-10","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name      | Type                     | Description                                                                    |\n| --------- | ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `caption` | `{ speaker; text; id? }` | What was said last and who said it. A new `id` (or speaker) starts a new line. |","table":"table-0"},"1593":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-11","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name   | Type     | Description                                                               |\n| ------ | -------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `hint` | `string` | Shown before anything is said, like \"Talk to the agent about Pricing v4\". |","table":"table-0"},"1594":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-12","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name      | Type     | Description                                      |\n| --------- | -------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `elapsed` | `number` | Seconds since the chat started, shown top right. |","table":"table-0"},"1595":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-13","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name                | Type         | Description             |\n| ------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------- |\n| `onStart` / `onEnd` | `() => void` | Start talking, and End. |","table":"table-0"},"1596":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-14","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name        | Type         | Description                                              |\n| ----------- | ------------ | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `onRestart` | `() => void` | Start again, from the row shown once the chat has ended. |","table":"table-0"},"1597":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-15","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name          | Type     | Description                                                                             |\n| ------------- | -------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `endedDetail` | `string` | The quiet line under \"Voice chat ended\". Defaults to the length and \"Transcript saved\". |","table":"table-0"},"1598":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-16","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                      |\n| -------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `labels` | `object` | Overrides for every bit of text (status words, buttons, notice). |","table":"table-0"},"1599":{"id":"/docs/components/voice-orb-17","page_id":"/docs/components/voice-orb","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/voice-orb#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The orb's\ncolours flow from the tokens: the accent is yours, `--vo-pl` (violet) is the agent, and the two are\nmixed in oklch so the step between them stays bright. The glass sphere is drawn on a canvas with\nWebGL where it can, falling back to layered gradients otherwise; with reduced motion it holds a\nsingle still frame and only redraws when the speaker changes."},"1600":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","type":"page","content":"Web search","breadcrumbs":["Library","Components","Agent status"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/web-search"},"1601":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-0","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search","content":"The agent's web searches as a trail — each query and what came back, each page read, skimmed or skipped and why, and an answer whose citations light their pages."},"1602":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-1","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/web-search#usage","content":"Usage"},"1603":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-2","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"Properties"},"1604":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-3","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/web-search#theming","content":"Theming"},"1605":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-4","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search","content":"Web search shows an agent researching out loud. Each query is a row with how many results came\nback and how long it took; a query that finds nothing is asked again in other words. Under each\nquery sit the pages it opened, each marked Read, Skimmed, or Skipped with the reason (paywall,\nblocked, timeout). Once the run is done the trail folds to one line and the answer streams in,\nits bracketed numbers pointing back at the pages that back them up."},"1606":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-5","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"| Name      | Type         | Description                                                                                                                          |\n| --------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `queries` | `WebQuery[]` | The searches, in order. Each has a key, the query text, a status, a result count, a time, an optional rewritten flag, and its pages. |","table":"table-0"},"1607":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-6","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                                    |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `done` | `boolean` | True once searching and reading are over. The trail folds to its summary line. |","table":"table-0"},"1608":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-7","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"| Name     | Type     | Description                                                                                                 |\n| -------- | -------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `answer` | `string` | The answer, with sources cited as numbers in brackets. Each number points at the page with that cite value. |","table":"table-0"},"1609":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-8","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                                           |\n| ------ | --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `open` | `boolean` | Whether the trail is open. Left out, it folds once `done` turns true. |","table":"table-0"},"1610":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-9","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"| Name                          | Type       | Description                               |\n| ----------------------------- | ---------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| `onOpenChange` / `openChange` | `callback` | Fires when the trail is opened or closed. |","table":"table-0"},"1611":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-10","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"| Name   | Type      | Description                                            |\n| ------ | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| `bare` | `boolean` | Without the panel, for a chat stream. True by default. |","table":"table-0"},"1612":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-11","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#properties","content":"A `WebPage` has a `title`, a `domain`, an optional `date`, a `status` (reading, read, skimmed,\npaywall, blocked, or timeout), and an optional `cite` number the answer refers to it by."},"1613":{"id":"/docs/components/web-search-12","page_id":"/docs/components/web-search","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/web-search#theming","content":"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Skipped\npages dim and their tag turns amber; a running page shows a spinner. The site initials stack on the\nheader, and hovering a citation lights the page that backs it up along with its site mark."},"1614":{"id":"/docs/faq","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"page","content":"FAQ","breadcrumbs":["Library"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq"},"1615":{"id":"/docs/faq-0","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Common questions about Visuno — frameworks, theming, licensing, and how the components ship."},"1616":{"id":"/docs/faq-1","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#general","content":"General"},"1617":{"id":"/docs/faq-2","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"Frameworks"},"1618":{"id":"/docs/faq-3","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#theming--styling","content":"Theming & styling"},"1619":{"id":"/docs/faq-4","page_id":"/docs/faq","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/faq#using-the-components","content":"Using the components"},"1620":{"id":"/docs/faq-5","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq","content":"Short answers to the questions that come up most. If something isn't covered here,\nopen an issue on GitHub."},"1621":{"id":"/docs/faq-6","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#general","content":"Visuno is an open-source UI component library for building **agent-powered products**.\nEvery component ships natively for **React**, **Angular**, and **Flutter**, built from one\nshared set of design tokens — so a component looks and behaves the same wherever you use it."},"1622":{"id":"/docs/faq-7","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#general","content":"Yes. Visuno is open source under the **MIT licence** — free for personal and commercial\nprojects, with no attribution required. See the components repository\nfor the full licence text."},"1623":{"id":"/docs/faq-8","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#general","content":"The React build is the reference implementation and is stable. Angular and Flutter are\nnative ports that mirror the same props and behaviour. As with any pre-1.0 library, pin a\nversion and read the changelog before upgrading."},"1624":{"id":"/docs/faq-9","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"Three, from a single design source:"},"1625":{"id":"/docs/faq-10","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"| Framework | Form                          | Package         |\n| --------- | ----------------------------- | --------------- |\n| **React** | `.tsx` components (React 18+) | `@visuno/react` |","table":"table-0"},"1626":{"id":"/docs/faq-11","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"| Framework   | Form                                                  | Package           |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ----------------- |\n| **Angular** | Standalone components (`vo-*` selectors, Angular 18+) | `@visuno/angular` |","table":"table-0"},"1627":{"id":"/docs/faq-12","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"| Framework   | Form                                  | Package             |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| **Flutter** | Dart widgets, themed to match the web | `visuno` on pub.dev |","table":"table-0"},"1628":{"id":"/docs/faq-13","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"The React version is the reference; Angular and Flutter mirror the same props and behaviour."},"1629":{"id":"/docs/faq-14","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"That's the goal — one design, three frameworks. React leads, and the Angular and Flutter\nports follow. Each component's docs page shows the code for every framework it currently\nships in, side by side."},"1630":{"id":"/docs/faq-15","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"React, Angular, and Flutter use their usual toolchains."},"1631":{"id":"/docs/faq-16","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#frameworks","content":"Yes. The React components are plain React 18+ components with no framework lock-in, so they\nwork in Next.js, Vite, Remix, or any React setup."},"1632":{"id":"/docs/faq-17","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#theming--styling","content":"Set `data-theme=\"dark\"` on a parent element (web), or use `Brightness.dark` in the Flutter\ntheme. Every component reads the same tokens, so your whole UI flips at once."},"1633":{"id":"/docs/faq-18","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#theming--styling","content":"The default **Blueprint** style is crisp and squared; **Soft** is rounded and plush. Switch\nto Soft on the web with `data-style=\"soft\"` on a parent element."},"1634":{"id":"/docs/faq-19","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#theming--styling","content":"Yes. Design tokens drive everything — `--vo-*` custom properties on the web, and\n`VoColors` / `VoSpace` / `VoRadius` in Flutter. Override a token once and the change flows\nthrough every component."},"1635":{"id":"/docs/faq-20","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#using-the-components","content":"Pick a component from the sidebar, copy the snippet for your framework, and drop it in.\nPull the shared core once (tokens + helpers), and every component you add after that just\nworks."},"1636":{"id":"/docs/faq-21","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#using-the-components","content":"Components are built with semantic markup, keyboard support, and reduced-motion handling\nwhere animation is involved. Accessibility notes specific to a component are called out on\nits docs page."},"1637":{"id":"/docs/faq-22","page_id":"/docs/faq","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/faq#using-the-components","content":"Open an issue on the issue tracker. Planned\nwork and what's shipped are tracked on the roadmap and\nchangelog."},"1638":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","type":"page","content":"Accessibility","breadcrumbs":["Library","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility"},"1639":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","content":"How Visuno components handle semantics, keyboard, focus, contrast, and reduced motion — and what's still on you."},"1640":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-the-components-do","content":"What the components do"},"1641":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-stays-on-you","content":"What stays on you"},"1642":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#per-component-notes","content":"Per-component notes"},"1643":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","content":"Agent interfaces move a lot: things stream in, states change, and panels open and close. Visuno\ncomponents are built so that motion and live updates don't lock anyone out. This page covers what the\nlibrary handles and what stays your responsibility."},"1644":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-the-components-do","content":"Components use the right element for the job — real `<button>`s for actions, headings and lists where\nthey belong, and ARIA roles only where native semantics fall short. Interactive controls expose a\nname, role, and state to assistive tech."},"1645":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-the-components-do","content":"Anything you can click, you can reach and operate from the keyboard. Focus order follows reading\norder, overlays (modals, popovers) trap focus while open and return it to the trigger on close, and\nEscape dismisses transient surfaces."},"1646":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-the-components-do","content":"Every interactive element has a visible focus ring drawn from the `--vo-focus` token, so keyboard\nusers can always see where they are. The ring respects the active theme and style."},"1647":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-the-components-do","content":"Components that animate — streaming status, shimmering states, fades between lines — honour\n`prefers-reduced-motion`. When a viewer asks their OS for less motion, animations are shortened or\nremoved and content simply appears, with no loss of information."},"1648":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-the-components-do","content":"Components that update on their own (status pills, toasts, live answers) announce changes through\nARIA live regions so screen-reader users hear what changed without having to go looking for it."},"1649":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-the-components-do","content":"The default light and dark themes are tuned to meet WCAG AA contrast for text and essential UI.\nMeaning is never carried by color alone — states also use a glyph, label, or shape."},"1650":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-stays-on-you","content":"The library gives you accessible building blocks; the composition is yours. A few things to get\nright in your app:"},"1651":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-stays-on-you","content":"**Labels and text alternatives** — give icon-only buttons an accessible name, and images and charts\na meaningful description for the data they show."},"1652":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-stays-on-you","content":"**Contrast of custom tokens** — if you override `--vo-*` colors (see Theming),\nre-check text and UI contrast against the new values."},"1653":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-stays-on-you","content":"**Heading structure** — keep a sensible heading order on the page around the components."},"1654":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#what-stays-on-you","content":"**Reading order** — place components in the DOM in the order you want them read and tabbed."},"1655":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#per-component-notes","content":"Accessibility details specific to a component — which keys it responds to, what it announces, how it\nbehaves under reduced motion — are called out in the **Theming** and usage sections of that\ncomponent's docs page."},"1656":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#per-component-notes","content":"<Card title=\"Theming\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/theming\" description=\"Tokens, dark mode, and the focus ring.\" />"},"1657":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/accessibility#per-component-notes","content":"<Card title=\"FAQ\" href=\"/docs/faq\" description=\"More short answers, including accessibility.\" />"},"1658":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"page","content":"Installation","breadcrumbs":["Library","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation"},"1659":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation","content":"Add Visuno to a React, Angular, or Flutter project — install the package, pull the shared core once, then drop in components."},"1660":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"1661":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#set-up","content":"Set up"},"1662":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#install-the-package","content":"Install the package"},"1663":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#pull-the-core","content":"Pull the core"},"1664":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#add-a-component","content":"Add a component"},"1665":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#install-the-package-1","content":"Install the package"},"1666":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#pull-the-core-1","content":"Pull the core"},"1667":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#add-a-component-1","content":"Add a component"},"1668":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#install-the-package-2","content":"Install the package"},"1669":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#apply-the-theme","content":"Apply the theme"},"1670":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#add-a-widget","content":"Add a widget"},"1671":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"1672":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation","content":"Visuno ships the same design across **React**, **Angular**, and **Flutter**. Whatever your stack, the\nshape is the same: **install the package**, **pull the shared core once** (design tokens + a little\nCSS/helpers), then add components one at a time. The React build is the reference; Angular and\nFlutter mirror its props and behaviour."},"1673":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#prerequisites","content":"| Framework | You need                                                   |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **React** | React 18+ and a bundler (Next.js, Vite, Remix — anything). |","table":"table-0"},"1674":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#prerequisites","content":"| Framework   | You need                                |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| **Angular** | Angular 18+ with standalone components. |","table":"table-0"},"1675":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#prerequisites","content":"| Framework   | You need             |\n| ----------- | -------------------- |\n| **Flutter** | Flutter 3+ (Dart 3). |","table":"table-0"},"1676":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#set-up","content":"Pick your framework. Each starts by installing the package, then pulling the shared core once."},"1677":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#set-up","content":"The React components are plain React 18+ components with no framework lock-in, so they work in\nNext.js, Vite, Remix, or any React setup."},"1678":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#pull-the-core","content":"Import the shared tokens and base styles **once**, near the root of your app (e.g. in `layout.tsx`\nor your global CSS entry):"},"1679":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#add-a-component","content":"Import the component and drop it in:"},"1680":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#add-a-component","content":"Components are **standalone** — import the one you need directly into your component's `imports`, no\nmodule boilerplate."},"1681":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#pull-the-core-1","content":"Add the token stylesheet to your global styles **once** (e.g. `styles.css`, or the `styles` array\nin `angular.json`):"},"1682":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-23","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#add-a-component-1","content":"The Flutter widgets are themed to match the web. Wrap your app in the Visuno theme once, then use\nthe widgets anywhere."},"1683":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-24","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#install-the-package-2","content":"Add it from the command line:"},"1684":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-25","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#install-the-package-2","content":"Or add it to your `pubspec.yaml` and run `flutter pub get`:"},"1685":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-26","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#apply-the-theme","content":"Wrap your app **once** so every widget inherits the shared tokens:"},"1686":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-27","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Theming\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/theming\" description=\"Dark mode, the two styles, and the token system.\" />"},"1687":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-28","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#next-steps","content":"<Card title=\"Browse components\" href=\"/docs/components/status-pill\" description=\"Live previews and code for every component.\" />"},"1688":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/installation-29","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/installation#next-steps","content":"Install the package and pull the core once, and every component you add after that just works — it\nreads the same tokens and inherits your theme automatically."},"1689":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","type":"page","content":"Theming","breadcrumbs":["Library","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/theming"},"1690":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming","content":"Two switches — dark mode and style — plus the shared --vo-* token system that drives every color, space, radius, and motion."},"1691":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#the-two-switches","content":"The two switches"},"1692":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#dark-mode","content":"Dark mode"},"1693":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#style","content":"Style"},"1694":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#the-token-system","content":"The token system"},"1695":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#override-a-token","content":"Override a token"},"1696":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#how-it-fits-together","content":"How it fits together"},"1697":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming","content":"Every Visuno component reads from one shared set of **design tokens**, so you theme the whole UI from\none place instead of styling components one by one. There are two switches everyone uses out of the\nbox — **dark mode** and **style** — and underneath them, the tokens you can override to make the\nlibrary your own."},"1698":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#the-two-switches","content":"On the web (React and Angular) both switches are attributes on a parent element; on Flutter they live\nin the theme object. Every component below the switch responds at once."},"1699":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#dark-mode","content":"Set dark mode once, high up, and the whole subtree flips."},"1700":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#style","content":"Two styles, one design: **Blueprint** (default) is crisp and squared; **Soft** is rounded and plush."},"1701":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#style","content":"You can combine the switches freely — light/dark × Blueprint/Soft is four looks from the same source."},"1702":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#the-token-system","content":"Tokens are the single source of truth for every color, space, radius, and motion value. Components\nnever hardcode these — they read tokens — so overriding a token flows through the whole library."},"1703":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#the-token-system","content":"| Platform                  | Tokens look like               | Where to set them                   |\n| ------------------------- | ------------------------------ | ----------------------------------- |\n| **Web** (React / Angular) | `--vo-*` CSS custom properties | On `:root`, or scoped to any parent |","table":"table-0"},"1704":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#the-token-system","content":"| Platform    | Tokens look like                    | Where to set them   |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------- | ------------------- |\n| **Flutter** | `VoColors` / `VoSpace` / `VoRadius` | In the Visuno theme |","table":"table-0"},"1705":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#override-a-token","content":"Change a token once and it flows to every component under it."},"1706":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#how-it-fits-together","content":"**Tokens** hold the raw values (color, space, radius, motion)."},"1707":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#how-it-fits-together","content":"**The two switches** (`data-theme`, `data-style` on the web; the theme object on Flutter) select\nwhich set of token values is active."},"1708":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#how-it-fits-together","content":"**Components** read tokens only — so flip a switch or override a token, and every component\nupdates in lockstep."},"1709":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#how-it-fits-together","content":"Change a token once and the change is everywhere — that is the whole point of the system."},"1710":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#how-it-fits-together","content":"<Card title=\"Accessibility\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/accessibility\" description=\"Contrast, keyboard, focus, and reduced motion.\" />"},"1711":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/theming-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/theming","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/theming#how-it-fits-together","content":"<Card title=\"Browse components\" href=\"/docs/components/status-pill\" description=\"Each page has a Theming note for that component.\" />"},"1712":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","type":"page","content":"Using with AI","breadcrumbs":["Library","Getting started"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai"},"1713":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-0","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","content":"Point your AI coding assistant at Visuno — llms.txt, per-page Markdown, and prompts that get correct, on-token output."},"1714":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-1","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#machine-readable-docs","content":"Machine-readable docs"},"1715":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-2","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#give-an-assistant-the-context","content":"Give an assistant the context"},"1716":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-3","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#prompting-tips","content":"Prompting tips"},"1717":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-4","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#a-prompt-that-works","content":"A prompt that works"},"1718":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-5","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#building-agents-with-visuno","content":"Building agents with Visuno"},"1719":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-6","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","content":"Visuno is built for agent products, and it works well **with** coding agents too. The docs ship in\nmachine-readable form so an assistant can pull exact component APIs, props, and token rules instead\nof guessing. This page shows what's available and how to use it."},"1720":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-7","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#machine-readable-docs","content":"Every docs page is available as plain text and Markdown, and the whole site is summarised in two\n`llms.txt` files that follow the llms.txt convention."},"1721":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-8","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#machine-readable-docs","content":"| URL         | What it is                                                                            |\n| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/llms.txt` | An index of the docs — every page with its title and link, for an assistant to crawl. |","table":"table-0"},"1722":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-9","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#machine-readable-docs","content":"| URL              | What it is                                                                               |\n| ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/llms-full.txt` | The entire documentation inlined as one text file, ready to paste into a context window. |","table":"table-0"},"1723":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-10","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#machine-readable-docs","content":"| URL                     | What it is                                                                      |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `/llms.mdx/docs/<path>` | Any single page as raw Markdown (e.g. `/llms.mdx/docs/components/status-pill`). |","table":"table-0"},"1724":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-11","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#machine-readable-docs","content":"These are generated from the same source as the site, so they're always in sync with the live docs."},"1725":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-12","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#give-an-assistant-the-context","content":"Pick whichever fits your tool:"},"1726":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-13","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#give-an-assistant-the-context","content":"**Paste a page** — grab one component's Markdown from `/llms.mdx/docs/components/<name>` and paste\nit into the chat before you ask for code. The assistant then has the exact props and examples."},"1727":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-14","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#give-an-assistant-the-context","content":"**Point at the index** — give the assistant `/llms.txt` and let it fetch the pages it needs."},"1728":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-15","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#give-an-assistant-the-context","content":"**Drop in everything** — for a big task, paste `/llms-full.txt` so the whole library is in context."},"1729":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-16","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#prompting-tips","content":"The library has a few hard rules; stating them up front keeps generated code correct and on-brand:"},"1730":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-17","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#prompting-tips","content":"**Reuse, don't reinvent.** Ask the assistant to compose the real components (`StatusPill`, `Button`,\n`Modal`, …) rather than hand-rolling markup. If a component exists, use it."},"1731":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-18","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#prompting-tips","content":"**Tokens only — no literals.** Tell it that all color, spacing, radius, and motion come from the\nshared `--vo-*` tokens, and that hardcoded colors or pixel radii are a bug."},"1732":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-19","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#prompting-tips","content":"**Name the framework.** Say React, Angular, or Flutter explicitly — the props match across all\nthree, but the syntax differs."},"1733":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-20","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#prompting-tips","content":"**Respect the two switches.** Output should work in light and dark (`data-theme`) and in both the\nBlueprint and Soft styles (`data-style`) without changes."},"1734":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-21","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#a-prompt-that-works","content":"> You are building UI with the Visuno component library. Use only Visuno components (fetch their APIs\n> from `/llms.txt`), style everything through the `--vo-*` design tokens — never hardcode colors,\n> spacing, or radii — and make it work in dark mode and the Soft style. Target: **React**. Build a\n> run-status row using `StatusPill`."},"1735":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-22","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#building-agents-with-visuno","content":"Because the components are designed for agent interfaces, they map cleanly onto the states an AI\nproduct moves through — thinking, reading, working, waiting for review, streaming an answer, logging\nactions. Browse the **Agent status** and **Conversation** groups in the sidebar for the building\nblocks, and compose them into your own flows."},"1736":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-23","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#building-agents-with-visuno","content":"<Card title=\"Browse components\" href=\"/docs/components/status-pill\" description=\"APIs and live examples for every component.\" />"},"1737":{"id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai-24","page_id":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/getting-started/using-with-ai#building-agents-with-visuno","content":"<Card title=\"llms.txt\" href=\"/llms.txt\" description=\"The machine-readable docs index.\" />"},"1738":{"id":"/docs/imprint","page_id":"/docs/imprint","type":"page","content":"Imprint","tags":[],"url":"/docs/imprint"},"1739":{"id":"/docs/imprint-0","page_id":"