 — component selectors now use PascalCase that mirrors the React component names (`<vo-status-pill>` → `<StatusPill>`, `<vo-icon>` → `<Icon>`, `<vo-agent-tree>` → `<AgentTree>`, …). The three selectors that shadowed native HTML elements are prefixed to stay unambiguous: `<VoButton>`, `<VoButtonCopy>`, `<VoProgress>`. The `voGridItem` / `vo-field-zone` directives become `gridItem` / `fieldZone`. The shared `--vo-*` design tokens and `vo-*` CSS classes are unchanged. **Breaking:** update Angular templates to the new tag names."],[14,"**Angular** — use the same shared web styles as React for consistent typography, controls, icons, and Soft/Blueprint themes."],[1777,"**Charts and tables** — present data: stat cards and more."],[1792,"**Charts and tables**, **Dates**, and **Forms and inputs** — stat cards, segmented\ncontrol, buttons, badge, progress, and tooltip."],[1708,"**Components** read tokens only — so flip a switch or override a token, and every component\nupdates in lockstep."],[1652,"**Contrast of custom tokens** — if you override `--vo-*` colors (see Theming),\nre-check text and UI contrast against the new values."],[1791,"**Conversation** components — live answer, thread panel, composer, model picker, voice\ncapture and orb, tool call, artifact card, and more."],[1798,"**Copy-paste recipes** — common agent-UI compositions built from several components."],[1772,"**Dark mode** — `data-theme=\"dark\"` on a parent element (web); `Brightness.dark` in the Flutter\ntheme."],[1778,"**Dates** — pick and switch: segmented controls and date tools."],[19,"**Docs preview** — live example stages now always use the docs page's own theme\n(light or dark), never the browser's colour-scheme preference. The per-preview\nLight/Dark toggle has been removed; the component tokens follow the site theme."],[1793,"**Docs site** with live previews, light/dark and Blueprint/Soft toggles, and per-framework\ncode for every component."],[9,"**Docs** — a global site footer now appears on every page (MIT licence, Star on GitHub, a link to the machine-readable **llms.txt**, Imprint, and \"Powered by SDK Industries\"), plus a floating **back-to-top** button that fades in once you scroll."],[13,"**Docs** — new getting-started guides: **Installation** (per-framework setup), **Theming** (the two switches and the `--vo-*` token system, with per-framework code tabs), **Accessibility** (semantics, keyboard, focus, reduced motion), and **Using with AI** (point a coding assistant at the `llms.txt` docs). Grouped under a collapsible **Docs** section in the sidebar, and every nav entry now carries a Visuno icon."],[1728,"**Drop in everything** — for a big task, paste `/llms-full.txt` so the whole library is in context."],[1779,"**Forms and inputs** — the basics: buttons, badges, progress, tooltips."],[24,"**Frameworks slider** — the frameworks strip is now an auto-scrolling black & white\nlogo slider covering React, Angular, Flutter and the React\nmeta-frameworks it works with (Next.js, Remix, Gatsby, Astro)."],[1794,"**Full three-framework parity** — bringing every documented component to React, Angular,\nand Flutter."],[37,"**GitHub Pages** deployment enabled, with the private components repository read through\na GitHub App token in CI."],[1653,"**Heading structure** — keep a sensible heading order on the page around the components."],[20,"**Icon** — new shared component in all four frameworks: one line icon from a shared\nMIT set of ~5,200, or your own SVG. Colour follows `currentColor` so icons theme for\nfree; sizes run `xs`–`xl` on a 24×24 grid. Any name resolves on the web; Angular and\nFlutter draw names outside the compiled core set, and custom glyphs, from a `path`.\nThe whole set now uses canonical, descriptive names (`chevron-right`, `circle-check`,\n`terminal-2`…) across every framework."],[30,"**Imprint page** added with the legal information of SDK Industries, linked from\nthe docs navigation and the homepage footer."],[1797,"**Installation & setup guide** — a first-class getting-started flow per framework."],[1651,"**Labels and text alternatives** — give icon-only buttons an accessible name, and images and charts\na meaningful description for the data they show."],[23,"**Landing page** — the home page now showcases the **whole library** live: every\nshipped component appears as a running preview card, grouped by category, with the\ncomponent count derived from the list. New marketing hero leading with the Visuno\nname, a secondary \"Star on GitHub\" action, and feature pills."],[25,"**Modal** — new shared component in all three frameworks: a centred dialog over a\ndimmed backdrop, closed by the backdrop, a button or Escape, with focus and page\nscroll kept in check. It carries the active style and theme to its portal, so it\nmatches the surrounding components (rounded in Soft, correct light/dark)."],[1800,"**More components** — driven by what agent products actually need; suggestions welcome."],[1732,"**Name the framework.** Say React, Angular, or Flutter explicitly — the props match across all\nthree, but the syntax differs."],[17,"**Number field** — new shared component in all four frameworks: type a number\nor step it with minus and plus, with units, limits, and a note when a value is\nclamped to fit."],[18,"**OTP field** — new shared component in all four frameworks: a one-time code,\none box per digit, that auto-advances, navigates by keyboard and fills from a\npaste."],[21,"**Packages** — the library now publishes as installable packages: `@visuno/react` and\n`@visuno/angular` on npm, and `visuno` on pub.dev for Flutter. Each is released from its\nframework directory in the components repo."],[1726,"**Paste a page** — grab one component's Markdown from `/llms.mdx/docs/components/<name>` and paste\nit into the chat before you ask for code. The assistant then has the exact props and examples."],[1727,"**Point at the index** — give the assistant `/llms.txt` and let it fetch the pages it needs."],[1654,"**Reading order** — place components in the DOM in the order you want them read and tabbed."],[1733,"**Respect the two switches.** Output should work in light and dark (`data-theme`) and in both the\nBlueprint and Soft styles (`data-style`) without changes."],[1730,"**Reuse, don't reinvent.** Ask the assistant to compose the real components (`StatusPill`, `Button`,\n`Modal`, …) rather than hand-rolling markup. If a component exists, use it."],[28,"**Run cost** — the spend bar now glides with the number instead of stalling."],[26,"**Run summary** — the \"Run details\" and \"Open changes\" buttons now work: Run\ndetails opens a Modal with the run's stats, Open changes opens a full diff view."],[16,"**Search input** — new shared component in all four frameworks: a search\nfield with scoped filters, recent queries and an inline agent answer."],[15,"**Slider** — new shared component in all four frameworks: a track with a\nsingle value or a range, optional discrete steps and named stops, and an\nagent-recommended value marked on the track. Keyboard and drag, tokens only."],[31,"**Stat cards** homepage preview reworked into a responsive single-column layout."],[1773,"**Style** — the default **Blueprint** style, or **Soft** via `data-style=\"soft\"` (web). Blueprint\nis crisp and squared; Soft is rounded and plush."],[1707,"**The two switches** (`data-theme`, `data-style` on the web; the theme object on Flutter) select\nwhich set of token values is active."],[1796,"**Theming guide** — a dedicated page on the `--vo-*` token system and how to build a\ncustom theme."],[27,"**Thinking states** — four new indicators: Pulse, Wave, Bounce and Spiral."],[29,"**Toast** — a dismissed toast can be shown again straight after."],[1731,"**Tokens only — no literals.** Tell it that all color, spacing, radius, and motion come from the\nshared `--vo-*` tokens, and that hardcoded colors or pixel radii are a bug."],[1706,"**Tokens** hold the raw values (color, space, radius, motion)."],[22,"**Vanilla JS dropped** — Visuno is now **three frameworks**: React, Angular and Flutter.\nThe Vanilla JS tabs have been removed from every component page, and the docs, FAQ and\nroadmap updated to match. React is now the reference implementation."],[1799,"**Versioned releases** — semver-tagged packages with migration notes in the\nchangelog."],[1765,"**Visuno** is an open-source UI component library for building agent interfaces. Every component\nships natively for **React**, **Angular**, and **Flutter**, built from a single shared set of\ndesign tokens — so a component looks and behaves the same wherever you use it."],[346,"`ChangedFile` / `Hunk` / `DiffLine`"],[720,"`HandoffPerson` is `{ name; initials?; color?; team?; presence?; tone?: ok \\| warn }` — `name` is the\nkey, `tone` puts a green or orange dot before the presence."],[1393,"`Task.status` is one of `running`, `failed`, `queued`, `paused` or `done`. `Task.agent` is\n`{ name, initials, color }`, where `color` is an avatar token like `var(--vo-av-b)`."],[1710,"<Card title=\"Accessibility\" href=\"/docs/getting-started/accessibility\" description=\"Contrast, keyboard, focus, and reduced motion.\" />"],[1736,"<Card title=\"Browse components\" href=\"/docs/components/status-pill\" description=\"APIs and live examples for every component.\" />"],[1711,"<Card title=\"Browse components\" href=\"/docs/components/status-pill\" description=\"Each page has a Theming note for that component.\" />"],[1687,"<Card title=\"Browse components\" href=\"/docs/components/status-pill\" description=\"Live previews and code for every component.\" />"],[1780,"<Card title=\"Browse components\" href=\"/docs/components/status-pill\" description=\"Live previews and code for every component.\" />"],[1781,"<Card title=\"Components on GitHub\" href=\"https://github.com/Visuno/components\" description=\"The source for all three frameworks.\" />"],[1657,"<Card title=\"FAQ\" href=\"/docs/faq\" description=\"More short answers, including access