clamps an out-of-range value and says so — \"Set to 100 (max)\"."],[900,"Type freely, then it settles on blur or Enter; the up and down arrow keys step by `step`, and the\nminus/plus buttons repeat while held."],[1743,"Umsatzsteuer-ID"],[1752,"Umsatzsteuer-Identifikationsnummer gemäß § 27 a Umsatzsteuergesetz:\nDE323262474"],[3,"Unreleased"],[1757,"Unser Angebot enthält Links zu externen Websites Dritter, auf deren Inhalte wir\nkeinen Einfluss haben. Deshalb können wir für diese fremden Inhalte auch keine\nGewähr übernehmen. Für die Inhalte der verlinkten Seiten ist stets der jeweilige\nAnbieter oder Betreiber der Seiten verantwortlich."],[1747,"Urheberrecht"],[41,"Usage"],[60,"Usage"],[73,"Usage"],[92,"Usage"],[114,"Usage"],[139,"Usage"],[154,"Usage"],[171,"Usage"],[194,"Usage"],[218,"Usage"],[246,"Usage"],[264,"Usage"],[276,"Usage"],[293,"Usage"],[311,"Usage"],[328,"Usage"],[344,"Usage"],[368,"Usage"],[388,"Usage"],[409,"Usage"],[431,"Usage"],[449,"Usage"],[468,"Usage"],[488,"Usage"],[506,"Usage"],[527,"Usage"],[542,"Usage"],[563,"Usage"],[584,"Usage"],[604,"Usage"],[625,"Usage"],[648,"Usage"],[668,"Usage"],[681,"Usage"],[701,"Usage"],[724,"Usage"],[738,"Usage"],[757,"Usage"],[774,"Usage"],[790,"Usage"],[811,"Usage"],[829,"Usage"],[850,"Usage"],[866,"Usage"],[887,"Usage"],[904,"Usage"],[918,"Usage"],[944,"Usage"],[968,"Usage"],[985,"Usage"],[1008,"Usage"],[1028,"Usage"],[1052,"Usage"],[1067,"Usage"],[1081,"Usage"],[1100,"Usage"],[1117,"Usage"],[1136,"Usage"],[1154,"Usage"],[1173,"Usage"],[1189,"Usage"],[1208,"Usage"],[1229,"Usage"],[1249,"Usage"],[1267,"Usage"],[1280,"Usage"],[1297,"Usage"],[1320,"Usage"],[1334,"Usage"],[1348,"Usage"],[1367,"Usage"],[1380,"Usage"],[1397,"Usage"],[1417,"Usage"],[1430,"Usage"],[1444,"Usage"],[1464,"Usage"],[1481,"Usage"],[1495,"Usage"],[1515,"Usage"],[1529,"Usage"],[1548,"Usage"],[1564,"Usage"],[1583,"Usage"],[1602,"Usage"],[1619,"Using the components"],[1712,"Using with AI"],[1756,"Verpflichtungen zur Entfernung oder Sperrung der Nutzung von Informationen nach den\nallgemeinen Gesetzen bleiben hiervon unberührt. Eine diesbezügliche Haftung ist\njedoch erst ab dem Zeitpunkt der Kenntnis einer konkreten Rechtsverletzung möglich.\nBei Bekanntwerden von entsprechenden Rechtsverletzungen werden wir diese Inhalte\numgehend entfernen."],[1742,"Vertreten durch"],[1621,"Visuno is an open-source UI component library for building **agent-powered products**.\nEvery component ships natively for **React**, **Angular**, and **Flutter**, built from one\nshared set of design tokens — so a component looks and behaves the same wherever you use it."],[1719,"Visuno is built for agent products, and it works well **with** coding agents too. The docs ship in\nmachine-readable form so an assistant can pull exact component APIs, props, and token rules instead\nof guessing. This page shows what's available and how to use it."],[1672,"Visuno ships the same design across **React**, **Angular**, and **Flutter**. Whatever your stack, the\nshape is the same: **install the package**, **pull the shared core once** (design tokens + a little\nCSS/helpers), then add components one at a time. The React build is the reference; Angular and\nFlutter mirror its props and behaviour."],[1562,"Voice capture"],[1581,"Voice orb"],[1600,"Web search"],[1605,"Web search shows an agent researching out loud. Each query is a row with how many results came\nback and how long it took; a query that finds nothing is asked again in other words. Under each\nquery sit the pages it opened, each marked Read, Skimmed, or Skipped with the reason (paywall,\nblocked, timeout). Once the run is done the trail folds to one line and the answer streams in,\nits bracketed numbers pointing back at the pages that back them up."],[275,"Weekly agent runs, split by outcome, with a range switch."],[1641,"What stays on you"],[1188,"What the agent did, what changed and what needs you."],[1640,"What the components do"],[2,"What's new in Visuno — components, docs, and tooling, newest first."],[72,"When the agent and the team were busy, by day and hour."],[526,"Where the agent's time went, by kind of task."],[1784,"Where Visuno is headed — what's shipped, in progress, and planned."],[1789,"Where Visuno is headed. This is a direction, not a dated commitment — priorities shift\nwith what people need. Have a request? Open an issue on\nGitHub."],[1754,"Wir sind nicht bereit oder verpflichtet, an Streitbeilegungsverfahren vor einer\nVerbraucherschlichtungsstelle teilzunehmen."],[884,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style\n(`data-style=\"soft\"`). The trigger and panel sit on a surface with the card shadow;\neach model's tile takes its own `color` with a letter colour that reads on it, the\npicked row's filled meters take the accent, and a busy row and its notice take the\nwarn tint — all from the theme tokens, so it reads against the dark stage."],[365,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Added and\nremoved lines take the ok and bad tints; a hunk's Keep reads as the accent on a tint of itself, and\nturns to the green done chip once kept — all from the theme tokens. The comment box uses the field\ntokens, becoming a squircle in Blueprint where the browser supports it."],[915,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Boxes use\nthe field tokens, the accent for focus, and the success/danger tokens for `status`; in Blueprint the\nboxes are squared off, in Soft they are rounded. The code is set in the monospace token."],[261,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each file\ntakes its hue from its type — PDF, image, CSV and the rest — drawn from the palette tokens, so the\nbadge, the ring and the row wash stay in step across the themes; in Soft the drop zone and badges are\nrounder. The dashed drop-zone edge, the uploading rings and the reading shimmer all respect\n`prefers-reduced-motion`."],[168,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each kind\nkeeps its colour from the chart palette — purple for the model, teal for tools, orange for apps — and\nthe playhead runs in the accent, turning green at the finish. In Blueprint the bars square off and a\nrunning bar switches from a sweeping sheen to a marching stripe; a failed bar is red and hatched in\nevery theme."],[136,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each lane's\nhue comes from the theme's agent palette tokens (`--vo-pb`, `--vo-pl`, `--vo-pm` …) with a livelier\n\"mark\" variant for its track, line and finished badge, so the lanes stay 3:1 against the surface; in\ndark mode the agent colours are light already and are used as they are. In the Soft style the lanes\nare rounder and the tracks are hatched rather than washed."],[1478,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Each toast\nsits on a surface with the toast shadow and its badge tint comes from the theme tokens, so the deck\nreads against the dark stage; in Soft the cards are rounder. The fan-out and the arrival and dismiss\nmotion are tuned down when the viewer prefers reduced motion."],[273,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the badge is squared off and set in small caps with a hairline in its own color; in Soft\nit is a pill."],[1526,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bar and card are squared off with hairline borders; in Soft they are rounded panels.\nThe tooltip itself and the avatar colours (`--vo-av-*`) come from the theme, so they stay legible on\neither background."],[1170,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bar, the tag and the toggle are squared off; in Soft they are rounded. The fill takes\nthe accent mark while running and the warning mark once paused at the cap, and the status tag tints\nto match its state, all from the tokens."],[1561,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the bars square off and running bars switch from a sweeping sheen to a steady stripe. Each\nkind keeps its colour from the chart palette; a slow bar is amber and hatched in every theme."],[1331,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the cards are squared off with hairline borders; in Soft they are rounded panels with a\nsofter shadow. The sparkline colours fall back to the chart palette (the accent, then violet, green\nand orange) unless a card sets its own `color`."],[1097,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the header, chips and edit blocks are squared off with hairline edges; in Soft they are\nrounded. The timeline rail, the pulse on the current step, and the shimmer on the title all take\ntheir colors from the tokens; added and removed lines use the add and remove colors."],[446,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the pill, the bar and the panel are squared off; in Soft they are rounded. The ring takes\nthe accent mark and the warning mark past the warning share, and the bar segments take the part\npalette (blue, teal, violet, grey) from the tokens unless a part sets its own color."],[982,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the ring, segments and bar are squared off with hairline tracks; in Soft they are rounded\nwith a softer fill. The state colours and the meter's warn and danger bands come from the theme, so\nthey read correctly on either background."],[70,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the rows and the output panes are squared off with hairline edges; in Soft they are\nrounded chips with soft fills. Added and removed lines in a row's output take the add and remove\ncolors from the tokens."],[1186,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In\nBlueprint the running job gets a hairline in the accent and the progress bars fill in steps. A\nfailed job turns red with a hatched fill; the step glyphs are a spinner while running, a tick when\ndone, and a cross on failure."],[341,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). In Soft\nthe card has rounded corners and floats on a soft shadow; in Blueprint it is squared off with a\nhairline instead of the float. An interactive card lifts on hover and keeps a visible focus ring;\nwith reduced motion it still restyles but does not travel."],[965,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). It sits\nflat in a chat thread by default; set `bare={false}` for a card of its own. The step numbers, the\nrunning tint, the amber retry and the green done mark all come from the theme tokens, so each state\nreads at a glance, and in Soft the rows and buttons are rounder."],[465,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). It sits\nflat in the chat thread by default; set `bare` to `false` to give it its own surface card. The active\nstep dot and the picked option's key badge take the accent tint, so the prompt reads against the stage\nin either theme; in Soft the card, options and pills are rounder."],[539,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Segment\ncolours come from the chart palette tokens (`--vo-c1..c6`), the card sits on a surface, and the\nlegend hover tint and the centre text read from the theme tokens. The arcs sweep in and the total\ncounts up on load; with `prefers-reduced-motion` the ring appears already drawn."],[1613,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). Skipped\npages dim and their tag turns amber; a running page shows a spinner. The site initials stack on the\nheader, and hovering a citation lights the page that backs it up along with its site mark."],[622,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nactive bad thumb and the thank-you line take their tints from the `--vo-bad` and `--vo-ok` tokens,\nthe selected chips from the accent, and the box line from the field tokens, so the sheet reads\nagainst the stage; in Soft the chips, box and buttons are rounder."],[826,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nanswer text, the question bubble, the citation chips and the sources list all draw from the theme\ntokens, so an active citation and its source row share the one accent tint; in Soft the chips and\nfollow-up buttons are rounder."],[1133,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ndocument sits on a surface panel; the floating toolbar uses the ink/on-ink tokens so it reads as a\ndark pill over the text, and the picked sentence tints with `--vo-sel`. The struck-through old text\nuses the bad token for its line, and the new words fade and de-blur in as they arrive."],[1427,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nmarks and the typed line use the active theme's accent and text colors; the counter is set in the\nnumeric style. Motion is paused for readers who prefer reduced motion — the line is shown whole\nrather than typed."],[1461,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nopen tab's underline uses the accent mark token and the reply field sits on a surface with an\ninset field line, so it reads against the dark stage; in Soft the field is rounder (squircle)."],[645,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npage is drawn as paper — white ink-on-paper in light mode, a dark document in dark mode — while\nthe rest of the component follows the theme tokens. A highlighted source region tints and rings\nwith the accent, and an unsure one with the warning tint, so each keeps its contrast against the\nink; in Soft the document, panel and buttons are rounder."],[524,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npanel sits on a surface; values hover and flash with the accent tint, dots and avatars take\nthe hue tokens, and the folding sections draw from the shared `fold` and popover tokens, so\neverything reads against either theme. In Soft the panel, menus and chips are rounder."],[754,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npanels sit on a surface with the card shadow; a picture's placeholder gradient and the scan line\nread against either theme. In Blueprint the dots are square cells and the picture shows through\nthem at half strength with a hard scan line in the accent's mark; in Soft the composer, chips and\ntiles are rounder. With reduced motion a picture fades in once it is done rather than resolving\nstep by step."],[503,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\npreview sits on a chip-tinted stage; the slider fill and knob, the accent CTA and the agent's note\nall draw from the theme tokens, and the sample card's own radius, padding, spacing and shadow are\nexactly what the sliders drive. The agent respects `prefers-reduced-motion`, snapping to the tuned\nvalues instead of walking them."],[787,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nprogress segments and glyphs take their colour from the theme tokens — `--vo-ok` for a pass,\n`--vo-bad` for a fail, the accent mark while running — so results read the same on either\nbackground; in Soft the rows and buttons are rounder. The glyph crossfades in as each state lands,\nand the bar transition is skipped under `prefers-reduced-motion`."],[1441,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nrunning step turns in the accent with a soft halo, finished steps and the rail between them turn\ngreen, and a slow step waits in amber. In Blueprint the marks are squared off and the result writes\nin with a plain fade instead of a blur."],[1377,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ntrack and loader take the accent color from the active theme; in Soft the row and track are softer\nand more rounded than in Blueprint."],[1277,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\ntrack and sliding knob take the active theme's surface and accent colors; in Blueprint the control\nis squared off, in Soft it is a pill with a rounder knob."],[325,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The\nvariants read against the theme's accent and surface tokens; in Soft the pills are rounder and\nsofter, and the busy and done faces blur across in either theme."],[290,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The bars\nuse the chart palette (`--vo-c1..c6`: the accent, then violet, orange, green…) unless a series sets\nits own `color`; the readout tooltip sits on the ink tone and the big number and labels read from the\nforeground and muted tokens. In Soft the bars and tooltip are rounder."],[428,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The box\nsits on a surface with a soft shadow and the shared tokens drive its chips, menus and the accent\nSend button, so it reads against the stage; in Soft the box and its pills are rounder."],[1512,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The call\nrows sit on the stage with a chip-tinted icon badge and chip-tinted JSON blocks; keys, strings and\nnumbers take their own palette tokens, and the running spinner and fold motion follow the shared\nease. In Soft the rows and JSON blocks are rounder."],[485,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a `--vo-panel` surface; the header mark, the verdict tags and the checks' ok/bad glyphs all\ntake their colours from the theme tokens (`--vo-ok`, `--vo-warn`, `--vo-bad`, `--vo-pb`), and the\nShip button follows the accent, so the whole review reads against either theme. Once it is live the\nheader mark shifts to the ok tint."],[1394,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface and every colour comes from the theme tokens: the status pills tint from the\naccent (Running), `--vo-ok` (Done) and `--vo-bad` (Failed), with Queued and Paused staying muted;\nthe checkbox fills with the accent and its tick springs in. The table reflows into a stacked layout\ninside a narrow card via a container query, so it reads on a phone as well as full width."],[665,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface and the bars run from the first chart colour (`--vo-c1`, the accent) down to the\nnext (`--vo-c2`), so each stage reads a shade apart; the biggest drop uses the bad tone and the\nagent's note tints with the accent — all from the theme tokens. In the default style the bars carry\na light accent edge on the track; in Soft they are flat fills."],[560,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the card shadow; the warning uses the warn tint, a sent draft the ok tint, and\na scheduled one the blue \"preview\" tint — all from the theme tokens. In Soft the card, chips and pills\nare rounder."],[847,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the panel shadow; the line, the area fill and the marker all take the accent\nmark, the change tag tints green or red from the theme's `ok`/`bad` tokens, and the driver bars take\ntheir own colours (or the accent), so the whole thing reads against the stage in either mode."],[1364,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the panel shadow; the running glyph spins in the accent, a done step turns\nthe tick green, your messages sit in a chip bubble on the right, and the agent's heads-up tints\namber until you answer it. All colours, radii and spacing come from the theme tokens, so in Soft the\ncard, pills and message box are rounder."],[243,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the shared shadow, the icon tile and version marks take the accent, and the\nreader opens over the card's nearest positioned ancestor — the stage here, your chat column in an\napp. In Soft the card and its buttons are rounder; the stack also casts a soft shadow on the desk\nthat fades as the sheets are laid out."],[1545,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the shared shadow; the share bars use the accent mark token, the change chips\nthe `ok` / `bad` tints, and the ranks the mono font — all from the theme tokens, so the list reads\nthe same against either background. In Soft the card and the sort switch are rounder."],[1492,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface with the toast shadow and its tone tints come from the theme tokens, so it reads\nagainst the dark stage; in Soft the card and its buttons are rounder."],[89,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface, and each cell is a mix of the accent into the chip by its value — so the whole\ngrid shifts with the theme's accent and the empty cells read against the surface. In Soft the card\nand cells are a touch rounder."],[1005,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface, the prompt on a chip, and a filled blank takes the accent tint (`--vo-accent-bg`)\nwhile an empty one is outlined and a needed one turns `--vo-bad` — all from the theme tokens, so it\nreads in either mode; in Soft the card, fields and pills are rounder."],[721,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card\nsits on a surface; the countdown bar, the presence dot and the foot row take their colours from the\n`--vo-*` tokens — amber from the warn tokens under five minutes or when the person is out, green from\nthe ok tokens once they have it. The two columns stack when the card is narrow."],[385,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card sits\non a surface with the pop shadow; the citation chips use the hover and accent tokens, the quote's accent\nrule uses `--vo-accent-mark` and its highlight uses the selection tint, so it all reads against the\nstage. In Soft the chips and card are rounder."],[698,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The card,\nrows, bars and gauge track all come from the theme tokens; the gauge fill follows the score (its green\nand red are the component's own `--vo-hs-ok` / `--vo-hs-bad`, the accent in between), and an open or\nhovered row picks up the row tint. In Soft the card and the Fix pill are rounder."],[1025,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The cards\nsit on a chip fill that lifts to a surface with a faint ring when picked; the field is a pill on a\nsurface with the shared shadow, and the Send button uses the accent tokens (a disabled hatch until a\nstarter is picked). All colours, radii and spacing come from the `--vo-*` tokens."],[1049,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The diff\nchip, confidence meter and tags take their colours from the theme tokens — the current value reads as\n`bad` and the options as `ok` by default — and the icon tile uses the accent tint, so the card reads\nagainst the dark stage; in Soft the swatches, tile and pills are rounder."],[1226,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The dots\ntake the chart palette (`--vo-c1`…`--vo-c6`); the gridlines, axes, median lines and the selection box\nare mixed from the line and foreground tokens, and the tooltip sits on the ink token — so the chart\nreads on either theme without any hard-coded colours."],[1150,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The editor\nkeeps one height so it sits still, and its quiet text (word count, placeholder, struck words) comes up\ntoward the foreground in dark mode to stay legible. The suggestion's new words use the accent tint with\na blur-in that is reduced to an instant reveal under `prefers-reduced-motion`. In Soft the toolbar's\nactive format and the suggestion pick up a hairline of the accent mark."],[901,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The field,\nits hairline and the steppers all draw from the shared `--vo-*` tokens; the number is set in the\ntabular-numerals face so digits don't jitter as they change."],[1294,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The fill\nand thumbs take the accent, the rail and ticks the field/line tokens, and the recommended mark the\naccent's ring colour — all from `--vo-*`, so it recolours with the theme automatically."],[808,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The first\nline and its fill use the accent; the rest take the chart palette (`--vo-c2`, `--vo-c3`, …). The grid\nlines, the pointer rule and the dark tooltip pill all come from the theme tokens, so the chart reads\non either background. In Flutter the lines are drawn with a `CustomPainter` and the draw-in and\ncount-up run on an `AnimationController`."],[1246,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The gauge\nsegments and the row swatches use the chart palette (`--vo-c1`…`--vo-c6`); the band chip, the Weakest\nflag and the proposal card tint from the theme tokens (`--vo-ok`, `--vo-warn`, `--vo-surface`,\n`--vo-line`), so the breakdown reads on either background. In Soft the rows and buttons are rounder."],[151,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The glyph\nand the current segment take the phase's colour — the accent while it works, amber while it waits,\nred on an error and green when done. In Blueprint the segments are squared off and the shimmer rests\non a solid colour."],[1205,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The glyph,\nthe `+`/`−` diffs and the \"Needs you\" dot all take their colour from the theme tokens (`--vo-ok`,\n`--vo-add`, `--vo-del`, `--vo-warn-mark`), so the summary reads the same against any surface; in Soft\nthe card and its pills are rounder."],[1599,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The orb's\ncolours flow from the tokens: the accent is yours, `--vo-pl` (violet) is the agent, and the two are\nmixed in oklch so the step between them stays bright. The glass sphere is drawn on a canvas with\nWebGL where it can, falling back to layered gradients otherwise; with reduced motion it holds a\nsingle still frame and only redraws when the speaker changes."],[1414,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The output\nis 12px monospace on a 1.8 line height, the state tag and left rail take the accent while the run is\nlive and turn green or red once it is over, and a block cursor blinks after the newest line — all drawn\nfrom the theme tokens. In the Blueprint style the rail thins and the cursor marches; Soft rounds the\ncorners and the scrollbar."],[308,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The page\nis drawn small, with real words where they matter and grey lines for the rest; a price the agent has\ntaken is marked in the accent fill. While you have control the frame turns the accent colour. In\nBlueprint the frame and chips are squared off."],[111,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface with the card shadow; a failed run tints with the bad tokens, the running clock and\nthe Approve pill use the accent, and the avatar marks take the shared `--vo-av-*` colours with their\nown ink. In Soft the panel and its rows are rounder."],[601,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface with the card shadow; pass and fail take the `--vo-ok` and `--vo-bad` tokens for\ntheir glyphs and bar segments, and a failed case tints with `--vo-bad-bg`, so it all reads against\nthe stage. In Soft the panel, pills and segmented control are rounder."],[406,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface; the changed-line wash comes from the `ok` token, the open line and its note from\nthe selection tint, and the syntax colours from the shared highlight tokens, so the code reads the\nsame against either theme."],[1580,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nsits on a surface; the recording dot uses the `--vo-bad` tone and pulses, unsure words are tinted\nwith `--vo-hl` (and `--vo-hl-ok` once fixed), and the wave is drawn from the `--vo-fg2`, `--vo-faint`\nand `--vo-muted` tokens, so it reads in either theme. In Soft the panel and its buttons are rounder."],[863,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The panel\nuses the active theme's raised surface, text and shadow tokens; the backdrop dims with the ink token.\nMotion is paused for readers who prefer reduced motion — the dialog simply appears instead of rising in."],[1317,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The pill\nand rows ride the shared `--vo-*` tokens; the filter chips are white with a dimmed edge that steps up\non the picked one, and the relevance bars fill with `--vo-accent-mark`. In Soft the chips and rows are\nrounder. The entrance stagger and the one-time auto-open are skipped under reduced motion."],[1345,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) and in the Soft style (`data-style=\"soft\"`). The pill\nsits on a surface with the shared shadow, so it picks up the theme's surface and token colours; in\nSoft it is rounder, and in dark it reads against the dark stage."],[57,"Works in light and dark (`data-theme=\"dark\"`) an